COLLDATA("sh13068","en",[[1,"I asked my Lord, mighty and majestic, for three qualities, and He granted me two and withheld one. I asked Him not to set an enemy upon my ummah from other than themselves, and He granted me that. I asked Him not to destroy my ummah by drought, and He granted me that. And I asked Him not to make them into factions, but He refused me."],[2,"The Prophet ﷺ said to a man: \"You and your property belong to your father.\""],[3,"The Prophet ﷺ taught a man to say when he went to bed: \"O Allah, I have turned my face to You, and I have entrusted my back to You, and I have consigned my affair to You, and I have surrendered myself to You; out of fear of You and desire for You. There is no refuge and no escape from You except to You. I believe in Your Book which You revealed, and Your Prophet whom You sent. If he dies that night, he will be forgiven.\""],[4,"Iyad b. Himar al-Mujashi'i al-Nahshali ؓ gave a horse as a gift to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before he became Muslim, and he said: \"I dislike the gift of the polytheists.\""],[5,"My ummah is a community shown mercy. Allah placed its punishment in its own hands. So when the Day of Resurrection comes, to every Muslim man will be given a man from the people of other religions, and he will be his ransom from the Fire."],[6,"Amputation is for a quarter dinar or more."],[7,"A time will come upon people when whoever does not have yellow and white [gold and silver] will not enjoy life."],[8,"Remain upright, though you will not be able to do so completely. Know that the best of your deeds is prayer, and no one maintains wudu except a believer."],[9,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed wudu, then he turned over a jubba that was on him and wiped his face with it."],[10,"The noblest part of faith is that people feel safe from you. The noblest part of Islam is that people are safe from your tongue and hand. The noblest migration is that you abandon sins. The noblest jihad is that you are killed and your horse is hamstrung."],[11,"I was riding behind Ibn Umar when he passed by a shepherd playing a reed pipe. He struck the face of the camel and turned it away from the road. He put his fingers in his ears and said: \"Do you hear it? Do you hear it?\" until the sound stopped. I said: \"I do not hear it.\" Then he returned it to the road. He said: \"This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do.\""],[12,"The night prayer is two by two. If you fear the approach of dawn, then pray one rak'ah as witr."],[13,"Indeed every religion has a character, and the character of Islam is modesty."],[14,"I entered upon Tamim al-Dari while he was governor of Jerusalem, and he was cleaning barley for his horse. I said to him, 'O governor, was there no one to suffice you from this?' He said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever cleans barley for his horse in the path of Allah, then stands with it until he hangs it upon it, Allah records for him for every grain a good deed.'"],[15,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed the effeminate men and said: 'Do not admit them into your houses.'"],[16,"A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'I have given birth to a boy and named him Muhammad and gave him the kunya Abu al-Qasim. It was mentioned to me that you dislike that.' He ﷺ said: 'What is it that made my name lawful and my kunya forbidden? And what is it that made my kunya forbidden and my name lawful?'"],[17,"Dawud ﷺ would not eat except from the work of his own hands."],[18,"When the Day of Resurrection comes, Allah will call a servant from His servants and make him stand before Him, and will ask him about his status just as He asks him about his wealth."],[19,"Jibril said to me: Give glad tidings to Khadijah of a house in Paradise made of hollow pearls, with no noise in it and no fatigue."],[20,"The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother."],[21,"When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the prescribed one."],[22,"Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim."],[23,"War is deception."],[24,"When one of you stands in prayer, he should not close his eyes."],[25,"Preemption applies in every co-owned share, whether in a house or a walled garden; it is not lawful for him to sell it until he notifies his partner, who may then take it or leave it."],[26,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ said: I have never regretted anything as much as I regret not asking the Messenger of God ﷺ about the wind. Abu Hurayrah said: I asked him about it: O Messenger of God, what is the wind? He said: It is from the breath of God; He sends it with mercy and He sends it with punishment."],[27,"I was sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ when a man came who had performed ablution but had missed a spot on his foot that the water did not reach. The Prophet ﷺ said: Go and complete your ablution. So he did."],[28,"He forbade muhaqalah, muzabanah, and mulamasah, and he forbade shighar."],[29,"The cry of a newborn when it is born is a prod from Satan."],[30,"Jafar b. Abi Talib returned to the Messenger of God ﷺ from the land of Abyssinia, and the Messenger of God ﷺ kissed him between his eyes and said: I do not know whether I am happier at Jafar's return or at the conquest of Khaybar."],[31,"Whoever eats seven ajwah dates from the dates of al-Aliyah in the morning, no poison or magic will harm him until evening."],[32,"The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear; leave what makes you doubtful for what does not make you doubtful."],[33,"The heads of the Khawarij were brought and set up on the steps of the mosque of Damascus. People began to look at them, and I went out to look at them. Abu Umamah came on a donkey wearing a sunbulani shirt, looked at them, and said: What has Satan done to this community? He said it three times. These are the worst slain under the sky; the best slain under the sky are those whom they killed. These are the dogs of Hell—he said it three times—then he wept and left. Abu Ghalib said: I followed him and said: I heard you say something; did you say it? He said: Glory be to God! I would be bold indeed. Rather I heard it from the Messenger of God ﷺ many times. I said to him: I saw you weep. He said: Out of mercy for them; they were once among the people of Islam. Then he said to me: Do you not recite? I said: Yes. He said: Recite from Al Imran, so I recited. He said: Do you not hear the word of God, Mighty and Majestic: \"As for those in whose hearts is deviation, they follow what is ambiguous of it.\" There was deviation in the hearts of these, and they were led astray. Recite at the beginning of the hundredth verse, so I recited until I reached: \"On the day when faces turn white and faces turn black. As for those whose faces turn black: Did you disbelieve after your belief?\" I said: O Abu Umamah, are they these? He said: Yes, they are these."],[34,"Give the hired worker his wages before his sweat dries."],[35,"Whoever visits a sick person and says: I ask God the Almighty, Lord of the Mighty Throne, to heal you, seven times—that person will be healed, unless his appointed time has come."],[36,"When he bowed, if a vessel of water were placed on his back, it would remain still because of his evenness."],[37,"Whoever eats of these green vegetables: garlic, onions, leeks, and radishes, let him not approach our mosque, for the angels are harmed by what harms the children of Adam."],[38,"Whoever gives a man security for his blood and then kills him, I am innocent of the killer, even if the killed one is a disbeliever."],[39,"That the Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah on the day of the conquest, and upon his head was a black turban."],[40,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted the sale of 'araya by estimating their fruit by measure."],[41,"A man from the people of al-'Awali would invite the Prophet ﷺ at midnight to a meal of barley bread, and he would accept his invitation."],[42,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade garments dyed with safflower, al-qassi, gold rings, and garments hemmed with silk brocade. He said: And I know that I am to you among the sincere advisers."],[43,"I said: O Jibril, does your Lord, mighty is His remembrance and exalted is His majesty, pray? He said: Yes. I said: What is His prayer? He said: 'Glorious, Holy, My mercy has preceded My wrath, My mercy has preceded My wrath.'"],[44,"When the prayer is called, do not stand until you see me."],[45,"How can I be at ease when the holder of the horn has put the horn to his mouth and inclined his forehead, waiting for when he will be commanded? They said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you command us? He said: 'Say: Sufficient for us is Allah, and He is the best disposer of affairs.'"],[46,"Whoever commits a sin in this world and is punished for it, Allah, mighty is His remembrance, is more just than to repeat his punishment upon His servant in the Hereafter. And whoever commits a sin in this world and Allah conceals it for him and pardons him, Allah, mighty and majestic is He, is more generous than to return to something He has already pardoned and concealed."],[47,"Prayer at night and during the day is two units at a time, two units at a time."],[48,"When one of you puts on sandals, let him begin with the right, and when he removes them, let him begin with the left."],[49,"I used to scrape the semen from the garment of the Messenger of God ﷺ and he would pray in it."],[50,"No prize is permitted except in a hoof, or a foot, or a blade."],[51,"I have prepared for My righteous servants what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and has not occurred to the heart of a human."],[52,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, by God, indeed you are dearer to me than my own self, and you are dearer to me than my family and my wealth, and dearer to me than my child, and I am in the house and I remember you, and I cannot bear it until I come to you and look at you. And when I remember my death and your death, I know that when you enter Paradise, you will be raised with the prophets, and when I enter Paradise, I fear that I will not see you. The Prophet ﷺ did not answer him anything until Gabriel ﷺ came down with this verse: 'Whoever obeys God and the Messenger, they will be with those whom God has blessed among the prophets, the truthful, the martyrs, and the righteous,' the verse."],[53,"Your remaining time compared to the nations before you is only like what is between the afternoon prayer and the setting of the sun."],[54,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say about one who passes in front of a praying person: If he refuses, then push him back; if he refuses, then fight him, for he is only a devil."],[55,"O Banu Abd Manaf, O Banu Abd al-Muttalib, if you are given authority over this matter, do not prevent anyone who circumambulates this House from praying at any hour he wishes, whether night or day."],[56,"My community will remain upon the natural disposition as long as they do not delay the sunset prayer until the stars appear densely."],[57,"The Messenger of God ﷺ employed the people of Khaybar for half of what came out of it of crops or dates, and he used to give his wives each year one hundred wasq: eighty wasq of dates and twenty wasq of barley."],[58,"The briber and the bribed are in the Fire."],[59,"A person is with the one he loves."],[60,"Take the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal there is blessing."],[61,"Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim."],[62,"Ten from Quraysh are in Paradise: Abū Bakr is in Paradise, ʿUmar is in Paradise, ʿUthmān is in Paradise, ʿAlī is in Paradise, Ṭalḥa is in Paradise, al-Zubayr is in Paradise, Saʿd is in Paradise, Saʿīd b. Zayd is in Paradise, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf is in Paradise, and Abū ʿUbayda b. al-Jarrāḥ is in Paradise — ؓ ."],[63,"The Prophet ﷺ took hold of part of my body and said: O ʿAbd Allāh, be in this world as if you were a stranger or a wayfarer, and count yourself among the people of the graves."],[64,"Every act of kindness is charity."],[65,"O Allah, bless my community in its early morning on Thursday."],[66,"Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise."],[67,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[68,"Whoever conceals the fault of a believer, Allah will conceal him from the Fire."],[69,"War is deception."],[70,"When a daughter is born to a man, Allah — Mighty and Majestic — sends angels who say: Peace be upon you, O people of the house. They surround her with their wings and wipe their hands over her head, and they say: A weak one has come forth from a weak one; the one responsible for her will be aided until the Day of Resurrection."],[71,"My anger is intense against one who wrongs someone who finds no helper other than Me."],[72,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about found property, and he said: Found property is not lawful. Whoever finds something must announce it. If its owner comes, let him return it to him. If he does not come, let him give it in charity. Then if he comes, let him give him the choice between the reward and what belongs to him."],[73,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to travel from Makkah to Madinah fearing none but God, praying two rakʿahs, two rakʿahs."],[74,"When we returned from Tabūk, a man asked the Messenger of God ﷺ: “When is the Hour?” He said: “One hundred years will not come upon the people while on the face of the earth there remains a soul breathed into today.”"],[75,"God — Mighty and Majestic — says every day to Paradise: “Be fragrant for your inhabitants,” and it increases in fragrance. That is the coolness that people find at dawn, from that."],[76,"I asked Anas b. Mālik ؓ: “How do I perform ablution?” He said: “You ask me how to perform ablution, but you do not ask me how I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ perform ablution. I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ perform ablution three times, three times, and he said: ‘Thus has my Lord — Mighty and Majestic — commanded me.’”"],[77,"When God spoke to Mūsā, he could see the crawling of ants on the rock in the dark night from a distance of ten parasangs."],[78,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a neighborhood of Banū al-Najjār, and there were young girls beating the duff and saying: “We are singing girls of Banū al-Najjār; how excellent is Muḥammad as a neighbor!” The Prophet ﷺ said: “God knows that my heart loves you.”"],[79,"When the Prophet ﷺ said: “God hears the one who praises Him,” none of us would bend his back until the Prophet ﷺ prostrated, then we would prostrate with him."],[80,"Remorse is repentance."],[81,"That the Prophet ﷺ sent him and Aws b. al-Ḥadathān during the days of Tashrīq, and he called out: “No one enters Paradise except a believing soul, and the days of Minā are days of eating and drinking.”"],[82,"The people of Paradise are one hundred and twenty rows; my community among them are eighty rows."],[83,"That the Prophet ﷺ recited: “And take from the standing place of Ibrāhīm a place of prayer.”"],[84,"It is near that whoever lives among you will see ʿĪsā b. Maryam as a just and fair leader. He will abolish the jizyah, break the cross, and kill the pig, and war will lay down its burdens."],[85,"May Allah curse the Jews; fats were forbidden to them, so they sold them and consumed their price."],[86,"The support of my community is through its worst members."],[87,"I was holding the hand of al-A'mash, and he said: I recited the Quran to Yahya b. Waththab thirty times, each time I recited: 'And shun the filth' [al-Muddaththir 74:5], and likewise Yahya recited it to 'Alqama, and 'Alqama to 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud, and Ibn Mas'ud to the Prophet ﷺ."],[88,"Gabriel ﷺ taught me to recite in one mode, and I kept requesting more, and he kept increasing me until it reached seven modes."],[89,"Shall I not tell you about the people of Paradise? The people of Paradise are every gentle, soft-hearted, easygoing, and approachable person."],[90,"You claim that I am the last of you to die, but indeed I will be the first of you to die, and you will follow me in groups, striking one another's necks."],[91,"I was commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and forbidden to gather up hair or clothing."],[92,"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has not created any disease without creating a cure for it, except for old age, and that is death."],[93,"Any man to whom his cousin comes and asks him from his surplus wealth, and he withholds it from him, Allah will withhold His bounty from him on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever withholds surplus water in order to withhold surplus pasture, Allah will withhold His bounty from him on the Day of Resurrection."],[94,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Fatima: Our Prophet is the best of the prophets, and he is your father. Our martyr is the best of the martyrs, and he is your father's uncle, Hamza. Among us is one who has two wings with which he flies in Paradise wherever he wishes, and he is your father's cousin, Ja'far. Among us are the two grandsons of this community: al-Hasan and al-Husayn, and they are your two sons. And among us is the Mahdi."],[95,"When one of you doubts and does not know how many units he has prayed, let him strive to ascertain the correct number until he is certain, then let him complete based on what he believes, then let him prostrate twice for forgetfulness."],[96,"The best of my community is the generation in which I was sent, then those who follow them, then those who follow them."],[97,"Regarding His—Mighty and Majestic—saying: 'But if remission is made to someone from his brother, then let there be pursuing with fairness and payment to him with kindness,' he said: The Children of Israel, when someone among them was killed intentionally, nothing was lawful for them except retribution; but the blood money was made lawful for you. So this one was commanded to pursue with fairness, and this one was commanded to pay with kindness. That is a lightening from your Lord."],[98,"We were with Utbah, four women—there was not a woman among us but that she strove with perfume, so that she might be more fragrant than her companion. Utbah did not touch perfume, except that he would touch an oil with which he wiped his beard, and he was more fragrant than us. When he went out among the people, they would say: 'We have never smelled a scent more pleasant than the scent of Utbah.' One day I said to him: 'We strive with perfume, yet you are more fragrant than us—so from what is that?' He said: 'The shara took hold of me during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, so I came to him and complained of that to him. He commanded me to strip, so I stripped, sat before him, and cast my garment over my private parts. Then he blew into his hand over my back and belly, and this fragrance has clung to me since that day.'"],[99,"The Prophet ﷺ married Maymunah while he was in ihram."],[100,"God does not accept a prayer without purification, nor a charity from the spoils of war."],[101,"Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."],[102,"A sin that is not forgiven, a sin that is not left, and a sin that is forgiven. As for the sin that is not forgiven, it is associating partners with God. As for the sin that is not left, it is the wrongdoing of people against one another. As for the sin that is forgiven, it is a servant's sin between himself and God Most High."],[103,"From the people of this qiblah, those who will enter the Fire are so many that none can count them except God, because they disobeyed God, were audacious in disobeying Him, and opposed obeying Him. Then I will be permitted to intercede, and I will praise Him—glorified be His remembrance—prostrating, just as I praise Him standing... and he mentioned the hadith. I say: And its completion is: '...Then it will be said to me: \"Raise your head, ask and you will be given, intercede and you will be granted intercession.\"'"],[104,"When the star rises, affliction is lifted from every land."],[105,"Gabriel ﷺ said to him: 'Recite the Quran in seven dialects.'"],[106,"When God—glorified be His remembrance—wills to create a soul, and the man has intercourse with the woman, his fluid flies into every vein and nerve of hers. Then on the seventh day, God brings before him every vein between him and Adam. Then he recited: 'In whatever form He willed, He assembled you.'"],[107,"In the time of the Prophet ﷺ, a sinking of the earth was mentioned toward the east. Some of the people said: 'O Messenger of God, will an earth in which there are Muslims be swallowed up?' He said: 'Yes, when most of its inhabitants are wicked.'"],[108,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me not to bring a woman to her husband if she has not received any of her dower."],[109,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ sneezed, he covered his face."],[110,"If one of you touches his private part directly with his hand, with no barrier between them, then wudu' becomes obligatory for him."],[111,"Any man who marries a woman for a small or large dower while not intending to give her her due, he deceives her. If he dies without giving her her due, he will meet God on the Day of Resurrection as an adulterer. And any man who takes a loan not intending to repay its owner, deceiving him until he takes his wealth, and then dies without repaying his debt, he will meet God as a thief."],[112,"The most I fear for my community is seeking rain by the stars, injustice of the ruler, and denial of divine decree."],[113,"Three types will be given their reward twice: a man of the People of the Book who believed in his prophet, then lived until the Prophet ﷺ and believed in him; a man who had a slave woman, freed her, and then married her; and a slave who fears God and obeys his masters."],[114,"Do not lift the staff from your family, and make them fear God, the Mighty and Majestic."],[115,"When the Prophet ﷺ sent out a military expedition, he would say: 'In the name of God, by God, and in the path of God, and upon the religion of the Messenger of God. Do not steal from the spoils, do not act treacherously, do not mutilate, and do not kill children.'"],[116,"There is no prayer after the morning prayer until the sun rises, nor after the afternoon prayer until the sun sets."],[117,"The Prophet ﷺ recited with them in the Maghrib prayer: 'Those who disbelieved and hindered from the path of God.'"],[118,"Shall I inform you of the men among you who will be in Paradise? They said: 'Yes, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'The prophet is in Paradise, the truthful one is in Paradise, the martyr is in Paradise, the newborn is in Paradise, and a man who visits his brother in a quarter of the city, visiting him only for the sake of God, the Mighty and Majestic, is in Paradise.' Then he said: 'Shall I inform you of the women among you who will be in Paradise?' They said: 'Yes, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'Every fertile and loving woman who, when she is angry or wronged or her husband is angry, says: \"Here is my hand in your hand; I will not sleep until you are pleased.\"'"],[119,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Hassan b. Thabit: 'Satirize the polytheists, and Gabriel is with you.'"],[120,"A bedouin came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of God, will our clothes in Paradise be woven by our own hands?' The people laughed. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Why are you laughing? At an ignorant man asking a learned one? No, O bedouin, but they will split open from the fruits of Paradise.'"],[121,"You burn, you burn; and when you pray Fajr, it washes them away. Then you burn, you burn; and when you pray Zuhr, it washes them away. Then you burn, you burn; and when you pray Asr, it washes them away. Then you burn, you burn; and when you pray Maghrib, it washes them away. Then you burn, you burn; and when you pray Isha, it washes them away. Then you sleep, and nothing is recorded against you until you wake."],[122,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Umm Atiyya, a female circumciser in Madinah: When you circumcise, reduce but do not remove completely; for that is more radiant for the face and more pleasing for the husband."],[123,"I said: O Messenger of God, a man who is the protector of his people and defends his companions — will his share be like the share of others? He said: May your mother lose you, O son of Umm Sa'd! Are you not provided for and given victory except through your weak ones?"],[124,"Whoever God takes away his sight and he is patient and seeks reward, it is incumbent and binding upon God that his two eyes will not see the Fire."],[125,"There is no envy except in two cases: a man to whom God, Mighty and Majestic, has given the Quran and he stands with it by night and day, following what is in it, so a man says: If only God gave me the like of what He gave so-and-so, I would stand with it as so-and-so stands. And a man to whom God has given wealth and he spends and gives charity, so a man says: something like that."],[126,"Three traits — whoever has them is free from miserliness: one who pays the zakat of his wealth with a pleased soul, honors the guest, and gives in times of calamity."],[127,"Whoever performs ablution should snuff water into the nose and expel it, and whoever uses stones to clean himself should do so an odd number of times."],[128,"The passing away of my community will be through stabbing and the plague. We said: We know stabbing, but what is the plague? He said: The piercing of your enemies among the jinn, and in each there is martyrdom."],[129,"The Prophet ﷺ stopped at Marr al-Zahran, and a leg of a gazelle was gifted to him. He returned it to the messenger and said: Convey peace to him and tell him: Were it not that we are in a state of ihram, we would not have returned it to you."],[130,"O assembly of merchants, you attend your sales with oaths and vain talk, so mix them with a little charity."],[131,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while two disputants were arguing before him. He said to me: Judge between them. I said: May my father and mother be your ransom, you are more entitled to that. He said: Judge between them. I said: On what basis? He said: Strive; if you are correct, you get ten good deeds, and if you are not correct, you get one good deed."],[132,"Indeed, God supports this religion with people who have no share of good."],[133,"My father Safwan migrated to the Prophet ﷺ and pledged allegiance to him upon Islam. The Prophet ﷺ extended his hand and wiped over it. Safwan said, 'I love you, O Messenger of God.' The Prophet ﷺ said to him, 'A person is with the one he loves.'"],[134,"He used to say the talbiyah: 'Here I am, O God, here I am. Here I am, You have no partner, here I am. Indeed, all praise and favor are Yours, and the dominion. You have no partner.'"],[135,"'What do you call those who enter among you from the people of the villages who have no kinship with you?' I said, 'We call them the boors or the riffraff.' Aisha ؓ said, 'We used to call them the emigrants in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ.'"],[136,"Establish the prayer, give the zakat, perform the Hajj, perform the Umrah, and remain upright, and uprightness will be maintained for you."],[137,"Do not seek breast-feeding from a weak-minded woman."],[138,"I never saw the private parts of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[139,"Whoever visits a sick person plunges into mercy, and when he sits, he immerses himself in it."],[140,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the lizard. He said, 'A nation that was transformed, and God knows best.'"],[141,"Let me not find any of you placing one leg over the other and then singing, while abandoning the recitation of the Quran."],[142,"Wealth does not decrease from charity, and no man forgives an injustice except that God increases him in honor thereby. So forgive, and God will honor you. And no man opens for himself a door of begging except that God opens for him a door of poverty."],[143,"Every intoxicant is wine, and every wine is forbidden."],[144,"'Have you considered that if Juhaynah, Muzaynah, Aslam, and Ghifar are better in the sight of God than Asad, Ghatafan, and Banu Amir b. Sa'sa'ah, have they failed and lost?' They said, 'Yes. Indeed, Juhaynah, Muzaynah, Aslam, and Ghifar are better than Asad, Ghatafan, and Banu Amir b. Sa'sa'ah.'"],[145,"What an excellent condiment vinegar is."],[146,"He saw a man praying the two rak'ahs of the forenoon (al-ghadāh) when the mu'adhdhin began to pronounce the iqāmah, so the Prophet ﷺ nudged his shoulder and said, \"Should this not have been before this?\""],[147,"Indeed God wrote a book, and it is with Him upon the Throne. And He sent down from that book two verses with which He sealed Surah al-Baqarah. Indeed, Satan does not enter a house in which they are recited for three nights."],[148,"He used to forbid eating leeks and onions when entering the mosque."],[149,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"May a man pray in a single garment?\" He said, \"Does every one of you find two garments?\""],[150,"I entered upon Abu Musa al-Ash'ari while he was eating chicken meat. He said, \"Come and eat.\" I said, \"I have sworn not to eat chicken meat.\" Abu Musa said, \"Eat, for I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ eating it. And I will inform you about your oath: I and some companions of mine came to the Messenger of God ﷺ asking him for mounts. He swore that he would not provide us mounts, and he had no mounts to give. By God, we had not left before some she-camels with white-tipped humps were brought to him, and he ordered mounts for us. When we left, we remembered the oath of the Messenger of God ﷺ, so we returned to him. He said, 'What brought you back?' We said, 'We remembered your oath, O Messenger of God, and feared that you had forgotten it.' He ﷺ said, 'By God, I did not forget it, but whoever swears an oath and then sees something else better than it, let him do that which is better and expiate for his oath.'\""],[151,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked while he was at the middle jamrah, \"Which deeds are best?\" He said, \"A word of truth before a tyrannical ruler.\""],[152,"Ali b. Abi Talib sent me and said, \"Do you know on what mission I am sending you? I am sending you on the mission on which the Messenger of God ﷺ sent me: Do not leave any image but that you efface it, and no raised grave but that you level it.\""],[153,"\"I traveled with the Messenger of God ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar, and I did not see them exceed two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs.\""],[154,"A person is with those whom he loves."],[155,"The prayer of the awwabin is when the young camels feel the heat of the sun (i.e., mid-morning)."],[156,"I am Ahmad, Muhammad, al-Hashir, al-Muqaffi, and al-Khatam."],[157,"We have seen ourselves recently, when we performed Hajj, we would say: 'Labbayka ta'zīman ilayka 'udhran, hādhī Zubaydun qad atatka qasran, yaqta'na khabtan wa jibālan wa'rā, qad ja'alū al-andād khilwan sufrā.' And we have seen ourselves stopping in the interior of Muhassir, fearing that the jinn might snatch us away. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Withdraw from the interior of 'Urana, for they are your brothers when they submit.' And he taught us the talbiya: 'Labbayka Allāhumma labbayk, labbayka lā sharīka laka labbayk, inna al-hamda wa al-ni'mata laka wa al-mulk, lā sharīka lak.'"],[158,"Al-Zubayr encountered a thief and interceded for him. It was said to him: 'Wait until we bring him to the ruler.' He said: 'When he reaches the ruler, then may God curse the intercessor and the one for whom intercession is made, as the Messenger of God ﷺ said.'"],[159,"The congregational prayer exceeds the prayer of a man alone by twenty-five."],[160,"Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will be bridled on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire."],[161,"Fast when you see it, and break your fast when you see it; and if it is obscured to you, then complete the number as thirty."],[162,"There is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness, and no prayer for one who has no purification, and no religion for one who has no prayer. The position of prayer in religion is like the position of the head in the body."],[163,"No one has been given anything after certainty like well-being, and we ask God for well-being in this world and the Hereafter. Indeed, truthfulness and righteousness are in Paradise. Indeed, lying and wickedness are in the Fire."],[164,"Three are among the character traits of faith: one who, when he becomes angry, his anger does not lead him into falsehood; one who, when he is pleased, his pleasure does not remove him from truth; and one who, when he has power, does not reach for what is not his."],[165,"Whoever recites 'Qul huwa Allāhu aḥad' (Say: He is God, the One), it is as if he has recited a third of the Qur'an; and whoever recites 'Qul yā ayyuhā al-kāfirūn' (Say: O disbelievers), it is as if he has recited a quarter of the Qur'an."],[166,"Whoever recites 'Qul huwa Allāhu aḥad' twelve times after the dawn prayer, it is as if he has recited the Qur'an four times, and he will be the most virtuous of the people of the earth that day if he is God-fearing."],[167,"I indeed know a stone that used to greet me before I was sent."],[168,"A group of people from this nation will certainly spend the night on food, drink, and amusement, and wake up having been transformed into apes and pigs."],[169,"Whoever peers into the house of a people without their permission, it is lawful for them to gouge out his eye."],[170,"None of you should say: 'O Allah, forgive me if You will.' Rather, let him be firm in asking, for none can compel Him."],[171,"I saw ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ facing the Black Stone, kissing it, then saying: 'By Allah, I know that you are a stone that can neither harm nor benefit. Had I not seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissing you, I would not have kissed you.'"],[172,"He used to touch her face while he was fasting."],[173,"Do not turn around during your prayer, for there is no prayer for one who turns around."],[174,"Regarding His saying: 'The day when some of the signs of your Lord come,' he said: 'The rising of the sun from its west.'"],[175,"I witnessed ʿAlī ؓ on the pulpit adjuring the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Whoever heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the day of Ghadīr Khumm what he said, let him testify.' Twelve men among them stood up—Abū Hurayrah, Abū Saʿīd, and Anas b. Mālik—and testified that they heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever [O Allah, whoever] I am his mawlā, ʿAlī is his mawlā. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him.'"],[176,"Whoever says, 'I am a scholar,' is ignorant. Whoever says, 'I am ignorant,' is ignorant. Whoever says, 'I am in Paradise,' is in the Fire. Whoever says, 'I am in the Fire,' is in the Fire."],[177,"I came to Umm Salamah to offer condolences for al-Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī. She said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me and sat on a bed of ours. Fāṭimah— ؓ and have mercy on her—came to him with something and placed it down. He said: 'Call for me Ḥasan, Ḥusayn, and your cousin.' When they gathered with him, he said: 'These are my family and my household. So remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly.'"],[178,"Gold for gold, silver for silver, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, dates for dates, raisins for raisins, like for like, hand to hand. Whoever adds or asks for addition has committed ribā."],[179,"The believer is frail and patching; blessed is the one who perishes upon his patching."],[180,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding His saying—Mighty and Majestic—: 'The Hajj is in well-known months,' he said: 'Shawwāl, Dhū al-Qaʿdah, and Dhū al-Ḥijjah.'"],[181,"The Messenger of God ﷺ put me in charge of the captives of Qurayzah. I would look at the private part of a boy; if I saw that it had grown hair, I struck his neck, and if I did not see that it had grown hair, I placed him among the spoils of the Muslims."],[182,"Washing urine from a garment was [done] seven times, and people kept raising the matter with the Prophet ﷺ until he made washing urine from a garment [to be] once."],[183,"The mut'ah of Hajj was exclusively for us, the companions of Muhammad ﷺ."],[184,"Abu Ma'n Thabit b. Nu'aym al-Hawji narrated to us, Adam b. Abi Iyas al-'Asqalani narrated to us, Qays b. al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, with his chain and something similar."],[185,"“What brought you two out at this hour?” They said, “By God, what brought us out was what we feel in our stomachs of the pangs of hunger.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “By the One in whose hand is my soul, nothing other than that brought me out.” So they stood up and set off until they came to the door of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari. Abu Ayyub had mentioned some food or milk to the Messenger of God ﷺ, but that day he was delayed and did not come at his usual time, so his family fed it [to others]. He went off to his palm trees to work among them. When they came to Abu Ayyub’s door, his wife came out and said, “Welcome to the Messenger of God ﷺ and those with him.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her, “Where is Abu Ayyub?” She said, “He will come to you, O Prophet of God, this hour.” The Messenger of God ﷺ turned back, and Abu Ayyub caught sight of him while he was working among some palm trees of his. He came hurrying until he caught up with the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “Welcome to the Prophet of God and those with him.” He said, “O Messenger of God, this is not the time at which you used to come to me,” so he brought him back. He went to a cluster of palm trees and cut it. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, “What did you intend by this?” He said, “O Messenger of God, I wanted you to eat from its fresh ripe dates, its unripe dates, its dried dates, and its low-hanging stalks, and I will certainly slaughter for you along with this.” He said, “If you slaughter, do not slaughter a milking animal.” So he took a young she-goat or a young he-goat of his and slaughtered it, and said to his wife, “Bake bread, and I will cook. You know better about baking.” He set about half of the kid and cooked it, and roasted half. When the food was ready, it was placed before the Messenger of God ﷺ and his companions. The Messenger of God ﷺ took some of the kid and placed it on a loaf, then said, “O Abu Ayyub, send this to Fatimah; she has not had the like of this for days.” When they ate and were full, the Prophet ﷺ said, “Bread, meat, unripe dates, dried dates, fresh ripe dates,” and his eyes filled with tears. Then he said, “This is part of the bliss about which you will be asked on the Day of Resurrection.” That weighed heavily upon his companions. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “When you obtain the like of this and reach out with your hands, say, ‘In the name of God and by God’s blessing,’ and when you are full, say, ‘Praise be to God who filled us, quenched our thirst, bestowed favor, and excelled’; for this suffices for that.” The Messenger of God ﷺ would not have anyone do him a kindness without wanting to repay him, so he said to Abu Ayyub, “Come to us tomorrow.” He did not hear, so 'Umar said to him, “The Messenger of God ﷺ is telling you to come to him.” When he came to him, he gave him a young slave girl and said, “O Abu Ayyub, treat her well, for we have seen nothing but good as long as she was with us.” When Abu Ayyub brought her, he said, “I find nothing better for the testament of the Messenger of God ﷺ than to manumit her,” so he manumitted her. No one narrated it from 'Abd Allah b. Kaysan except al-Fadl b. Musa."],[186,"Remorse is repentance."],[187,"When the Prophet ﷺ arrived in Makkah, he circumambulated the House seven times, then went out from the gate of al-Safa and climbed al-Safa. He said, “We begin with what God began with.” Then he recited, “Indeed, al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the rites of God.”"],[188,"There is no prophet and no ruler but that he has two inner circles: an inner circle that commands him to what is right and good and guides him to it, and an inner circle that does not spare any effort to corrupt him. Whoever is protected from the inner circle of corruption has indeed been protected."],[189,"I never heard the Messenger of God ﷺ grant a dispensation for any kind of lying except in three cases. The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say, “I do not count them as lying: a man who makes peace between people, intending thereby reconciliation; a man who says something in war; and a man speaking to his wife, or a woman speaking to her husband.”"],[190,"He used to stand in prayer at night until his feet became cracked. 'A'ishah said, “Do you do this when God has forgiven you your past and future sins?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Should I not be a grateful servant?”"],[191,"Whoever I am his mawla, 'Ali is his mawla."],[192,"God does not conceal a servant’s sin in this world and then reproach him for it on the Day of Resurrection."],[193,"Whoever falsely accuses his slave of adultery, the prescribed punishment will be carried out on him on the Day of Resurrection."],[194,"The Prophet ﷺ said on the Day of the Confederates: O Allah, Revealer of the Book, Mover of the clouds, Swift in reckoning, Defeater of the confederates—defeat them and shake them."],[195,"The prayer is cut off by the black dog, the woman, and the donkey. I said: What is it about the black one as opposed to the red or the yellow one? He said: O son of my brother, I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ just as you asked me, and he said: \"The black dog is a devil.\""],[196,"O Abu Hurayrah, when you perform ablution, say: In the name of Allah, and praise be to Allah; for your guardian angels will not rest from writing good deeds for you until you break that ablution."],[197,"The Prophet ﷺ gave Khaybar on the basis of half of what the land and the palm trees produced."],[198,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Should I wipe over the leather socks, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes, three days for the traveler, and they are not removed due to defecation, urination, or sleep, and one day for the resident."],[199,"The people of good in this world are the people of good in the Hereafter, and the people of evil in this world are the people of evil in the Hereafter."],[200,"The creation of any one of you is gathered in his mother's womb for forty days, then he becomes a clinging clot for a similar period, then a lump of flesh for a similar period. Then the angel comes and writes: wretched or blessed, male or female."],[201,"Be upright toward Quraysh as long as they are upright toward you. But if they do not do so, then put your swords on your shoulders and destroy their green ones. And if you do not do that, then be wretched farmers, eating from the labor of your own hands."],[202,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ: As for the greeting of peace (salam), I know it, but how is the prayer upon you? So he taught him to say: O Allah, send prayers upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent prayers upon Ibrahim; truly You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. And bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim; truly You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."],[203,"Indeed, peace (salam) is one of the names of Allah—exalted is He—which He placed on earth as a greeting for the people of our religion and a security for the people under our protection."],[204,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: Recite to me. I said: Should I recite to you when it was revealed to you? He said: \"I love to hear it from someone other than myself.\" So I began and recited Surah al-Nisa' until I reached: \"So how will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and We bring you as a witness against these?\" His eyes welled up with tears, so I stopped. He said: \"Ask, and you will be given.\""],[205,"Regarding His saying – Mighty and Majestic is He –: “Say: I ask of you no reward for it, save affection among the near of kin” [Q 42:23], he said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had no clan of Quraysh but that he had a mother among them, until he had a mother among Hudhayl. So Allah – Mighty and Majestic is He – said: ‘Say: I ask of you no reward for it, except that you safeguard me regarding my relatives, and do not betray me, and do not call me a liar, and do not harm me.’”"],[206,"When one of you doubts in his prayer, let him strive for what is correct and prostrate twice while sitting."],[207,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ bought a camel from me and let me ride its back as far as Madinah."],[208,"Let none of you wish for death. If he must, let him say: ‘O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is better for me, and take me when death is better for me.’"],[209,"No human being performs a deed more saving from the punishment than the remembrance of Allah – Mighty and Majestic is He.” It was said: “Not even jihad in the way of Allah?” He said: “Except that you strike with your sword until it breaks.”"],[210,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the Ka‘bah on the Day of Conquest, and around the Ka‘bah there were three hundred and sixty idols. He began thrusting them with a stick and saying: “The truth has come and falsehood has vanished; indeed falsehood is bound to vanish” [Q 17:81], and they fell on their faces."],[211,"There is no prayer for one who does not recite the Opening of the Book."],[212,"Blessed is he who controls his tongue, whose house is spacious enough for him, and who weeps over his error."],[213,"It will be said to the people of Paradise: ‘You shall be healthy and never fall ill; you shall live and never die; you shall enjoy comfort and never be miserable; you shall remain youthful and never grow old.’"],[214,"Whoever is hungry or in need and conceals it from people, complaining only to Allah, Allah is bound to open for him provision for a year from lawful sources."],[215,"A pilgrim in ihram was thrown by his riding camel [his she-camel] and died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Wash him with water and lotus leaves, shroud him in his two garments, do not cover his head, and do not bring perfume near him; for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.”"],[216,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood at a house in which there were a number of Quraysh. He took hold of the two doorposts and said: “Is there anyone in the house but a Qurayshi?” They said: “No, except a son of a sister of ours.” He said: “The son of a people’s sister is one of them.” Then he said: “This affair will remain with Quraysh as long as, when mercy is asked of them, they show mercy; when they judge, they are just; and when they distribute, they are equitable. Whoever among them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people.”"],[217,"The Messenger of God ﷺ named himself to us with names, some of which we memorized. He said: “I am Muhammad, and Ahmad, and al-Muqaffī, and the Prophet of Mercy, and the Prophet of Compassion.”"],[218,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “I desire jihād but I am not able to do it.” He said: “Do you still have either of your parents?” He said: “My mother.” He said: “Then seek God’s pardon in being dutiful to her. If you do that, then you are a pilgrim, a performer of ‘umrah, and a warrior in jihād as long as your mother is pleased with you. So fear God and be dutiful to her.”"],[219,"Some people from Kindah came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: “You are from us,” and they claimed him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “We do not deny our mother, nor do we disavow our father. We are from the descendants of al-Naḍr b. Kinānah.”"],[220,"Sūrat al-An‘ām was sent down upon me all at once, escorted by seventy thousand angels, who had a loud chanting of glorification and praise."],[221,"God is gentle and loves gentleness, and He gives for gentleness what He does not give for harshness."],[222,"If you spit during prayer, spit to your left or under your left foot."],[223,"A man’s being killed defending his wealth is martyrdom."],[224,"Whoever helps an oppressor with falsehood in order to invalidate a right by his falsehood has disavowed the protection of God, Mighty and Majestic, and the protection of His Messenger ﷺ. Whoever consumes a dirham of usury is like one who commits thirty-three acts of fornication. And whoever’s flesh grows from unlawful earnings, the Fire is more fitting for him."],[225,"The mother of Abū Ṭalḥah’s sons, who was Umm Sulaym, came and said: “O Messenger of God, God is not ashamed of the truth: Is a woman required to perform the purificatory bath if she sees what a man sees?” I laughed and said: “Does a woman have a wet dream?” He ﷺ said: “If it were not for that, she would not resemble his mother.”"],[226,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while an Abyssinian slave of his was massaging his back. I said: “What is the matter with you, O Messenger of God?” He said: “The she-camel bolted with me.”"],[227,"I was eating with the Prophet ﷺ some ḥays in a wooden bowl. ‘Umar ؓ passed by and he called him, so he ate. His finger touched my finger, and he said: “If I were obeyed concerning you women, no eye would see you.” Then the verse of the veil was revealed."],[228,"We did not fast with the Messenger of God ﷺ twenty-nine days more often than we fasted with him thirty days."],[229,"Whoever has a boy born to him should offer an 'aqiqah for him from camels, cows, or sheep."],[230,"She came to the Prophet ﷺ and said that she was experiencing istihadah (non-menstrual bleeding). She claimed that he said: 'That is a vein. So when the menstrual period comes, abandon the prayer; and when it departs, perform ghusl, wash the blood from yourself, then pray.'"],[231,"Modesty is all good."],[232,"I seek Allah's forgiveness during the day, and I turn to Him in repentance one hundred times every day."],[233,"A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we have learned how to greet you with salam, but how do we send salah upon you?' He said: 'Say: O Allah, send salah upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent salah upon Ibrahim; indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim; indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.'"],[234,"Whoever says at the time of his death: 'There is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, and there is no might or power except with Allah,' the Fire will never consume him."],[235,"Fatimah bt. Qays asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the woman with istihadah. He said: 'She should sit for the days of her menstrual periods, then perform ghusl at every time of purity, then use a cloth, and pray.'"],[236,"If there is anything sought as a remedy and beneficial for illness, then cupping benefits against illness. So perform cupping on the seventeenth, nineteenth, or twenty-first."],[237,"The talbiyah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was: 'Here I am, O Allah, here I am. Here I am, You have no partner, here I am. Indeed all praise and favor belong to You, and sovereignty. You have no partner.'"],[238,"'Ammar asked permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'Welcome to the good and purified one.'"],[239,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never veiled himself from me since I embraced Islam, and he never saw me except that he smiled."],[240,"A woman may not be married in addition to her paternal aunt, nor in addition to her maternal aunt."],[241,"On the Day of Resurrection, the people of well-being will wish that their flesh had been cut with scissors, because of what they see of the abundant reward for the people of affliction."],[242,"The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother."],[243,"A man asked permission to enter upon her, but she refused to grant him permission. He said, \"I am your paternal uncle through breastfeeding.\" When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, she informed him, and he said, \"Grant him permission, for indeed he is your paternal uncle through breastfeeding.\""],[244,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, for what should I beat my orphan?\" He said, \"For what you would beat your own child, not safeguarding your property with his property, nor accumulating wealth from his property.\""],[245,"Umar ؓ addressed us in al-Jabiyah and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us as I stand among you, and said: \"Honor my Companions, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then falsehood will spread until a man testifies and is not asked to testify, and swears and is not asked to swear. Whoever desires the middle of Paradise, let him adhere to the community, for Satan is with the one, and he is farther from the two. Indeed, no man should be alone with a woman, for the third of them is Satan. Indeed, whoever is pleased by his good deed and grieved by his evil deed is a believer.\""],[246,"Al-Abbas ؓ came to visit the Prophet ﷺ during his illness, so he lifted him and seated him in his place on his bed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"May Allah raise you, O uncle.\" Al-Abbas said: \"Here is Ali seeking permission.\" He said: \"Let him enter.\" So he entered, and with him were al-Hasan and al-Husayn. Al-Abbas said: \"These are your children, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"And they are your children, O uncle.\" He said: \"I love them.\" He said: \"May Allah love you as you love them.\""],[247,"Whoever goes on a sea expedition in the cause of Allah—and Allah knows best who goes in His cause—has fulfilled all of his obedience to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sought Paradise in every pursuit, and fled from the Fire in every escape."],[248,"When a man wakes his wife at night, and they perform ablution and pray, they are recorded among the men who remember Allah often and the women who remember."],[249,"The people of Paradise, when they have intercourse with their wives, they return as virgins."],[250,"A person is with the one he loves."],[251,"When we traveled with our Prophet ﷺ, he commanded us to wipe over our leather socks for three days and their nights, and for the resident, one day and one night."],[252,"The wayfarer is the first to drink."],[253,"Eat the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal there is blessing."],[254,"The sandal of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had two straps, the sandal of Abu Bakr had two straps, and the sandal of 'Umar had two straps. The first to tie a single knot was 'Uthman."],[255,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I carried my mother on my neck for two farsakhs in intense heat, such that had you thrown a piece of meat into it, it would have cooked. Have I fulfilled her gratitude?' He said, 'Perhaps that may be for a single labor pain.'"],[256,"When a dog laps in the vessel of one of you, let him wash it with water seven times."],[257,"Every prayer in which the Opening of the Book is not recited is deficient."],[258,"A group from 'Uraynah came to the Prophet ﷺ and found Madinah unwholesome, so the Prophet ﷺ sent them out to the camels of charity. They drank from their milk and recovered, then they drove off the camels and apostatized from Islam. The Prophet ﷺ ordered that they be pursued, and they were overtaken. He cut off their hands and gouged out their eyes."],[259,"On the morning I had a wet dream, I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and told him that I had had a wet dream. He said, 'Do not enter upon women.' No day that came upon me was harder than that."],[260,"The excellence of 'A'ishah over women is like the excellence of tharid over all other food."],[261,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade shaving the nape of the neck except for cupping."],[262,"He forbade, during the battle of Awtas, that a man have intercourse with a pregnant woman until she gives birth."],[263,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to perform ghusl on Friday."],[264,"I was sent as a mercy, a guided one."],[265,"O Allah, bless my Ummah in its early mornings."],[266,"I memorized for you six things from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: There is no divorce except after marriage, no manumission except after ownership, no fulfillment of a vow in disobedience, no orphanhood after reaching puberty, no silence for a day until night, and no continuous fasting (wisal) in fasting."],[267,"He used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday in the first rak'ah: 'Alif Lam Mim. The revelation of the Book...' (Surah al-Sajdah), and in the second rak'ah: 'Has there come upon man...' (Surah al-Insan)."],[268,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over a funeral and said four takbirs over it."],[269,"The Prophet ﷺ gave as an extra share in the initial raid one-fourth, and in the return one-third."],[270,"The Prophet ﷺ took hold of the muscle of my calf and said: 'This is the place of the lower garment, and the lower garment has no right below the two ankles.'"],[271,"When the Prophet ﷺ prostrated, he spread his arms so that the whiteness of his armpits was visible."],[272,"Some captives were brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and there was a woman among the captives who was running about. When she found a baby among the captives, she took him, pressed him to her belly and nursed him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do you think this woman would throw her child into the fire?' We said: 'No, by Allah, while she is able not to throw him.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is more merciful to His servants than this woman is to her child.'"],[273,"The Prophet ﷺ looked toward Iraq, Syria and Yemen, then said: 'O Allah, bring their hearts to obey You, and remove those behind them.'"],[274,"When a boy knows his right hand from his left, command him to pray."],[275,"Whoever takes a span of land without right will be made to wear it around his neck on the Day of Resurrection from seven earths."],[276,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was at the standing place in Muzdalifah. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have come from the mountain of Tayyi’, and I have exhausted myself and wearied my mount. By Allah, I have not left any hill but I have stood upon it. Is there any Hajj for me, O Messenger of Allah?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever prays this prayer with us and has come to Arafah by night or day has fulfilled his rites and completed his Hajj.”"],[277,"Whoever sees me in a dream has truly seen me, for the devil cannot take my form or the form of the Kaaba."],[278,"Whoever does not trim his moustache is not one of us."],[279,"We prophets have been commanded three things: to hasten the breaking of the fast, to delay the pre-dawn meal, and to place the right hand over the left in prayer."],[280,"Do not sever relations, do not turn your backs on one another, do not hate one another, and be servants of Allah as brothers. It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days."],[281,"Have mercy on those on earth, and the One in heaven will have mercy on you."],[282,"He is not a liar who reconciles between people, saying good or conveying good."],[283,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to embrace his wives while fasting, and which of you can control his desire as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ could?"],[284,"Leave what causes you doubt for what does not cause you doubt."],[285,"Seek the Night of Decree on the twenty-seventh night."],[286,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the night prayer, and he said, “Two by two, and when one of you fears the approach of dawn, let him pray one rak’ah as witr.”"],[287,"Whoever says, ‘Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him,’ a palm tree is planted for him in Paradise."],[288,"The first to be called to Paradise are the ḥammādūn, those who praise God in prosperity and adversity."],[289,"I am the foremost of the Arabs to Paradise, Ṣuhayb is the foremost of the Romans to Paradise, Bilāl is the foremost of the Abyssinians to Paradise, and Salmān is the foremost of the Persians to Paradise."],[290,"Islam began as something strange, and it will return to being strange as it began, so blessed are the strangers. It was said: Who are the strangers, O Messenger of God? He said: Those who set things right when the people have become corrupt."],[291,"When the enemy is at the door of the house, do not go to him except with the permission of your parents."],[292,"When the Prophet ﷺ arrived from a journey, he would pray two rakʿahs."],[293,"The Messenger of God ﷺ led us in one of the two afternoon prayers, ẓuhr or ʿaṣr, and he gave the salutation after two rakʿahs. The hasty ones among the people left, saying: Has the prayer been shortened? In the group were Abū Bakr and ʿUmar, and they were too awed to speak to him. The hasty ones among the people left, and he [the Prophet] stood up [then he stood] by a piece of wood in the mosque on which he used to place his hand. A man from the group called Dhū al-Yadayn stood up to him—and the Messenger of God ﷺ used to call him Dhū al-Yadayn—and said: O Messenger of God, has the prayer been shortened or did you forget? He said: I did not forget, and the prayer has not been shortened. He asked the people, and they said: Dhū al-Yadayn has spoken the truth. So the Messenger of God ﷺ returned and prayed two rakʿahs like the first two or longer, then he prostrated twice."],[294,"Whoever performs ablution after bathing is not one of us."],[295,"The Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned Zamzam and said: It is blessed; it is food that nourishes and a cure for illness."],[296,"Visit occasionally and you will increase in love."],[297,"The imam is a guarantor, and the muezzin is entrusted. O God, guide the imams and forgive the muezzins."],[298,"Whoever is killed by his stomach will not be punished in his grave."],[299,"A man may be among the people of prayer, zakāh, ḥajj, ʿumrah, and jihād—until he mentioned the shares of good—and on the Day of Resurrection he will be recompensed only according to the measure of his intellect."],[300,"May Allah brighten the face of a servant who hears my words, understands them, and memorizes them. For perhaps a bearer of knowledge carries it to one more knowledgeable than himself. Three things upon which the heart does not bear malice: sincerity of action for Allah, sincere counsel to the rulers, and adherence to the community."],[301,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, I slaughter a sheep while I feel compassion for it. He said: And the sheep—if you have mercy on it, Allah will have mercy on you."],[302,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, my tongue has burned me. He said: Where are you from seeking forgiveness? I seek Allah's forgiveness and turn to Him in repentance one hundred times a day."],[303,"Does not the one who raises his head before the imam fear that Allah will turn his head into the head of a donkey?"],[304,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned affliction and the abundant reward Allah has prepared for its bearer if he is patient, and he mentioned well-being and the abundant reward Allah—Mighty and Majestic—has prepared for its bearer if he is grateful. I said: O Messenger of Allah, if I am given well-being and I am grateful, that is more beloved to me than being afflicted and being patient. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: And the Messenger of Allah loves well-being along with you."],[305,"Keep reciting the Qur'an, for it slips away more swiftly than birds fly to their nests."],[306,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would sit after saying the taslim until he said: O Allah, You are Peace, and from You is peace. Blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor."],[307,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to Bakr b. Wa'il: From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to Bakr b. Wa'il: Submit and you will be safe. No one read it except a man from Banu Dubay'ah, so they are called Banu al-Katib."],[308,"O Allah, bless my nation in its early mornings."],[309,"He forbade a man from slaughtering his sacrificial animal before praying."],[310,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in one of the two evening prayers—Zuhr or 'Asr—and he gave the salam after two rak'ahs. A man called Dhu al-Yadayn said to him: Has the prayer been shortened or did you forget? He said: Rather I forgot. So he stood and prayed the two rak'ahs, then prostrated two prostrations while sitting, then gave the salam."],[311,"The Prophet ﷺ applied perfume before entering ihram."],[312,"The children of Adam are on varying tiers: among them is one who is born a believer, lives as a believer, and dies as a believer; among them is one who is born a disbeliever, lives as a disbeliever, and dies as a disbeliever; and among them is one who is born a disbeliever, lives as a disbeliever, and dies as a believer."],[313,"The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to trade by sea to Syria."],[314,"The Prophet ﷺ missed a man who used to sit with him and said, \"Why do I not see so-and-so?\" They said, \"He has fallen ill,\" and they used to call fever \"ightibat.\" He said, \"Get up so we may visit him.\" When he entered upon him, the boy wept, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Do not weep, for Jibril ﷺ ...\""],[315,"Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will be bridled on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire."],[316,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: \"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity and laziness, and I seek refuge in You from harshness, heedlessness, poverty, humiliation, and destitution, and I seek refuge in You from immorality, discord, hypocrisy, seeking reputation, and showing off, and I seek refuge in You from deafness, muteness, insanity, leprosy, leukoderma, and the worst of diseases.\""],[317,"\"Who is your leader, O Banu Salimah?\" They said, \"Al-Jadd b. Qays, although we consider him miserly.\" He said, \"And what disease is worse than miserliness? Rather, your leader is al-Ja'd al-Qatat, Amr b. al-Jamuh.\""],[318,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked: \"Who are the family of Muhammad?\" He said, \"Every pious person.\" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: \"His allies are none but the pious.\""],[319,"The one who drinks from vessels of gold and silver only causes the fire of Hell to gurgle in his belly."],[320,"He prohibited khathf (throwing pebbles with the fingers)."],[321,"Whoever devotes himself entirely to Allah, Allah suffices him for every need and provides for him from where he does not expect. And whoever devotes himself entirely to this world, Allah entrusts him to it."],[322,"Anas b. Malik showed me ablution. He took a small water skin and placed it on his left side, and poured water onto his right hand and washed it three times. Then he moved the water skin to his right hand and performed ablution washing each part three times, and wiped his head three times. He took fresh water for his ear canals and wiped them. I said to him, \"You have wiped your ears?\" He said, \"O boy, they are part of the head, not part of the face.\" Then he said, \"O boy, did you see and understand, or should I repeat for you?\" I said, \"It is sufficient for me, and I have understood.\" He said, \"This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution.\""],[323,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day: \"The gates of heaven are opened on the first night of the month of Ramadan and are not closed until the last night of it.\""],[324,"Umm Salamah said: O Messenger of God, shall I go out with you on the expedition? He said: O Umm Salamah, jihad has not been prescribed for women. She said: I will treat the wounded, tend to the eye, and give water to drink. He said: \"Then yes.\""],[325,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ was in a state of major ritual impurity, he would not eat until he performed the ablution he performed for prayer."],[326,"He was asked: Where did the Messenger of God ﷺ pray when he entered the House? He said: Between the two pillars."],[327,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray at night until his feet became swollen. It was said: O Messenger of God, has not God forgiven you your past and future sins? He said: \"Should I not be a grateful servant?\""],[328,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was of medium height among the people, neither very tall nor short. He had a fair complexion, neither very white nor very dark. His hair was wavy, neither tightly curled nor straight. He was sent at the age of forty, and he stayed in Makkah for ten years and in Madinah for ten years, and he died at the age of sixty. There were not twenty white hairs on his head or in his beard."],[329,"God accepts charitable gifts, and He accepts only what is good from them, and He takes them with His right hand. Then He nurtures it for its owner as a man nurtures his foal or his young camel, until a morsel becomes like Mount Uhud."],[330,"\"Close up the rows, and let not Satan pass between you like small black sheep.\" It was said: What are small black sheep? He said: \"Black sheep that are in the land of Yemen.\""],[331,"\"Might is My lower garment, and pride is My cloak. Whoever contends with Me over either, I will punish him.\""],[332,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up only for the funeral procession that passed by him because it was the funeral of a Jew, and so he stood for it."],[333,"There is no treacherous person but he will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection by which he will be known."],[334,"Injury caused by a beast is without liability, and he ruled that one-fifth is due on buried treasure."],[335,"The worst thief among people is the one who steals his prayer. It was said: O Messenger of God, how does he steal his prayer? He said: \"He does not complete its bowing or its prostration. And the most miserly of people is the one who is miserly with the greeting of peace.\""],[336,"None will enter Paradise except a believer, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, supports this religion with the wicked man."],[337,"The mother of Sulayman b. Dawud said to Sulayman ﷺ : O Sulayman, do not sleep too much at night, for much sleep at night leaves a servant poor on the Day of Resurrection."],[338,"Whoever swears a binding oath deliberately to seize thereby wealth without right will meet Allah, Mighty and Majestic, while He is angry with him."],[339,"Shall I not teach you the words that Musa ﷺ spoke when he crossed the sea with the Children of Israel? We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Say: O Allah, to You belongs praise, and to You complaint is made, and You are the One whose help is sought, and there is no might and no power except with Allah, the Most High, the Magnificent. Abdullah said: I have not left them since I heard them from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Shaqiq said: I have not left them since I heard them from Abdullah. Al-A'mash said: I have not left them since I heard them from Shaqiq. Al-A'mash said: Then someone came to me in a dream and said: O Sulayman, add to these words: And we seek Your help against corruption in us, and we ask You for the righteousness of all our affairs."],[340,"When he dispatched a military expedition, he would say: Raid in the name of Allah and in the path of Allah; fight those who disbelieve in Allah. Do not embezzle, do not act treacherously, do not be cowardly, and do not kill a child, a woman, or an old man. When you besiege the people of a town or fortress, do not grant them the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger, but grant them your own protection and the protection of your fathers; for if you violate your own protection or that of your fathers, that is better for you than violating the protection of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and the protection of His Messenger ﷺ."],[341,"When you seek a need and wish to succeed, say: There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, the Most High, the Magnificent. There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, the Wise, the Generous. In the name of Allah, besides whom there is no god, the Living, the Forbearing. Glory be to Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne. Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. As if they, on the day they see what they are promised, had tarried only an hour of a day—a communication. Will any be destroyed except the defiantly disobedient people? As if they, on the day they see it, had tarried only an evening or its morning. O Allah, I ask You for the means that necessitate Your mercy, the firm resolves of Your forgiveness, the booty of every righteousness, and safety from every sin. O Allah, leave no sin of mine but You forgive it, no worry but You relieve it, no debt but You settle it, and no need among the needs of this world and the Hereafter but You fulfill it by Your mercy, O Most Merciful of the merciful."],[342,"Allah promised me that four hundred thousand of my nation will enter Paradise. Abu Bakr said: Increase for us, O Messenger of Allah. The Prophet ﷺ said: And like this—and he brought his palms together. Umar said: Enough for you, O Abu Bakr. Abu Bakr said: Leave me, O Umar; what harm would it be to you if He admitted us all to Paradise? Umar said: If Allah, Exalted is He, willed, He would admit His creation to Paradise with a single handful. The Prophet ﷺ said: Umar has spoken the truth."],[343,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by some women of the Ansar at a wedding of theirs while they were singing: And he gifted her rams that frolic in the pen, and your husband is in the assembly, and he knows what will be tomorrow. The Prophet ﷺ said: None knows what will be tomorrow except Allah, Mighty and Majestic."],[344,"Truffles are from manna, and their water is a cure for the eye, and ajwa dates are from Paradise, and they are a cure from poison. He also said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prescribed for sciatica the tail fat of a ram, divided into three parts, then melted and drunk each day one part on an empty stomach."],[345,"Night prayer is two by two, and when you fear dawn, pray one rak'ah of witr."],[346,"Attend the Friday prayer and draw near to the imam; for a man may be among the people of Paradise, yet he stays away from Friday prayer, so he is delayed from Paradise, though he is among its people."],[347,"The prayer in congregation excels the prayer of an individual by twenty-five prayers."],[348,"Whoever wrongs his brother in any way should seek to be absolved by him today, before it is taken from his good deeds. There will be no dinar or dirham then. If he has righteous deeds, an amount equivalent to his wrongdoing will be taken from them. If he has no righteous deeds, some of the evil deeds of his companion will be taken and cast upon him."],[349,"When the Prophet ﷺ heard an ugly name, he would change it. He passed by a village called ʿAfirah and named it Khadirah."],[350,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: Shall I not teach you some words which, if you say them, you will be forgiven, although you are already forgiven? They are: There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous. There is no god but Allah, the Most High, the Magnificent. Glory be to Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne. Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."],[351,"The passing away of my community will be by stabbing and the plague. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, we know the stabbing; what is the plague? He said: 'It is a jab from your enemies among the jinn, and in each there is martyrdom.'"],[352,"The best generation is the generation in which I am, then the second, then the third, then the fourth. Allah will not care about them at all."],[353,"The people of the lofty ranks will surely be seen by those below them as you see the brilliant star on the horizon of the sky. Abu Bakr and ʿUmar are among them and have been blessed."],[354,"O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the wives of the Ansar, their offspring, and the offspring of their offspring."],[355,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: Which part of the night is most likely to have prayers answered? He said: 'The depths of the night.'"],[356,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man asked him: I sometimes say things to myself which, if I were to utter them, would nullify my reward. He said: 'No one is afflicted with such speech except a believer.'"],[357,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drink Zamzam water while standing."],[358,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said in one of the Friday sermons: 'O assembly of Muslims, this is a day which Allah has made a festival for you, so perform the ritual bath, and be diligent with the toothstick.'"],[359,"If a person knew what would come to him after death, he would not eat a single morsel or drink a single drink without weeping and striking his chest."],[360,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ, and when he did not remember a man's name he would say: “O son of Abd Allah.”"],[361,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined the Hajj and the Umrah, and performed a single tawaf for both of them."],[362,"These are for this, and these are for this. Then the people dispersed, and they did not differ concerning the divine decree."],[363,"Indeed, I am leaving among you the two weighty things, one of which is greater than the other: the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, a rope extended from the heaven to the earth, and my progeny, the people of my house. They will never separate until they return to me at the pond."],[364,"The prayer was prescribed as two rak'ahs, then an addition was made to the prayer of the resident, while the prayer of the traveller was kept as it was."],[365,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the ghusl on Friday."],[366,"He would wake up in a state of janabah without having had a wet dream; then he would perform ghusl and fast."],[367,"The Prophet ﷺ said regarding the woman in postnatal bleeding and the menstruating woman: she should perform ghusl, enter ihram, and perform all the rituals except the tawaf of the House until she becomes pure."],[368,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the mut'ah of women."],[369,"I poured water over the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he washed his hands, rinsed his mouth, sniffed water into his nose, washed his face and his forearms, and wiped over his forelock, the two leather socks, and the turban."],[370,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the hair bun for a free woman and the braided hair for a slave woman."],[371,"When one of you comes to a gathering, let him greet with salam; and when he rises, let him greet with salam. The first is not more deserving than the second."],[372,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man praying the two rakʿahs of Fajr while they were performing the Morning Prayer, so the Prophet ﷺ said to him: “Which of them have you made your prayer?”"],[373,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked: “What is the right of camels?” He said: “That you slaughter their fat ones, lend their stud males, and milk them on the day they come to water.”"],[374,"There is nothing between a servant and disbelief except abandoning the prayer."],[375,"Regarding His saying, exalted and glorified be He: “Allah intends only to remove from you the impurity, O people of the household, and to purify you with a thorough purification,” he said: “It was revealed concerning five: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, ʿAlī, Fāṭimah, al-Ḥasan, and al-Ḥusayn.”"],[376,"I am leaving among you the two weighty things; if you hold fast to them you will never go astray: the Book of Allah and my progeny. They will never separate until they return to me at the Ḥawḍ."],[377,"A man was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who had stabbed another man in his thigh with a horn. The one whose thigh was stabbed said: “Grant me retaliation, O Messenger of Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Treat it and wait with it until we see what becomes of it.” The man said: “O Messenger of Allah, grant me retaliation.” He said to him the same thing. The man said: “Grant me retaliation, O Messenger of Allah.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted him retaliation. Then the leg of the man who had been granted retaliation withered, while the leg of the man from whom retaliation had been taken healed. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ invalidated its blood money."],[378,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set the ransom for the captives of Badr from the polytheists at four thousand for each man."],[379,"The best of you are those who learn the Qur’an and teach it."],[380,"Whoever goes out seeking knowledge is in the path of Allah until he returns."],[381,"My husband divorced me three times, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not grant me accommodation or maintenance."],[382,"The likeness of the believers in their mutual love and affection is that of the body: when one part of it complains, the rest of it responds with sleeplessness and fever. In the body there is a morsel of flesh; if it is sound and safe, the body is safe, and if it is corrupt, the rest of the body becomes corrupt: the heart."],[383,"When one of you enters the mosque, let him not sit down until he prays two rakʿahs."],[384,"When the heat becomes intense, then delay the prayer until it is cooler, for the intensity of the heat is from the scorching breath of Hell."],[385,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed for rain, saying: “O Allah, give us water.” Abu Lubabah b. ʿAbd al-Mundhir said: “O Messenger of Allah, the dates are in the drying yards.” He said: “O Allah, give us water until Abu Lubabah stands naked and blocks the water outlet of his drying yard with his waist-wrapper.” And there was not a cloud to be seen in the sky, but then it rained. They gathered around Abu Lubabah and said: “It will not stop until you stand naked and block the outlet of your drying yard as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said.” So he did it, and the sky cleared."],[386,"The Prophet ﷺ freed Safiyyah and made her emancipation her dower."],[387,"The first thing to be lifted from people is trustworthiness, and the last thing to remain is prayer, and many a praying person has no good in him."],[388,"Among the best of your garments is white, so clothe your living in it and shroud your dead in it. And among the best of your kohl is ithmid; it clears the sight and makes the hair grow."],[389,"I gave the Prophet ﷺ water from Zamzam to drink, and he drank while standing."],[390,"If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would wish for a third. Nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns in forgiveness to whoever repents."],[391,"The parable of my household among you is like the ark of Noah: whoever boards it is saved, and whoever stays behind from it perishes; and like the Gate of Remission of the Children of Israel."],[392,"Whoever is placed in charge of any affair of the Muslims and then deceives them will be in the Fire."],[393,"Whoever says “There is no god but Allah” will benefit from it one day in his lifetime, even if it is after punishment befalls him."],[394,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke up in a gloomy state of mind, and he remained so until evening. I said: “O Messenger of Allah, why do I see you gloomy?” He said: “Jibril ﷺ promised to come to me and has never broken his promise to me.” They looked and found a puppy under a bed of theirs. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that puppy to be taken out, and he ordered that place to be washed with water. Then Jibril ﷺ came and said: “You promised to come to me and did not break your promise to me.” He said: “Did you not know that we do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image?”"],[395,"The best thing a man leaves behind after his death is a righteous child who supplicates for him, an ongoing charity whose reward reaches him, and knowledge that is acted upon after him."],[396,"Regarding the pregnant woman who fears for herself, that she may break the fast, and the nursing woman who fears for her child."],[397,"The mukatab pays blood money according to the portion of him that has been manumitted, the blood money of a free person, and according to the portion of him that remains enslaved, the blood money of a slave."],[398,"Whoever loses his two precious things (his eyes) and is patient and seeks reward, I will not be satisfied with any reward for him less than Paradise."],[399,"If one of you, while in his prayer, finds a passing of wind, let him leave and perform ablution."],[400,"When the Prophet ﷺ sent al-‘Ala’ al-Hadrami to al-Bahrayn, I followed him, and I saw from him three qualities, and I do not know which of them is more astonishing. We reached the shore of the sea, and he said, 'Invoke the name of God and plunge in.' So we invoked the name, and we plunged in, and we crossed, and the water only moistened the lower parts of our camels’ hooves. When we returned, we found ourselves with him in a desolate stretch of land, and we had no water with us. We complained to him, and he said, 'Pray two rak‘ahs,' then he supplicated to God, and behold, a cloud like a shield appeared, then it let down its spouts, and we drank and gave water to others. Then he died, and we buried him in the sand. After we had traveled not far, we said, 'A wild beast will come and eat him,' so we returned, and we did not see him."],[401,"The Messenger of God ﷺ applied kohl while he was fasting."],[402,"Every loan is charity."],[403,"There is no writing that is thrown away in a desolate place on earth but that God, Mighty and Majestic, sends angels to it who surround it with their wings and sanctify it until God sends to it one of His close servants, and he lifts it from the ground. And whoever lifts from the ground a writing containing one of the names of God, Exalted be He, God raises his name in ‘Illiyyin and lightens the punishment for his parents, even if they were disbelievers."],[404,"O Muhammad, when you see people fighting over worldly things, then take your sword to the greatest rock in the Haram and strike it with it until it breaks, then sit in your house until a sinful hand comes to you or a decisive death.' So I did what the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me."],[405,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to make abundant remembrance, speak little vain talk, lengthen the prayer, and shorten the sermon, and he did not disdain to walk with the widow and the poor person to fulfill their needs."],[406,"The Prophet ﷺ was turned away from the qiblah while they were in prayer, so they turned during their bowing."],[407,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us and said, 'Take your shield.' We said, 'O Messenger of God, is it from an enemy that has come?' He said, 'Take your shield from the Fire. Say: Glory be to God, and praise be to God, and there is no god but God, and God is greatest, and there is no might and no power except with God; for they will come on the Day of Resurrection preceding and following and saving, and they are the enduring good deeds.'"],[408,"The fragrance of Paradise can be scented from a distance of five hundred years, but the one who reminds others of his favors, the one addicted to wine, and the one who is disobedient to his parents will not smell it."],[409,"I was among the captives on the day of Badr. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Treat the captives well.' I was with a group of the Ansar, and whenever they presented their lunch or dinner, they would eat the dates and feed me the bread, following the instruction of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to them."],[410,"Two things will not be combined in the Fire in a way that harms either of them: a Muslim who kills a disbeliever and then remains upright and does good. And two things will not be combined in the heart of a believer: dust in the path of Allah and the scorching heat of Hell. And two things will not be combined in the heart of a believer: faith and envy."],[411,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ observed i'tikaf in a dome made of palm leaves, with a door made of a straw mat, while the people were in the mosque."],[412,"People are like a hundred camels, among which you can hardly find one suitable for riding."],[413,"I was walking with Ibn Umar when he passed by some people who had set up a bird as a target. Ibn Umar said, 'May Allah curse the one who did this. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding this.'"],[414,"Allah, the Exalted, revealed to me that I should marry my two noble daughters to Uthman."],[415,"\"What an excellent young man Khuraym is, if only he would shorten his hair and raise his lower garment.\" Khuraym said, \"My hair will not go beyond my ears, nor my lower garment beyond my heels.\""],[416,"Wipe yourselves with the earth, for it is kind to you."],[417,"Whoever recites Ya Sin during the day or night, seeking the pleasure of Allah, will be forgiven."],[418,"Al-Abbas, the uncle of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, was among those who guarded him. When this verse was revealed: 'O Messenger, convey what has been sent down to you from your Lord. If you do not, then you have not conveyed His message. Allah will protect you from the people,' the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped having guards."],[419,"A promise is a debt."],[420,"If the one passing in front of a man while he is praying knew what is upon him, it would be better for him to stand for a year than to take that step."],[421,"We went on a military expedition with the Messenger of God ﷺ and captured some red donkeys belonging to the Jews. We slaughtered them and cooked them, and the Messenger of God ﷺ was informed. He ordered a caller, who announced among the people that the flesh of domesticated donkeys is not lawful; the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade it. They also found onions and garlic in their gardens and ate from them while the people were hungry. Then they went to the mosque, and the smell of the mosque was of onions and garlic. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever eats from this foul plant, let him not come near us in our mosque.\""],[422,"A letter came to me from the Messenger of God ﷺ, containing: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. From Muhammad, the Messenger of God ﷺ, to Ziyad b. Jahwar: You are at peace, for I praise God to you, [to you God], besides whom there is no deity. To proceed: I remind you of God and the Last Day. To proceed: every religion that people have professed will be abandoned except Islam, so know that."],[423,"Whoever ransoms a captive from the hands of the enemy, I am that captive."],[424,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had two garments that he wore on Fridays, and when he finished, we folded them until the next Friday."],[425,"The leaders are from Quraysh: their righteous ones are rulers over their righteous, and their wicked ones are rulers over their wicked. Each has a right, so give everyone with a right his due. If an Ethiopian slave with mutilated limbs is appointed over you, listen to him and obey as long as none of you is forced to choose between his Islam and the striking of his neck. If he is forced to choose between his Islam and the striking of his neck, let him stretch forth his neck, may his mother be bereft of him, for there is no worldly life or Hereafter after losing his Islam [his religion]."],[426,"A piece of gold was brought to the Prophet ﷺ as the first charity that came to him from a mine. He said: \"What is this?\" They said: \"Charity from a mine of ours.\" He said: \"There will be mines, and in them will be the worst of God's creation, mighty and majestic is He.\""],[427,"Do not revert after me to disbelief, striking one another's necks."],[428,"Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr."],[429,"God, exalted is He, is kind and loves kindness in all matters."],[430,"O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, after me there will be rulers whom he described as unjust. Whoever enters upon them, believes their lies, and helps them in their wickedness is not of me and I am not of him, and he will not come to me at the Basin. Whoever does not enter upon them, does not believe their lies, and does not help them in their wickedness is of me and I am of him, and he will come to the Basin. O Ka'b: it is right that flesh that grew from ill-gotten gain should not enter Paradise; the Fire is more fitting for it."],[431,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, my father is an old man who cannot perform the pilgrimage; shall I perform it on his behalf?\" He said: \"Would you settle a debt if he owed one?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"God's debt is more deserving. Perform the pilgrimage on his behalf.\""],[432,"Completing a kindness is better than beginning it."],[433,"The knowledgeable ones among the family of Muhammad ﷺ, and A'ishah bt. Abi Bakr, knew — so ask her — that the companions of the black one with the breast-like protrusion are cursed upon the tongue of the Prophet ﷺ."],[434,"Indeed God — Exalted is He — has those freed from the Fire every night of the month of Ramadan, except a man who broke his fast on wine."],[435,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed in a single garment, wrapping himself with it."],[436,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray while carrying Umamah bt. Abi al-'As b. al-Rabi', and she was the daughter of Zaynab bt. the Messenger of God ﷺ. When he bowed, he would put her down, and when he stood, he would carry her, until he finished his prayer."],[437,"I prayed behind Anas b. Malik ؓ a prayer in which he was forgetful with us, so he prostrated after the salam. Then he turned to us and said: Indeed I did only as I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ do."],[438,"We complained to the Messenger of God ﷺ about the scorching ground, but he did not relieve us. He said: Say often: There is no might nor power except with God, for it repels ninety-nine doors of harm, the least of which are worry and poverty."],[439,"Whoever a man becomes Muslim at his hands, Paradise is assured for him."],[440,"The ruin of my community lies in three things: in the Qadariyyah, in tribal partisanship, and in transmitting narrations without verification."],[441,"There is no shighar. They said: O Messenger of God, and what is shighar? He said: Marrying a woman in exchange for another woman, with no dower between them."],[442,"When the drop of semen settles in the womb, it remains a drop for forty nights, then it becomes a clinging clot for forty nights, then it becomes a lump of flesh for forty nights, then it becomes bones for forty nights, then God clothes the bones with flesh. Then the angel says: O Lord, male or female? And God — Mighty and Majestic — decrees, and the angel writes. Then he says: O Lord, wretched or blessed? And God — Mighty and Majestic — decrees, and the angel writes. Then he says: O Lord, his term, his provision, and his deeds? And God — Mighty and Majestic — decrees, and the angel writes."],[443,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would go out to the dawn prayer with his head dripping from the major ablution, then he would begin the day fasting."],[444,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the mosque until, when the sun rose, the Messenger of God ﷺ went out and I followed him. He said: \"Come with us so that we may enter upon Fatimah bt. Muhammad.\" We entered upon her, and she was asleep, lying down. He said: \"O Fatimah, what makes you sleep at this hour?\" She said: \"I have been feverish since last night.\" He said: \"Where is the supplication I taught you?\" She said: \"I forgot it.\" He said: \"Say: O Ever-Living, O Self-Subsisting, by Your mercy I seek help; set right for me all my affairs and do not entrust me to myself for the blink of an eye, nor to anyone among the people.\""],[445,"If the Messenger of God ﷺ saw of women what we see, he would have forbidden them the mosques as the women of the Children of Israel were forbidden."],[446,"Amputation is for a quarter dinar or more."],[447,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade throwing pebbles and said: \"No game is hunted with it, nor is an enemy wounded by it, but it gouges out an eye and breaks a tooth.\""],[448,"My intercession is for the people of major sins among my community on the Day of Resurrection."],[449,"Whoever fasts one day in the path of God, God will place between him and the Fire a trench like that between heaven and earth."],[450,"All of you are shepherds, and all of you are responsible for your flock. The ruler is a shepherd over the people and is responsible for his flock. The man is a shepherd over his household and is responsible for his wife and what his right hand possesses. The woman is a shepherdess of her husband's rights and is responsible for her house and her children. The slave is a shepherd over his master's property and is responsible for his wealth. So all of you are shepherds and all of you are responsible for your flock; therefore prepare answers for the questions.\" They said: \"O Messenger of God, and what is the answer?\" He said: \"Righteous deeds.\""],[451,"Whoever is a means for his Muslim brother to reach a person of authority in a matter of achieving a good or easing a difficulty, God will help him cross the bridge on the Day of Resurrection when feet slip."],[452,"Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will be bridled on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire."],[453,"Indeed, God has obligated upon the wealthy of the Muslims in their wealth only as much as suffices their poor. The poor will not suffer hardship when they are hungry and unclothed except because of what the wealthy neglect. Indeed, God, Mighty and Majestic, will call them to a severe reckoning on the Day of Resurrection, then punish them with a painful punishment."],[454,"The Messenger of God ﷺ often said to me: \"O A'ishah, what happened to your verses?\" I would say: \"Which of my verses do you mean, O Messenger of God? They are many.\" He would say: \"About gratitude.\" I would say: \"Yes, by my father and mother.\" The poet said: Ward off your weak one, lest his weakness overtake you one day,And consequences catch you that have grown.He will reward you or praise you, and trulyWhoever praises you for what you did is like one who repaid.Indeed, when you desire connection with a noble man,You will not find the cords of his rope weak.She said: He would say: \"O A'ishah, when God gathers the creatures on the Day of Resurrection, He will say to a servant of His servants to whom another servant of His servants has done a kindness: 'Did you thank him?' He will say: 'O Lord, I knew that was from You, so I thanked You for it.' He will say: 'You did not thank Me if you did not thank the one through whose hands I caused it to come.'\""],[455,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ: \"Which deeds are best?\" He said: \"Prayer at its proper time, dutifulness to parents, and striving in the path of God.\""],[456,"When we emigrated to Madinah, the Messenger of God ﷺ divided us into groups of ten. I was in the group of ten that was with the Messenger of God ﷺ. We had a sheep whose milk we drank among ourselves. One night he was late, and we had set aside his share for him. I got up while I was hungry and drank it. Then the Prophet ﷺ came while I had not yet slept. He went to the vessel in which we used to put the milk and found nothing in it. I said, \"O Messenger of God, shall I slaughter it?\" He said, \"No.\""],[457,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to perform witr with nine surahs in three rak'ahs: 'The mutual rivalry for piling up' (al-Takathur), 'Indeed, We sent it down on the Night of Decree' (al-Qadr), and 'When the earth is shaken' (al-Zalzalah) in one rak'ah; in the second: 'By time' (al-'Asr), 'When the victory of God comes' (al-Nasr), and 'Indeed, We have granted you the Abundance' (al-Kawthar); and in the third: 'Say, O disbelievers' (al-Kafirun), 'May the hands of Abu Lahab perish' (al-Masad), and 'Say, He is God, the One' (al-Ikhlas)."],[458,"When one of you eats, let him lick his three fingers, for he does not know in which of them the blessing lies."],[459,"God does not take away knowledge by snatching it away from people, but He takes away knowledge by taking away the scholars, until when no scholar remains, people take ignorant leaders. They are asked and they give legal opinions without knowledge, so they go astray and lead others astray."],[460,"The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is the one who abandons what God has forbidden."],[461,"Mention the good qualities of your dead, and refrain from mentioning their faults."],[462,"Convey from me even if it is a single verse, and relate from the Children of Israel, and there is no harm in that. And whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[463,"I was commanded to wear sandals and a ring."],[464,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us with two bundles in his hand, one of gold and the other of silk. He said, \"These two are forbidden for the males of my community and lawful for the females.\""],[465,"Any ruler who is put in charge of some affair of the Muslims and does not act sincerely toward them or strive for them as he strives for himself, God will cast him on his face into the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."],[466,"Do not use artificial bidding to raise prices (najash), and let no man sell over the sale of his brother, and let no settled person sell on behalf of a desert dweller, and let no man propose marriage over the proposal of his brother, and let no woman ask for the divorce of her sister so as to empty her vessel."],[467,"The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother."],[468,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was delivering a sermon, a man came stepping over people's necks until he sat close to the Prophet ﷺ. When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished his prayer, he said: \"What prevented you, O so-and-so, from coming to Friday prayer?\" He said: \"O Messenger of God, I was keen to place myself in the place you see.\" He said: \"I saw you stepping over people's necks and harming them. Whoever harms a Muslim has harmed me, and whoever harms me has harmed God, Mighty and Majestic.\""],[469,"\"It is from a woman's blessedness that her engagement is easy and her dowry is easy.\" Urwah b. al-Zubayr said: \"And I say: It is from the first of her ill-omen that her dowry be large.\""],[470,"Whoever enters a horse between two horses while he is safe from being beaten, it is gambling."],[471,"The gates of heaven are opened for five: for the recitation of the Quran, for the meeting of two armies, for the descent of rain, for the supplication of the wronged, and for the call to prayer."],[472,"Whoever does not abandon obscene speech and lying, God, Mighty and Majestic, has no need for him to abandon his food and drink."],[473,"The Prophet ﷺ prostrated in the dawn prayer with the Sūrah of the Prostration."],[474,"The Prophet ﷺ was on one of his journeys with a group of his companions, and the time for prayer came. The people did not find anything to perform ablution with. They said: \"O Messenger of God, we do not find anything to perform ablution with.\" A man from the group went off and came with a small vessel of water. The Messenger of God ﷺ performed ablution, then extended his fingers over the vessel, and they all performed ablution until they achieved what they wanted. Anas said: \"They were close to seventy.\""],[475,"Return the trust to the one who entrusted you, and do not betray the one who betrayed you."],[476,"I missed the Messenger of God ﷺ one night from his bed. I said: \"He has gone to his slave-girl Māriyah.\" I got up and felt along the wall, and I found him standing praying. I put my hand into his hair to see whether he had performed a full ablution or not. When he finished, he said: \"Your devil has taken hold of you, O ʿĀʾishah.\" I said: \"Do I have a devil?\" He said: \"Yes, and all the children of Adam.\" I said: \"And do you have a devil?\" He said: \"Yes, but God helped me against him, and he became Muslim.\""],[477,"A prayer following a prayer with no idle talk between them is a record in ʿIlliyyīn."],[478,"Two persons whose prayer does not go beyond their heads: a slave who has run away from his masters until he returns to them, and a woman who disobeys her husband until she returns."],[479,"I was about to order a man to lead the people in prayer on Friday, then burn the houses of a people who stay away from it."],[480,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon us while a young boy with us was complaining. He said: “What is wrong with him?” We said: “We suspected the evil eye in his case.” He said: “Will you not seek ruqya for him from the evil eye?”"],[481,"Barira was manumitted while she had a husband, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave her the choice. Barira was given some meat as charity, so they hung it up, and they brought food other than the meat to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: “Did I not see meat with you?” They said: “It is only something that was given as charity to Barira.” He said: “For Barira it is charity, and for us it is a gift.” Barira came to Aisha seeking her help with her kitaba (contract of manumission). Aisha said to her: “If your owners wish, I will buy you and pay your price on your behalf in one payment.” Barira went to her owners and told them that. They said: “And your wala’ will be for us.” She came to Aisha and said: “They say your wala’ will be for us.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Buy her, for the wala’ belongs to the one who manumits.”"],[482,"Journeys are not undertaken except to three mosques: this mosque of mine, the Sacred Mosque, and the Aqsa Mosque. A woman does not travel beyond two days except with her husband or a mahram. Two days in the year are not fasted: al-Fitr and al-Adha. There is no prayer after two prayers: after the Fajr prayer until the sun rises, and after Asr until the sun sets."],[483,"When the Prophet ﷺ arrived in Makkah, Abu Quhafa was brought to him with his head and beard as white as the thaghamah plant. He said: “Change the grey hair, and avoid black dye.”"],[484,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not visit a sick person except after three days."],[485,"Time does not increase except in severity, and people do not increase except in miserliness, and the Hour will not come except upon the worst of people."],[486,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Sahla bt. Suhayl, who was suffering from istihada (non-menstrual bleeding), to perform ghusl for every prayer. That was difficult for her, so he commanded her to combine Zuhr and Asr with one ghusl, and Maghrib and Isha with one ghusl, and to perform ghusl for Subh."],[487,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had direct skin contact with me while he was fasting."],[488,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Aisha and Hafsa while they were both fasting. Then he left and returned while they were eating. He said: “Were you not fasting?” They said: “Yes, but this food was given to us as a gift, and it pleased us, so we ate from it.” He said: “Fast another day in its place.”"],[489,"He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him disheveled and dusty in the appearance of a Bedouin. He said to him: “What wealth do you have?” He said: “Of every kind of wealth, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has given me.” He said: “When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, bestows a blessing upon a servant, He loves to see its trace upon him.”"],[490,"A surah of the Quran, which is only thirty verses, will argue on behalf of its companion until it enters him into Paradise, and it is Surah Tabarak."],[491,"Whoever is made a judge has been slaughtered without a knife."],[492,"I used to perform ghusl, I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from a single vessel, and I would say, \"Leave some for me, leave some for me.\""],[493,"Every condition that is not in the Book of Allah is invalid, even if it is a hundred conditions."],[494,"\"Be shy of Allah with true shyness.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we are shy, and praise be to Allah.\" He said, \"Whoever is shy of Allah with true shyness, let him guard the head and what it contains, and the belly and what it encloses, and let him remember death and affliction. And whoever desires the Hereafter, let him abandon the adornment of this world. Whoever does that has been shy of Allah with true shyness.\""],[495,"It will be said to the disbeliever, \"Who is your Lord?\" He will say, \"I do not know.\" At that moment he is deaf, blind, and mute. Then he is struck with a sledgehammer; if a mountain were struck with it, it would turn to dust. Everything hears it except the two heavy species (humans and jinn). He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite: \"Allah keeps firm those who believe with the firm word in the life of this world and in the Hereafter, and Allah sends astray the wrongdoers\" [Quran 14:27]."],[496,"Arguing about the Quran is disbelief."],[497,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed behind Abu Bakr ؓ."],[498,"My beloved friend Abu al-Qasim ﷺ enjoined upon me three things: fasting three days of every month, performing ghusl on Friday, and praying witr before sleeping."],[499,"When the muezzin gives the call to prayer in a village, Allah protects it from His punishment that day."],[500,"I took on a blood-money obligation for my people, so I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have taken on a blood-money obligation for my people, so help me with it.\" He said, \"Rather, we will bear it on your behalf, O Qabisah. It is for you from the zakat when it comes.\" Then he said, \"O Qabisah, asking is only lawful for one of three: a man who takes on a blood-money obligation for his people, intending thereby to bring about reconciliation, and he asks until he reaches the amount or is close, then he refrains; a man afflicted by a calamity that destroys his wealth, and he asks until he obtains enough to meet his basic needs; and a man afflicted by poverty, and three men of sound judgment from his people testify, saying, 'So-and-so has been afflicted by poverty,' and he asks until he obtains enough to sustain himself or meet his basic needs, then he refrains. Anything else besides these, asking is unlawful earnings that its owner consumes.\""],[501,"There is no divorce except after marriage."],[502,"Whoever intends a good deed but does not do it, a good deed is recorded for him. If he does it, it is recorded for him ten times its like up to seven hundred and seven times its like. Whoever intends an evil deed but does not do it, it is not recorded against him. If he does it, it is recorded against him as one evil deed, or Allah, Mighty and Majestic, erases it."],[503,"I prayed beside the Prophet ﷺ, and Aisha ؓ was behind us praying with us, while I was beside the Prophet ﷺ."],[504,"When one of you complains of pain, let him place his hand on that pain, then say: 'In the name of Allah and by Allah; I seek refuge in the might of Allah and His power from the evil of this pain of mine.'"],[505,"Prayer is interrupted by a black dog, a donkey, and a woman. I said to Abu Dharr: 'What is the matter with the black dog as opposed to other dogs?' He said: 'O son of my brother, I asked the Prophet ﷺ just as you asked me, and he said: \"O Abu Dharr, the black dog is a devil.\"'"],[506,"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs of Duha, Allah will build for him thereby a palace of gold in Paradise."],[507,"The most severely punished of people on the Day of Resurrection will be a scholar whose knowledge did not benefit him."],[508,"A man used to go to 'Uthman b. 'Affan ؓ concerning a need of his, but 'Uthman would not turn to him nor look into his need. So he met 'Uthman b. Hunayf and complained about that to him. 'Uthman b. Hunayf said to him: 'Go to the place of ablution and perform wudu', then go to the mosque and pray two rak'ahs in it, then say: \"O Allah, I ask You and turn to You by our Prophet Muhammad ﷺ, the Prophet of mercy. O Muhammad, I turn by you to your Lord [my Lord], Mighty and Majestic, that He may fulfill my need.\" And mention your need, then come to me so that I may go with you.' So the man went and did what 'Uthman told him. Then he came to the door of 'Uthman, and the doorkeeper came and took him by the hand and brought him into 'Uthman b. 'Affan, who seated him with him on the cushion and said: 'Your need?' He mentioned his need, and he fulfilled it for him. Then he said to him: 'I did not remember your need until this very hour,' and he said: 'Whatever need you have, come to us.' Then the man left him and met 'Uthman b. Hunayf and said to him: 'May Allah reward you well. He had not been looking into my need nor turning to me until you spoke to him about me.' 'Uthman b. Hunayf said: 'By Allah, I did not speak to him. But I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a blind man came to him and complained to him about the loss of his sight. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Will you not be patient?\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I have no guide, and it has become hard for me.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Go to the place of ablution, perform wudu', then pray two rak'ahs, then supplicate with these words.\" 'Uthman said: \"By Allah, we had not parted and the conversation had not gone on long before the man entered upon us as if he had never had any affliction at all.\""],[509,"Hearts have rust like the rust of iron, and their polish is seeking forgiveness."],[510,"A man came to al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ and asked them, and they said: 'Begging is only appropriate for three: a devastating need, a heavy guarantee, or a crushing debt.' So they gave him. Then he came to Ibn 'Umar, and he gave him without asking him. The man said to him: 'I came to your two cousins, and they asked me, but you did not ask me.' Ibn 'Umar said: 'The two sons of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were only being taught knowledge thoroughly.'"],[511,"Among what I fear for you are the desires of error in your bellies and your private parts, and the misguiding whims."],[512,"A person may do the deeds of the people of the Fire for a period of his life, then the path of the people of Paradise is presented to him, and he acts upon it until he dies upon it, and that is what was decreed for him. And a man may do the deeds of the people of Paradise for a period of his life, then the path of the people of the Fire is presented to him, and he acts upon it until he dies upon it, and that is what was decreed for him."],[513,"\"I was tending sheep belonging to the family of Abu Mu'ayt. The Prophet ﷺ came with Abu Bakr ؓ and said: 'O boy, do you have milk?' I said: 'Yes, but I am entrusted.' He said: 'Do you have a ewe that no male has mounted?' I said: 'Yes,' indicating a shatur ewe. Sallam said: 'A shatur is one that has no udder.' The Prophet ﷺ stroked the place of the udder, and it had no udder, but suddenly the udder was full and overflowing with milk. I brought the Prophet ﷺ a hollowed-out rock, and he milked it, then gave Abu Bakr to drink and gave me to drink. Then he said to the udder: 'Shrink,' and it returned as it was. So I saw this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, teach me.' He stroked my head and said: 'May Allah bless you, for you are a taught boy.' So I embraced Islam and came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. While we were with him on Hira', Surat al-Mursalat 'Urfan was revealed to him, and I took it while it was still fresh from his mouth. I took seventy surahs from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I took the rest of the Qur'an from his Companions.\""],[514,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched a military expedition, he would say: 'Raid in the name of Allah and in the path of Allah. Fight those who disbelieve in Allah. Do not steal from the spoils, do not act treacherously, do not mutilate, and do not kill a child or an old man.'"],[515,"I saw 'Uthman b. 'Affan ؓ perform wudu': he rinsed his mouth three times, sniffed water into his nose three times, washed his face three times, washed his hands three times each, wiped his head once, and washed his feet three times. Then he said: 'Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performing wudu.'"],[516,"The transgressing party will kill ʿAmmār."],[517,"Adhere to marriage, for whoever cannot afford it should fast, for it will be a shield for him."],[518,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade making an exception unless its nature is known."],[519,"Whoever visits a sick person immerses himself in mercy until he reaches him, and when he sits with him, mercy envelops him. When the Prophet ﷺ said what he said, I said, 'O Messenger of God, this is for the visitor of the sick, what is for the sick person?' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'When a servant is ill for three days, he emerges from his sins as on the day his mother gave birth to him.'"],[520,"The remorseful person awaits repentance, and the self-admiring person awaits disdain."],[521,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade killing frogs and said, 'Their croaking is glorification.'"],[522,"I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ, then I turned to leave, and he called me and said, 'I will not accept from you until you pledge to give sincere counsel to every Muslim,' so I pledged allegiance to him."],[523,"Tanning the hide purifies it."],[524,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to teach us istikhārah as he taught us a sūrah from the Qur'an, saying: 'When one of you intends a matter, let him say: O God, I seek Your guidance through Your knowledge, and I seek Your power through Your might, and I ask You of Your immense bounty; for You have power and I have none, and You know and I do not, and You are the Knower of the unseen. O God, if this matter is good for me in my religion, my worldly life, and my ultimate outcome, then decree it for me; and if something else is better, then facilitate good for me wherever it may be and avert evil from me wherever it may be, and make me content with Your decree.'"],[525,"The Messenger of God ﷺ led us in prayer during the month of Ramadan, eight rakʿahs, and then performed witr. The following night we gathered in the mosque hoping he would come out, and we remained there until morning. Then we entered upon him and said, 'O Messenger of God, we gathered last night in the mosque hoping that you would pray with us.' He said, 'I feared that it would be made obligatory upon you.'"],[526,"The heat of the Fire is seventy parts: sixty-nine for the one who commanded and one part for the killer, and that suffices him."],[527,"We used to greet the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying, and he would respond to us before we emigrated to Abyssinia. When we returned from Abyssinia, I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and greeted him, but he did not return my greeting. I was seized by distress over what is near and far, so I said, 'What is wrong with me? Has something happened to me or has something been revealed concerning me?' He said, 'No, O Ibn Masʿūd, God introduces in His command whatever He wills, and He has now introduced that you should not speak during prayer.'"],[528,"No year comes but the one after it is worse than it. We heard that from your Prophet ﷺ."],[529,"When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the prescribed one."],[530,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: Fear Allah wherever you are, and follow up a bad deed with a good deed that erases it, and treat people with good character."],[531,"He pronounced the talbiyah for Hajj and Umrah together. He mentioned that to Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ, and he said: You have been guided to the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ."],[532,"When it was revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'And whether you disclose what is in your own selves or conceal it, Allah will call you to account for it,' this weighed heavily on the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then it was revealed: 'He forgives whom He wills and punishes whom He wills,' and that relieved them."],[533,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and confessed to adultery, and she was pregnant. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed her until she gave birth, then he ordered her and her garments were fastened tightly around her, then he ordered her to be stoned, then he prayed over her. A man said to him: You pray over her when she committed adultery and you stoned her? The Prophet ﷺ said: She has repented with such a repentance that if seventy of the people of Madinah were to repent with it, it would be accepted from them. Have you found anything better than her giving her own life?"],[534,"The people of Yemen have come to you. They are most tender of hearts. Faith is Yemeni, wisdom is Yemeni, and understanding is Yemeni."],[535,"I said to Abdullah b. Umar ؓ: Did you witness the Pledge of Ridwan with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: Yes. I said: What was he wearing? He said: \"A cotton shirt, a stuffed jubbah, a cloak, and a sword. And I saw al-Numan b. Muqarrin al-Muzani standing at his head, holding up the branches of the tree from his head while the people were giving him the pledge.\""],[536,"Anas b. Malik ؓ mentioned seventy men from the Ansar. When night fell upon them, they would return to a signpost in Madinah and spend the night studying the Quran. When morning came, whoever had strength would gather firewood and fetch fresh water, and whoever had means would get a sheep and prepare it, so that by morning it would be hanging at the rooms of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When Khubayb was killed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent them out, and among them was my maternal uncle Haram b. Milhan. They came upon a clan of Banu Sulaym. Haram said to their leader: Shall I tell these people that we are not after them, so they will let us pass? They said: Yes. So he went to them and told them that. A man from among them met him with a spear and ran it through him. When Haram felt the touch of the spear in his body, he said: I have won, by the Lord of the Kabah. They closed in on them, and none of them remained to report. I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ grieve for a raiding party as he grieved for them. Anas said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ every time he prayed the morning prayer raise his hands supplicating against them. Then later Abu Talhah came saying: Do you want the killer of Haram? The Prophet said: What is the matter with him? May Allah do such and such to him. Abu Talhah said: Do not say that, for he has embraced Islam."],[537,"He entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was sleeping. The Prophet ﷺ woke up and hugged Halah to his chest, saying: Halah, Halah, Halah."],[538,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raided the people of Khaybar while they were unaware. They said: Muhammad and the army. The Prophet ﷺ said: Allah is greatest. Khaybar is destroyed. When we descend upon the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those warned."],[539,"I saw Ibrahim the Friend ﷺ on the night I was taken on the Night Journey. He said: O Muhammad, convey my greetings of peace to your community, and tell them that Paradise is good of soil, sweet of water, and that it is a plain, and its plants are the saying: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest, and there is no power and no strength except with Allah."],[540,"Whoever goes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl."],[541,"He used to test those of the believing women who emigrated to him with this verse: “O Prophet, when believing women come to you…” to the end of the entire verse."],[542,"He was in the house of Maymūnah ؓ, and water for purification was placed for the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Who placed it?” It was said: “Ibn ʿAbbās.” So he patted my shoulder and said: “O Allāh, give him understanding in religion and teach him interpretation.”"],[543,"Whoever learns archery and then forgets it, it is a blessing he has denied."],[544,"A person’s prayer in his home is better than his prayer in this mosque of mine, except for the prescribed prayers."],[545,"By Allāh, what is the world from its beginning to its end in comparison to the Hereafter except as when one of you puts his finger into the sea—let him see what he brings back."],[546,"Every intoxicant is khamr, and every intoxicant is unlawful."],[547,"The rewards of my community were shown to me, even the speck of dust that a man removes from the mosque, and the sins of my community were shown to me, and I did not see a sin greater than that of a man who was given an āyah or a sūrah and then forgot it."],[548,"It was reported from ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd ؓ that he was asked about a daughter, a son’s daughter, and a full sister (from the same father and mother). He said: “I will judge among them with the judgment of the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ: the daughter receives half, the son’s daughter receives one-sixth, and what remains goes to the full sister.”"],[549,"He liked, when going out for some need, to hear: “O Najīḥ, O Rāshid.”"],[550,"Nothing placed in the balance is weightier than good character."],[551,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ wrapping al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn in his garment, and he was saying: “These two are my sons and the sons of Fāṭimah. O Allāh, You know that I love them both.”"],[552,"Do not face the qiblah when defecating or urinating."],[553,"There is nothing for which there is no repentance except a person of bad character, for he does not repent from a sin without returning to something worse than it."],[554,"The destruction of my ummah will be at the hands of young boys from the foolish ones of Quraysh."],[555,"Three things: whoever does them has tasted the flavor of faith: whoever worships Allah (Mighty and Majestic) alone, that there is no god but He; and gives the zakah of his wealth willingly each year, and does not give the old, the mangy, or the sick, but from the middle of your wealth—for Allah (Mighty and Majestic) does not ask you for its best and does not command you to give its worst—and purifies his soul. A man said: 'What is purification of the soul?' He said: 'To know that Allah (Mighty and Majestic) is with him wherever he is.'"],[556,"The most merciful of my ummah to my ummah is Abu Bakr, and the most gentle of my ummah to my ummah is 'Umar b. al-Khattab, and the most honest in modesty of my ummah is 'Uthman, and the best judge of my ummah is 'Ali b. Abi Talib, and the most knowledgeable of it about the lawful and the unlawful is Mu'adh b. Jabal—he will come on the Day of Resurrection ahead of the scholars by a bow-shot—and the best reciter of my ummah is Ubayy b. Ka'b, and the best at the obligatory shares is Zayd b. Thabit, and 'Uwaymir has been given worship—meaning Abu al-Darda' ؓ all together."],[557,"O Allah, make us among those who have crossed the abode of the wrongdoers, and have felt estranged from the company of the ignorant, and have mixed the fruit of deeds with the light of sincerity, and have drawn water from the spring of wisdom, and have boarded the ship of discernment, and have sailed with the breeze of certainty, and have plunged into the sea of salvation, and have anchored at the shore of sincerity. O Allah, make us among those whose souls have roamed in the heights and have picked from the fruits of the gardens of gentle breeze, and have waded into the deep of joy, and have drunk from the cup of life, and have sought shade under [in] honor. O Allah, make us among those who have opened the gate of patience, and have blocked the trenches of anxiety, and have passed through the severe punishments, and have crossed the bridge of desire, for He—glorified be His name—says: 'But as for him who feared the standing before his Lord and restrained the soul from desire, then Paradise is the refuge.' O Allah, make us among those to whom the banners of guidance have pointed, and for whom the path of salvation has become clear, and who have traveled the way of pure certainty."],[558,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Mu'adh b. Jabal: 'Shall I teach you a supplication to invoke? If you had a debt like a mountain, Allah would settle it for you. Say, O Mu'adh: O Allah, Owner of the kingdom, You give the kingdom to whom You will and take the kingdom from whom You will, and You honor whom You will and humble whom You will. In Your hand is all good; You have power over all things. Most Merciful of this world and the Hereafter, You give them to whom You will and withhold them from whom You will. Have mercy on me with a mercy that suffices me from the mercy of anyone other than You.'"],[559,"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when some Bedouins came to him and began asking him on his right and left: 'O Messenger of Allah, is there any sin on us in such and such? Is there any sin on us in such and such?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah has removed sin except for a man who borrows from a Muslim man wrongfully—that is the one who sins and is destroyed.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, should we seek treatment for such and such?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Seek treatment, O servants of Allah, for Allah (Mighty and Majestic) has not sent down any disease but He has sent down for it a cure, except for one disease: old age.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing given to a person?' He said: 'Good character.'"],[560,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to 'A'ishah ؓ: 'O 'A'ishah, those who have divided their religion and become sects are the people of innovation and the people of desires, and there is no repentance for them. I am free of them, and they are free of me.'"],[561,"No backbiter enters Paradise, and the backbiter is the slanderer."],[562,"Whoever catches a rak'ah of Jumu'ah has caught it."],[563,"Whoever drinks from a vessel of gold or a vessel of silver, he is only gulping the fire of Hell into his belly."],[564,"There will be in the last days oppressive rulers, sinful ministers, treacherous judges, and lying jurists. Whoever among you lives to see that time should never be a tax collector, a tribal leader, or a guard for them."],[565,"If the inhabitants of the heavens and the inhabitants of the earth were to join together to kill a Muslim, God would cast them all down on their faces into the Fire."],[566,"Whoever drinks wine until he dies, it will be forbidden for him in the Hereafter."],[567,"I used to miss fasting days in Ramadan, and I would not make them up except in Sha'ban, because of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[568,"One day they were with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the house of 'A'isha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, and she ؓ . He said: While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, a platter of bread and meat was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ from the house of Umm Salama ؓ , and it was placed before the Prophet ﷺ. He said, 'Put your hands.' The Prophet ﷺ put his hand, and we put our hands and ate. Meanwhile 'A'isha was preparing a hastily cooked food. The platter that had been brought was passed around. When she finished her food, she brought it and placed it down, and she took up the platter of Umm Salama and broke it. She said and said. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Eat in the name of God. Your mother has become jealous.' Then he gave her platter to Umm Salama and said: 'Food for food, and vessel for vessel.'"],[569,"There is no right of preemption for a Christian."],[570,"Indeed, the people of the highest ranks are seen by those below them as you see the brilliant star on the horizon of the sky. Indeed Abu Bakr and 'Umar are among them, and how excellent they are."],[571,"When he gave a sermon, he would say: 'To proceed.'"],[572,"Preserve my memory in al-'Abbas, for he is the remnant of my forefathers."],[573,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had two freedmen: an Abyssinian and a Copt. One day they insulted each other. One of them said, 'O Abyssinian!' and the other said, 'O Copt!' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Do not say that. You are both men from the family of Muhammad ﷺ.'"],[574,"Arguing about the Qur'an is disbelief."],[575,"Indeed, God, Mighty and Majestic, boasts to His angels on the evening of 'Arafa about the people of 'Arafa, saying: 'Look at My servants. They have come to Me disheveled and dusty.'"],[576,"Help your brother whether he is an oppressor or oppressed. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I help him if he is oppressed, but how can I help him if he is an oppressor?' He said, 'Restrain him from oppression, for that is your help to him.'"],[577,"I entered Paradise and heard a sound. I looked and behold, it was Bilal."],[578,"I know a tree whose likeness is that of a believing man. I, being the youngest of the people, said, 'It is the date-palm.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'It is the date-palm.'"],[579,"Whoever sends one blessing upon me, Allah sends ten blessings upon him."],[580,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about Khalid b. al-Walid. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'O Khalid, do not harm a man of the people of Badr. Even if you spent the like of Uhud in gold, you would not attain his action.' Khalid said, 'They fall upon me and I reply to them.' The Prophet said, 'Do not harm Khalid, for he is a sword among the swords of Allah which Allah has poured upon the disbelievers.'"],[581,"Whoever grants respite to a debtor in difficulty or waives his debt, Allah will shade him in His shade on a day when there is no shade except His shade."],[582,"Concerning a woman who has a husband, possesses wealth, and her husband does not permit her to perform Hajj, he said, 'She may not set out except with her husband's permission.'"],[583,"For Marwah: this is the place of sacrifice, and all the ravines and roads of Makkah are places of sacrifice in the Umrah."],[584,"Whoever gives a man assurance of safety for his blood and then kills him, I am innocent of the killer, even if the one killed is a disbeliever."],[585,"The likeness of a hypocrite is that of a sheep wandering between two flocks: when it goes to these, they butt it, and when it goes to those, they butt it."],[586,"Whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."],[587,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray on a khumrah (a small mat)."],[588,"Whatever blessing Allah bestows upon a servant—in wealth, family, or children—and he says, “What Allah wills; there is no power except with Allah,” he will not see any affliction in it other than death. And he recited: “And why did you not say, when you entered your garden: ‘What Allah wills; there is no power except with Allah’?”"],[589,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah, the people were giving advance payments for grain and dates. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever gives an advance payment, let him give it for a specified term and a known measure.”"],[590,"Do not revile the dead, for by doing so you hurt the living."],[591,"Allah will raise the scholars on the Day of Resurrection, then say: “O assembly of scholars, I did not place My knowledge in you while I wished to punish you. Go, for I have forgiven you.”"],[592,"On the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Prophet ﷺ entered wearing a black turban."],[593,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I used to bathe together from a single vessel—a brass basin—and he would say, “Leave some for me, leave some for me.”"],[594,"By Him in whose hand is my soul, killing a believer is greater in the sight of Allah on the Day of Resurrection than the passing away of the world."],[595,"The imam is responsible, and the mu’adhdhin is entrusted. O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the mu’adhdhins."],[596,"The key to Paradise is prayer, and the key to prayer is ablution."],[597,"The Prophet ﷺ heard a man say to another, “O shahan-shah (king of kings).” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah is the King of kings.”"],[598,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed them, saying: “How long will you refrain from mentioning the immoral person? Expose him so that people may beware of him.”"],[599,"Adorn your festivals with the takbir."],[600,"Allah spread out two servants of His servants, increasing for them wealth and children. He said to one of them, “O so-and-so.” He replied, “At Your service, my Lord, and gladly.” He said, “Did I not increase wealth and children for you?” He said, “Yes, my Lord.” He said, “Then how did you deal with what I gave you?” He said, “I left it for my children, fearing poverty for them.” He said, “Indeed, if you knew true knowledge, you would have laughed little and wept much. Indeed, what you feared for them I have already brought down upon them.” And He says to the other, “O so-and-so, son of so-and-so.” He replies, “At Your service, my Lord, and gladly.” He says, “Did I not increase wealth and children for you?” He says, “Yes, my Lord.” He says, “Then how did you deal with what I gave you?” He says, “I spent it in obedience to You, and I entrusted my children after me to Your beautiful justice.” He says, “Indeed, if you knew true knowledge, you would have laughed much and wept little. Indeed, what you entrusted for them I have already brought down upon them.”"],[601,"No one should narrate stories to the people except a ruler, one commanded, or a hypocrite showing off."],[602,"The Aws and the Khazraj were two tribes of the Ansar, and between them in the pre-Islamic era there was enmity. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to them, that ceased, and Allah brought harmony between them. While they were sitting in a gathering of theirs, a man from the Aws recited a line of poetry containing satire against the Khazraj, and a man from the Khazraj recited a line of poetry containing satire against the Aws. They kept on, this one reciting a line and that one reciting a line, until some of them jumped at others and took up their weapons and set out to fight. That reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and revelation had come down to him. He came hurriedly, having uncovered his shins. When he saw them, he called to them: “O you who believe, fear Allah as He should be feared and do not die except as Muslims” until he finished the verses. They threw away their weapons and embraced one another, weeping."],[603,"I performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ once, and I prayed the dawn prayer with him at Mina. When he finished his prayer, there were two men behind the people who had not prayed with the people. He said, “Bring me the two men.” They were brought trembling in their quivering muscles. He said, “Did you not pray with us?” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, we had prayed in our camps and thought we would not catch the prayer.” He said, “Do not do that. If you pray in your camps and then catch the prayer, pray it, and it will be a supererogatory prayer for you.” One of them said, “Ask forgiveness for me, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “O Allah, forgive him.” Then the people crowded around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I was then among the most vigorous and strongest of men. I pushed through the people until I took hold of the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and placed it on my chest. I never felt anything colder or more pleasant than the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[604,"There will be rulers over you who delay the prayer. So pray the prayer at its proper time, and make your prayer with them a supererogatory prayer."],[605,"The most perfect of people in faith are those with the best character, who are easygoing and approachable, who befriend and are befriended. There is no good in one who does not befriend and is not befriended."],[606,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man praying alone in the mosque after the prayer had been performed, and said, “Is there no man who will give charity to this one and pray with him?”"],[607,"We saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over his leather socks."],[608,"The Prophet ﷺ recited: “Then joy and rest and a garden of delight” (as “farawhun wa rayhan”)."],[609,"Whoever goes out with a funeral until it is buried will have two qirats of reward. It was said, “Like what is a qirat?” He said, “Like Mount Uhud.”"],[610,"I did not pray behind your Prophet ﷺ except that I heard him when he finished saying: “O Allah, forgive me all my errors and sins. O Allah, revive me, mend me, and guide me to righteous deeds and character, for none guides to the righteous of them and none turns away their evil except You.”"],[611,"If one of you were to flee from his provision, it would overtake him just as death overtakes him."],[612,"The Prophet ﷺ turned to the people and said: O people, whoever of you is afflicted by a calamity after me, let him seek consolation in his calamity through me from the calamity that befalls him, for no one of my Ummah after me will be afflicted with the like of the calamity of losing me."],[613,"Travel is a piece of torment, preventing one of you from his sleep, food, drink, and pleasure. So when one of you finishes his business, let him hasten to his family."],[614,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: May a fasting person kiss? He said: And what harm is there in that? It is a fragrant herb that he smells."],[615,"Indeed, the Magians of this Ummah are the deniers of the decrees of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. If they fall ill, do not visit them; if you meet them, do not greet them; if they die, do not attend their funerals."],[616,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived, circumambulated the House, prayed two rak'ahs behind the Station of Ibrahim, and walked between al-Safa and al-Marwah. And indeed in the Messenger of Allah you have an excellent example."],[617,"The Prophet ﷺ recited: 'farawhun wa rayhan' (then rest and fragrant herb)."],[618,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to us in the land of Juhaynah: Do not make use of any part of a dead animal, neither its hide nor its sinews."],[619,"Regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: 'Their mark is on their faces from the trace of prostration,' he said: 'The light on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[620,"The Prophet ﷺ would not rise from his gathering until he said: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise. I ask Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance.' Then he would say: 'Indeed, it is an expiation for what occurs in the gathering.'"],[621,"He forbade fasting on three days: the day of doubt before seeing the moon, the day of Adha, and the day of Fitr."],[622,"Modesty and faith are paired together; they are never separated except together."],[623,"I gave glad tidings to Bilal, and he said to me: O 'Abdullah, with what do you give me glad tidings? I said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Bilal will come on the Day of Resurrection upon a riding camel whose saddle is of gold and whose reins are of pearls and rubies, with him a banner, followed by the mu'adhdhins, and he will admit them into Paradise, such that he will even admit one who called the adhan for forty mornings, seeking thereby the Face of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."],[624,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"O Ibn Mas'ud, which of the bonds of faith is most firm?\" I said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"The firmest bond of Islam is: allegiance for the sake of Allah, love for the sake of Allah, and hatred for the sake of Allah.\" Then he said: \"O Ibn Mas'ud.\" I said: \"At your service, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Do you know which of the people is most virtuous?\" I said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"The most virtuous of people are the best of them in deeds when they have understanding in their religion.\" Then he said: \"O Ibn Mas'ud.\" I said: \"At your service, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Do you know which of the people is most knowledgeable?\" I said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"The most knowledgeable of people are those most discerning of the truth when people differ, even if he is deficient in his deeds, even if he crawls on his rear. Those before you split into seventy-two sects; three of them were saved, and the rest perished. One sect confronted the kings and fought them for their religion and the religion of 'Isa b. Maryam ﷺ ; they were seized, killed, and sawn apart with saws. Another sect did not have the strength to oppose the kings nor to stay among them calling them to the religion of Allah and the religion of 'Isa b. Maryam, so they wandered through the lands and became monks. They are the ones about whom Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: 'And monasticism they invented; We did not prescribe it for them, except seeking the pleasure of Allah' (57:27).\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever believes in me, follows me, and affirms me has observed it as it should be observed. And whoever does not follow me, those are the ones who perish.\""],[625,"O Ka'b, may Allah protect you from rulers who will come after me. I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is that?\" He said: \"Whoever enters upon them, believes their lies, and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me and I am not of him, and he will never come to me at the Pond. Whoever does not enter upon them, does not believe their lies, and does not help them in their wrongdoing, he is of me and I am of him, and he will come to me at the Pond. No flesh that grows from unlawful sustenance will enter Paradise, and every flesh that grows from unlawful sustenance, the Fire is more fitting for it. People go out in the morning in two ways: one sells himself and destroys it, and one ransoms himself and sets it free. Prayer is a proof, fasting is a shield, and charity extinguishes sin as water extinguishes fire.\""],[626,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, whom should I treat with the best companionship?\" He said: \"Your mother.\" I said: \"Then whom?\" He said: \"Your mother.\" I said: \"Then whom?\" He said: \"Your mother.\" I said: \"Then whom?\" He said: \"Your father, then the nearest relative, then the nearest.\""],[627,"Whoever swears a false oath to seize thereby the property of a Muslim will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection while He is angry with him."],[628,"A woman is not married in addition to her maternal aunt, nor the maternal aunt in addition to her sister's daughter; a woman is not married in addition to her paternal aunt, nor the paternal aunt in addition to her brother's daughter; not the younger in addition to the older, nor the older in addition to the younger.\""],[629,"Rabi'ah came to the Prophet ﷺ asking his permission to depart with the first group of travelers. Jibril ﷺ came to him and said: \"O Muhammad, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sends you greetings of peace and says to you: Tell Rabi'ah not to depart with the first group, for I will surely reduce the number of a beloved one.\""],[630,"The Prophet ﷺ heard a man saying: \"Labbayk on behalf of Shubrumah.\" He said: \"Have you performed Hajj for yourself?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"Perform Hajj for yourself, then perform Hajj on behalf of Shubrumah.\""],[631,"When you are present with the deceased, say good, for the angels say 'Amin.' I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what should we say?\" He said: \"Say: O Allah, forgive us and him, have mercy on him, and grant me a good successor after him.\" She said: \"So Allah granted me Muhammad ﷺ as a successor after him.\""],[632,"All of my community is pardoned except those who commit sins openly. It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, who are those who commit sins openly?\" He said: \"A man who does a deed at night and his Lord conceals it, then in the morning he says: 'O so-and-so, last night I did such and such,' thus uncovering Allah's covering over him.\""],[633,"We were eating with the Prophet ﷺ, and we heard the food glorifying Allah."],[634,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to a piece of land in Madinah called Bathan. He said: \"O Anas, pour water for me for ablution.\" I poured water for him. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had relieved himself, he came to the vessel, and a cat had come and lapped from it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ paused for it until the cat had finished drinking, then he performed ablution. I mentioned the matter of the cat to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"O Anas, the cat is part of the household goods; it will never make anything dirty or impure.\""],[635,"Whoever Allah has given a handsome face, a good name, and placed him in a position that is not shameful, he is among the chosen ones of Allah from His creation.\" And Ibn 'Abbas said: \"The poet said: 'Where is the Prophet's condition when he once said: Seek good in those with beautiful faces.'\""],[636,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded a caller on a rainy day to say: Pray in your dwellings."],[637,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not cease reciting the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-'Aqabah."],[638,"When the Prophet ﷺ prayed, he would spread out his left (foot) and stand upright on his right."],[639,"For every joint of the son of Adam, charity is due each day; and the two rak'ahs of Duha suffice for all of that."],[640,"When a man enters Paradise, he will ask about his parents, his wife, and his children. It will be said to him: They have not reached your rank and your deeds. He will say: O Lord, I have worked for myself and for them. Then he will be commanded to join them. Ibn 'Abbas recited: 'And those who believed and their descendants followed them in faith.'"],[641,"We entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on Friday, and before him was food from which he was eating. He said: Come closer and eat from this food. We said: We are fasting, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Did you fast yesterday? We said: No. He said: Do you intend to fast tomorrow? We said: No. He said: Come closer and eat from this food, for Friday is not to be fasted alone."],[642,"When the Day of Resurrection comes, Allah will command a caller to announce: Indeed, I have established a lineage and you have established a lineage. I have made the noblest among you the most righteous, but you insisted on saying: So-and-so son of so-and-so is better than so-and-so son of so-and-so. Today I raise My lineage and lower your lineage. Where are the righteous?"],[643,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in a prayer in which he recited aloud, then turned to us and said: Do I see you reciting with your imam? We said: Yes, O Prophet of Allah. He said: Indeed, I say: Why am I disputed in the Qur'an? Do not do that. When the imam recites aloud, do not recite except the Opening of the Book (Umm al-Qur'an), for there is no prayer for one who does not recite the Opening of the Book."],[644,"It is near that the farthest outposts of the Muslims will be at Salah, and Salah is near Khaybar."],[645,"Whoever humbles himself before Me like this—and he gestured with the palm of his hand toward the ground—I will raise him like this—and he gestured with the palm of his hand toward the sky."],[646,"The delay of the wealthy in paying debts is oppression."],[647,"The Prophet ﷺ admonished against laughing at breaking wind, saying: Why does one of you laugh at what he himself does?"],[648,"There is no nation except that some of it is in the Fire and some of it is in Paradise, except my nation; all of it is in Paradise."],[649,"I have pardoned you concerning the zakat of horses and slaves."],[650,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me when we had finished the tawaf of the House: 'How did you do, O Abu Muhammad, regarding touching the corner?' I said, 'I touched it and left it.' He said, 'You have done correctly.'"],[651,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution three times, three times."],[652,"I saw on the Messenger of Allah ﷺ two yellow garments."],[653,"A man should not lie skin to skin with a man, nor a woman with a woman."],[654,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us, commanding us to give charity, and forbidding us from mutilation."],[655,"A Jew had a debt of four dirhams owed by me, and he pressed me for it, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was about to set out for Khaybar. I asked him to wait until I returned, saying, 'Perhaps we will gain some spoils.' He brought me before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said, 'Give him his due,' twice. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you are about to set out for Khaybar, and perhaps Allah will grant us spoils there.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Give him his due.' The Prophet ﷺ, when he said something three times, would not be argued with. I had a waist wrapper on me, and on my head was a turban. When I went out, I said, 'Buy this waist wrapper from me,' and he bought it for the dirhams that he was owed from me. I then wrapped myself with the turban that was on my head. A woman passed by with a cloak, and she clothed me with it."],[656,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he set out before the sun declined, would delay Zuhr until he prayed it with Asr; when he set out after the sun declined, he would bring Asr forward until he prayed them together. When he set out before sunset, he would delay Maghrib until he prayed them together; when he set out after sunset, he would pray it with Maghrib."],[657,"A man may utter a word pleasing to Allah without giving it much thought, and because of it he will be recorded among the people of Allah's pleasure until the Day of Resurrection; and a man may utter a word incurring Allah's wrath without giving it much thought, and because of it he will be recorded among the people of Allah's wrath until the Day of Resurrection."],[658,"There is no zakat on what is less than five uqiyas (of silver); no zakat on less than five camels; and no zakat on less than five awsuq (of grain)."],[659,"Whoever reviles the prophets is to be killed, and whoever reviles the Companions is to be flogged."],[660,"Regarding the lost animal, he used to say: O Allah, who returns what is lost and guides out of error, You guide from error; return to me my lost property by Your might and authority, for it is from Your gift and favor."],[661,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ captured us on the day of Hunayn, the day of Hawāzin, and went to distribute the captives and flocks, I came to him and began to recite this poetry: Bestow upon us, O Messenger of Allah, generously, for you are the man we hope for and await. Bestow upon a remnant whom fate has hindered, their unity scattered by the vicissitudes of time. Time has left us wailing in grief, their hearts full of distress and affliction. If you do not reach them with blessings you spread, O most forbearing of people when tested. Bestow upon women whom you used to suckle, when your mouth was filled with streams from her milk. When you were a small child you used to suckle her, and what you do and leave adorns you. Do not make us like one whose ostrich has fled; preserve some of us, for we are a bright group. We are grateful for blessings even when they are disbelieved, and with us after this day there is something stored. Clothe with pardon those whom you used to suckle from your mothers; pardon is renowned. O best of those for whom dark horses pranced in battle when the sparks ignite. We hope for pardon from you that you will clothe this creation with when you pardon and prevail. Pardon, may Allah pardon what you fear on the Day of Resurrection when victory is brought to you. He said: When the Prophet ﷺ heard this poetry, he said ﷺ: What belonged to me and the sons of ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib is yours. And Quraysh said: What belonged to us is for Allah and His Messenger. And the Anṣār said: What belonged to us is for Allah and His Messenger."],[662,"I will certainly find some people from my community who will come on the Day of Resurrection with good deeds like the mountains of Tihāmah, and Allah will make them scattered dust. They said: O Messenger of Allah, describe them to us so that we do not become among them while we do not know. He said: Indeed, they are from your brothers, but they are people who, when they are alone with what Allah has forbidden, violate it."],[663,"The most severely punished of people on the Day of Resurrection is an unjust leader."],[664,"Whoever fasts Ramadan and six days of Shawwāl has fasted the whole time."],[665,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man praying alone in the mosque after the prayer had been offered, so he said: Is there not a man who will give charity to this one by praying with him?"],[666,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the people of the Aʿrāf, and he said: They are men who were killed in the path of Allah while they were disobedient to their fathers. Their martyrdom prevented them from entering the Fire, and their disobedience prevented them from entering Paradise. They will be on a wall between Paradise and the Fire until their flesh and fat waste away, until Allah finishes the reckoning of creation. When Allah finishes the reckoning of His creation and no one remains but them, He will encompass them with His mercy and admit them to Paradise by His mercy."],[667,"Al-ʿAbbās b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I went to some people who were conversing, and when they saw me they fell silent, and that was only because they find me burdensome. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: They have done it. By the One in whose hand is my soul, none of them believes until he loves you for my sake. Do they hope to enter Paradise through my intercession while the sons of ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib do not hope [and the sons of ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib do not hope]?"],[668,"Any hide that has been tanned has become pure."],[669,"Every shepherd is responsible for his flock."],[670,"Whoever says when he hears the call to prayer: O Allah, by the right of this perfect call and the established prayer, grant Muhammad the means and the excellence, and raise him to the praiseworthy station which You have promised him, my intercession on the Day of Resurrection becomes lawful for him."],[671,"The last of the two matters from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was abandoning ablution from what fire has touched."],[672,"May Allah have mercy on a servant who is easy-going when he judges and easy-going when he demands repayment."],[673,"O Aishah, if modesty were a man, he would be a righteous man; and if obscenity were a man, he would be an evil man."],[674,"When one of you sees someone afflicted, let him say: 'Praise be to Allah who has favored me over you and over many of His servants with great favor.' If he says that, then he has shown gratitude for that blessing."],[675,"No one has ever earned anything like the virtue of knowledge that guides its possessor to guidance or turns him away from ruin; and a person's religion is not upright until his deeds are upright."],[676,"Before he died, the Prophet ﷺ used to say frequently: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I see that you frequently say: \"Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance.\"' He said: 'I have been commanded with a matter,' and he recited: 'When the victory of Allah and the conquest comes.'"],[677,"He used to dislike a man coming to his family at night (unexpectedly)."],[678,"Hamzah b. Amr al-Aslami said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I fast continuously and do not break my fast. Should I fast while traveling?' He said: 'If you wish, then fast; and if you wish, then break your fast.'"],[679,"The Prophet ﷺ named him Muta', and said to him: 'O Muta', go to your companions. Whoever enters under this banner of mine will be safe from punishment.'"],[680,"Two things are not permissible to withhold: water and fire."],[681,"He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have embraced Islam, so what should I supplicate with?' He said: 'Say: \"O Allah, I seek guidance from You for the most righteous of my affairs, and I seek refuge with You from the evil of my soul.\"'"],[682,"A servant continues to be truthful and strive for truthfulness until he is recorded with Allah as a truthful one. And a servant continues to lie and strive for lying until he is recorded with Allah as a liar."],[683,"The Prophet ﷺ ruled by an oath with a witness."],[684,"Regarding His words, Mighty and Majestic: [Your Lord has placed beneath you a sariyyan] (19:24), he said: a stream."],[685,"The Prophet ﷺ used to perform witr at the beginning of the night, its middle, and its end."],[686,"The Muslims used to exchange gifts during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ as a bond among them. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: If people were to embrace Islam, they would exchange gifts without need."],[687,"I missed the Prophet ﷺ, so I followed him to the graveyards. He said: Peace be upon you, abode of a believing people. You are our forerunners. Then he turned and saw me and said: Woe to her! If she could, she would have done it."],[688,"When Chosroes perishes, there will be no Chosroes after him, and when Caesar perishes, there will be no Caesar after him. By Him in Whose hand is my soul, their treasures will surely be spent in the path of God, Mighty and Majestic."],[689,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ recite: (And tall palm trees) with the letter ṣād."],[690,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ with his brother, whose belly had swollen. He said: O Messenger of God, my brother's belly has swollen, so I went to the physicians and they instructed me to cauterize him. Should I cauterize him? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Do not cauterize him; return him to his family. Then a camel passed by him and kicked his belly, and it subsided. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and he said: If you had brought him to the physicians, you would have said: The fire healed him."],[691,"He used to visit his wives with a single ghusl."],[692,"Woe to the rich from the poor on the Day of Resurrection. They will say: Our Lord, they wronged us regarding the rights You ordained for us upon them. He will say: By My might and My majesty, I will surely draw you near and distance them. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ recited: In their wealth is a known right for the beggar and the deprived."],[693,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed the Eid prayer at the prayer ground, screening himself with his spear."],[694,"He used to gesture during the prayer."],[695,"Among what the Prophet ﷺ supplicated on the evening of Arafah was: O Allah, You see my place, hear my words, and know my secret and my open conduct; nothing of my affair is hidden from You. I am the wretched, the poor, the one seeking help and protection, the fearful, the anxious, the one who confesses and acknowledges his sin. I ask You as a destitute person asks, and I beseech You as a lowly sinner beseeches, and I call upon You as a fearful, blind man calls, one whose neck is humbled before You, whose body is abased, and whose nose is rubbed in the dust. O Allah, do not make me wretched in my supplication to You, and be to me compassionate and merciful, O Best of those asked, and O Best of those who give."],[696,"My community will never be disgraced as long as they observe the month of Ramadan. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is their disgrace in neglecting the month of Ramadan? He said: Violating sacred prohibitions in it. Whoever commits fornication in it or drinks wine, Allah curses him and those in the heavens until the like of it from the following year. If he dies before reaching the next Ramadan, he has no good deed with Allah by which to guard against the Fire. So be mindful of the month of Ramadan, for good deeds are multiplied in it as they are not multiplied in other than it, and likewise evil deeds."],[697,"Whoever wears silk, and drinks from silver vessels, is not one of us. And whoever corrupts a wife against her husband or a slave against his masters is not one of us."],[698,"If Allah permitted the people of Paradise to trade, they would trade in cloth and perfume."],[699,"By Him in Whose hand is my soul, a man does not believe until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself."],[700,"I saw al-Sa'ib b. Yazid whose beard was white while his head was black. I said: O my master, why does your head not turn white? He said: My head will never turn white. That is because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by while I was a boy playing with other boys, and he greeted the boys, and I was among them. I returned the greeting to him from among the boys, so he called me and said to me: What is your name? I said: Al-Sa'ib b. Yazid, son of the nephew of al-Namir. He placed his hand on me and said: May Allah bless you. So the place where the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ touched will never turn white."],[701,"No Muslim is pricked by a thorn except that Allah writes for him ten good deeds, erases from him ten evil deeds, and raises him ten degrees by it."],[702,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the tashahhud: All greetings are for Allah, and all prayers and pure words. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger."],[703,"Gabriel said to me: O Muhammad, love whomever you wish, for you will part from him; and live as long as you wish, for you will die. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Gabriel gave me the shortest sermon."],[704,"Three things, whoever does not have them is not from me nor from Allah. It was said: What are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Forbearance by which the ignorance of an ignorant person is repelled, good character by which he lives among people, and piety that restrains him from disobeying Allah, Mighty and Majestic."],[705,"By Him in Whose hand is my soul, nothing has been joined to something better than knowledge joined to forbearance."],[706,"Indeed provision is not decreased by disobedience, nor is it increased by a good deed, and abandoning supplication is disobedience."],[707,"We used to witness fighting alongside the Messenger of God ﷺ, and when the sun declined, he said to us: 'Attack!' So we attacked."],[708,"We escorted one of the Prophet's wives in a bridal procession to the Prophet ﷺ. When we entered upon him, he brought out a wooden bowl of milk and drank from it, then handed it to his wife. She said: 'I do not desire it.' He said: 'Do not combine hunger with lying.' Then he handed the cup to me, and I began to pass the cup around my mouth, and I would not drink from it except so that my lips might touch the trace of his lips. Then we left him, upon him be peace, and his wife."],[709,"Whoever raises a young child until he says 'There is no god but God,' God, Mighty and Majestic, will not call him to account."],[710,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out and saw in the mosque a man who did not complete his bowing or his prostration. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The prayer of a man who does not complete the bowing and the prostration is not accepted.'"],[711,"It was said: 'O Messenger of God, which Islam is best?' He said: 'One from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.' It was said: 'Which emigration is best?' He said: 'To emigrate away from what your Lord dislikes.' It was said: 'Which jihad is best?' He said: 'One whose horse is hamstrung and his blood is shed.'"],[713,"I asked Anas b. Malik: 'How was the recitation of the Messenger of God ﷺ?' He said: 'When the Messenger of God ﷺ recited, he would prolong his voice.'"],[714,"Fasting in winter is the cold booty."],[715,"The lifetime gift ('umra) belongs to the heir."],[716,"Fasting on the day of 'Arafah is an expiation for two years: a past year and a coming year."],[717,"Indeed God created Paradise, and He created for it people along with their clans and tribes, and they are not increased nor decreased. A man said: 'O Messenger of God, what then is the point of action?' He said: 'Act, for every person is facilitated to that for which he was created.'"],[718,"'Ali is with the Quran and the Quran is with 'Ali; they will not separate until they come to me at the Basin."],[719,"Whoever disbelieves in a verse of the Quran has disbelieved."],[720,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade on the day of Khaybar the flesh of domestic donkeys."],[721,"The aqiqah is slaughtered on the seventh day, or the fourteenth, or the twenty-first."],[722,"This community will split into seventy-three sects, all of them in the Fire except one. They said: What is that sect? He said: That which I and my companions are upon today."],[723,"Indeed, Isa b. Maryam - there is no prophet [or messenger] between me and him, except that he is my successor in my community after me. He will kill the Dajjal, break the cross, abolish the jizyah, and war will lay down its burdens. Whoever among you meets him, let him convey peace to him."],[724,"Whoever wakes up grieving over the world wakes up angry with his Lord. Whoever wakes up complaining of a calamity that has befallen him is only complaining against Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Whoever humbles himself before a rich man to obtain some of what he possesses incurs the wrath of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, upon himself. And whoever is given the Quran and enters the Fire, Allah has distanced him."],[725,"He used to seek protection for al-Hasan and al-Husayn, saying: I seek protection for you both with the perfect words of Allah from every devil and poisonous creature, and from every evil eye."],[726,"Three things - whoever has them has tasted the flavor of faith: whoever has nothing dearer to him than Allah and His Messenger; whoever would prefer to be burned in the Fire rather than apostatize from his religion; and whoever loves for the sake of Allah and hates for the sake of Allah."],[727,"Let not the awe of people prevent any of you from speaking the truth when he sees it or hears it."],[728,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept one night, and they woke up after the sun had risen. He arose, mounted his riding camel, traveled a little, then dismounted, then ordered the muezzin, who called the adhan and the iqamah, and he prayed. A man was in a corner, so he said: What prevented you from praying? He said: I was in a state of major impurity, O Messenger of Allah, and we had no water. He said: Perform tayammum with clean earth, then pray, and when you come to water, then wash."],[729,"A judge should not judge between two parties while he is angry."],[730,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am old, blind, live far away, and have no guide. Is there any concession for me? He said: Do you hear the call? He said: Yes. He said: I find no concession for you."],[731,"Whoever dies while bearing witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah will enter Paradise."],[732,"The wives of the people of Paradise will sing to their husbands with the most beautiful voices anyone has ever heard. Among what they sing is: 'We are the good and beautiful ones, wives of a noble people, who look with joy in their eyes.' And among what they sing is: 'We are the eternal ones, so we do not die; we are the safe ones, so we do not fear; we are the residing ones, so we do not depart.'"],[733,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say after the Fajr prayer: 'O Allah, I ask You for good provision, beneficial knowledge, and accepted deeds.'"],[734,"The Prophet ﷺ mentioned the Dajjal and said: 'He will come from here – no, rather from here,' and he gestured toward the east."],[735,"Three things: whoever does them with trust in Allah and seeking reward, it is binding upon Allah to help him and bless him: whoever strives to free a slave with trust in Allah and seeking reward, it is binding upon Allah to help him and bless him; and whoever marries with trust in Allah and seeking reward, it is binding upon Allah to help him and bless him; and whoever revives dead land with trust in Allah and seeking reward, it is binding upon Allah to help him and bless him."],[736,"Whoever cheats us is not one of us, and deceit and treachery are in the Fire."],[737,"Regarding the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: 'You are only a warner, and for every people there is a guide' (Qur'an 13:7), the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The warner and the guide is a man from Banu Hashim.'"],[738,"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, if he witnesses a matter, let him speak the truth about it or remain silent."],[739,"The delight of my eye has been placed in prayer."],[740,"The injury caused by a beast of burden is without liability."],[741,"The people of good in this world are the people of good in the Hereafter, and the people of evil in this world are the people of evil in the Hereafter."],[742,"A man was admonishing his brother about modesty, so the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Leave him, for modesty is part of faith.'"],[743,"The weeping of the believer is from his heart, and the weeping of the hypocrite is from his head."],[744,"He came to 'A'ishah and asked permission to enter. She disliked giving him permission. When the Prophet ﷺ arrived, she said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Abu al-Qu'ays came to me and asked permission, and I refused to permit him.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Let your paternal uncle enter upon you.' Abu al-Qu'ays was the brother of 'A'ishah's wet nurse."],[745,"What an excellent young man Khuraym is, if only he would shorten his hair and raise his lower garment. Khuraym said: 'My hair has not gone past my ears, nor my lower garment past my heels, since the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that.'"],[746,"He used to pray while traveling on his riding beast, gesturing, and he made his prostration lower than his bowing."],[747,"Take the gift as long as it is a gift. When it becomes a bribe for the religion, then do not take it, and you will not abandon it; poverty and need prevent you. Indeed, the mill of Banu Maraḥ has turned, and Banu Maraḥ have been killed. Indeed, the mill of Islam is turning, so turn with the Book wherever it turns. Indeed, the Book and the authority will separate, so do not part with the Book. Indeed, there will be rulers who judge for you. If you obey them, they will lead you astray; and if you disobey them, they will kill you.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what should we do?' He said: 'As the companions of 'Isa b. Maryam did: they were sawn with saws and carried on wood. Death in obedience is better than life in disobedience to Allah, Mighty and Majestic.'"],[748,"The imam is a guarantor, and the mu'adhdhin is entrusted. O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the mu'adhdhins."],[749,"The Quraysh invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to give him wealth so that he would be the richest man in Makkah, and to marry him to whatever women he desired, and to follow in his footsteps. They said: 'This is yours from us, O Muhammad, and refrain from insulting our gods and do not mention them with evil. If you refuse, then we will impose upon you one single condition, and in it there is good for you.' He said: 'And what is it?' They said: 'Worship our god for a year – al-Lat and al-'Uzza – and we will worship your God for a year.' He said: 'Until I see what comes to me from my Lord.' Then revelation came from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, from the Preserved Tablet: Say: O disbelievers, I do not worship what you worship – the surah. And Allah, Exalted, revealed: Say: Do you order me to worship other than Allah, O ignorant ones? Rather, worship Allah, and be among the thankful."],[750,"I was walking with the Prophet ﷺ when he reached the rubbish dump of a people and urinated standing. He called me and said: 'Why did you move away from me?' So I came until I was at his heels. Then water was brought, and he performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks."],[751,"Allah has cursed wine, its pourer, its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its seller, its buyer, and the consumer of its price."],[752,"The Prophet ﷺ said to a man: 'Cleanse yourself and protect yourself.'"],[753,"'Uthman ؓ performed ablution three times, then said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution like this ablution of mine.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever performs ablution like my ablution, then prays two rak'ahs without speaking to himself in them except good, his previous sins will be forgiven.'"],[754,"Whoever guarantees for me what is between his jaws and his legs, I will guarantee for him Paradise."],[755,"The congregational 'Isha' prayer is equivalent to standing (in prayer) for a night, and the congregational Fajr prayer is equivalent to standing (in prayer) for a night."],[756,"My close friend ﷺ enjoined me that the blame of a blamer should not overtake me concerning Allah; and that I should look at one who is lower than me, and not look at one who is above me. He also enjoined me to love the poor and be close to them, to speak the truth even if it is bitter, to maintain ties of kinship even if it is severed, not to ask people for anything, and to say abundantly: 'La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah al-'Aliyy al-'Azim' (There is no might nor power except with Allah, the Most High, the Most Great), for it is one of the treasures of Paradise."],[757,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ two rak'ahs while traveling, and with Abu Bakr two rak'ahs, and with 'Umar two rak'ahs. Then the paths diverged with you. By Allah, I would love to have two acceptable rak'ahs rather than four rak'ahs (i.e., two rak'ahs of the Prophet's Sunnah are better than four of others)."],[758,"The feet of a servant will not move on the Day of Resurrection until he is asked about five things: about his life and how he spent it; about his youth and how he used it; about his wealth, where he earned it and how he spent it; and about what he did with the knowledge he had."],[759,"'Umar b. al-Khattab entered upon Salman al-Farisi, who threw him a cushion. He said: 'What is this, O Abu 'Abdullah?' Salman al-Farisi replied: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"No Muslim visits his Muslim brother and he throws him a cushion out of honor and respect for him except that Allah forgives him.\""],[760,"Indeed, this is a day which Allah has made a festival, so whoever attends the Friday prayer should perform ghusl, and if he has perfume, he should apply some of it, and you should use the siwak."],[761,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me: 'O 'Ali, shall I not teach you a supplication which, if you supplicate with it, you will be forgiven, even if you are already forgiven?' I said: 'Of course.' He said: 'La ilaha illa Allah al-'Aliyy al-'Azim (There is no god but Allah, the Most High, the Most Great); la ilaha illa Allah al-'Aliyy al-Karim (There is no god but Allah, the Most High, the Most Generous); la ilaha illa Allah Rabb al-'Arsh al-'Azim (There is no god but Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne).'"],[762,"I am the first of people to know the verse of hijab. When it was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'Do not enter upon women.' No day passed that was more difficult for me than that."],[763,"Indeed, Allah has overlooked for my Ummah mistakes, forgetfulness, and what they are compelled to do."],[764,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the minbar, and with him was al-Hasan b. 'Ali, ﷺ , and he said: 'This son of mine is a sayyid (chief), and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will reconcile through his hands between two great groups of Muslims.'"],[765,"He said to 'Ali, Fatimah, Hasan, and Husayn, peace be upon them: 'I am at war with those who wage war against you, and at peace with those who make peace with you.'"],[766,"While the Prophet ﷺ was on one of his journeys, he heard a caller saying: 'Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar.' He said: 'Upon the fitrah (natural disposition).' Then he said: 'Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah (I bear witness that there is no god but Allah).' He said: 'You have testified to the testimony of truth.' Then he said: 'Ashhadu anna Muhammadan Rasul Allah (I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah).' He said: 'He has come out of the Fire.' Then he said: 'Look, you will find him to be a shepherd of goats or a keeper of dogs.' The time for prayer came, so he called it, and they looked and found him to be a shepherd."],[767,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Hassan b. Thabit: Satirize the polytheists. O Allah, support him with the Holy Spirit."],[768,"Do not sell what you do not have."],[769,"How was the pace of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he departed from Arafat? He said: A brisk walk, and when he found an open space he urged his mount faster."],[770,"Five things: whoever comes with them along with faith in Allah will enter Paradise – whoever guards the five prayers with their ablution, bowing, and prostration; gives the zakat from his wealth with a willing heart; performs Hajj to the House if he is able to find a way; fasts Ramadan; and fulfills the trust."],[771,"The fortunate one is he who was fortunate in his mother's womb."],[772,"Ruqba and umra: their course is the course of inheritance."],[773,"O people, suspect your own opinions. For by Allah, we never took up the handles of our swords to face a matter that humbled us except that it led us easily to a matter we recognized – except this matter of yours, for it only increases in severity and confusion. I saw myself on the day of Abu Jandal, and if I could find helpers against the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I would have objected."],[774,"Allah made the five prayers obligatory upon the tongue of your Prophet ﷺ: four rak'ahs when resident, two rak'ahs when traveling, and one rak'ah in fear."],[775,"A woman said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother died and she owed a fast. He said: Fast on behalf of your mother."],[776,"When a Muslim servant falls ill or travels, the like of his deeds while resident and healthy is recorded for him."],[777,"Indeed I jest, but I say nothing but truth."],[778,"Prices became high during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so they said: O Messenger of Allah, set prices for us. He said: Indeed Allah is the One who sets prices, withholds, and expands. I hope to meet Allah, Mighty and Majestic, with none of you seeking recompense from me for an injustice regarding honor or wealth."],[779,"Woe to the heels from the Fire."],[780,"Islam is built upon five: testifying that there is no god but Allah, establishing the prayer, giving the zakat, pilgrimage to the House, and fasting Ramadan."],[781,"When one of you prays and removes his sandals, he should not harm anyone with them; let him place them between his legs."],[782,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a military expedition, and we awoke to find the Messenger of Allah ﷺ not present. We said, 'Let us look for him.' While we were doing so, we heard a sound like the rumbling of a millstone. We went toward the sound and found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you leave your bed while we are around you and do not wake any of us, even though we are in enemy territory?' He replied, 'A messenger came to me from my Lord and gave me the choice between half of my community entering Paradise or intercession, and I chose intercession.' Abu Musa said: 'I said, \"Supplicate Allah to make me among the people of intercession.\" He said, \"O Allah, make him among its people.\" Then another spoke, and another, and another. When they became many, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"My intercession is for whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.\""],[783,"Two should not converse privately to the exclusion of the third."],[784,"Be a scholar, or a student, or a listener, or a lover, and do not be the fifth, lest you perish.' Ata' b. Muslim said: Mis'ar said to me: 'You have added a fifth that we did not have.' He said: 'The fifth is that you hate knowledge and its people.'"],[785,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ missed anything from Ramadan, he would make it up during the first ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah."],[786,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and when we approached Madinah I wanted to hurry. He said: 'Wait until the woman whose husband is absent has shaved and the disheveled woman has combed her hair.'"],[787,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed Zuhr and Asr as five rak'ahs, and then performed the two prostrations of forgetfulness."],[788,"On the day of Khaybar, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out a man, but he showed cowardice. Then Muhammad b. Maslamah came and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have never seen the like of today.' Muhammad b. Maslamah wept. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do not wish to meet the enemy, and ask Allah for well-being; for you do not know what trials you may face from them. When you meet them, say: O Allah, You are our Lord and their Lord, and our forelocks are in Your hand; You alone slay them. Then remain seated on the ground. When they overwhelm you, rise up and say Allahu akbar.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Tomorrow I shall certainly send a man who loves Allah and His Messenger and whom they love, who will not turn his back.' On the morrow he sent Ali, who was suffering from severe ophthalmia. He said, 'Go forth.' Ali said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I cannot see where I place my feet.' He spat into his eyes, tied the banner for him, and handed him the standard. Ali asked, 'O Messenger of Allah, for what shall I fight?' He replied, 'So that they testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah. When they do that, they have protected their blood and wealth from me except by its right, and their reckoning is with Allah, Mighty and Majestic.'"],[789,"When the first fruit of the season was brought to him, he would receive it or place it on his eyes, then give it to the youngest child present."],[790,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ashajj of Abd al-Qays: 'You have two qualities that Allah loves: forbearance and deliberateness.'"],[791,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in a house crowded with people. He stood at the door, and the Prophet ﷺ looked right and left but did not see a place, so he took his cloak, folded it, and threw it to him, saying: “O Jarīr, sit on it.” Jarīr took it, hugged it, kissed it, and then returned it to the Prophet ﷺ, saying: “May God honor you, O Messenger of God, as you have honored me.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When a nobleman of a people comes to you, honor him.”"],[792,"Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr and my cousin."],[793,"It was said: “O Messenger of God, will we have intercourse with our wives in Paradise?” He said: “A man will indeed have intercourse with a hundred virgins in a single day.”"],[794,"The imam is a guarantor and the mu'adhdhin is entrusted. O God, guide the imams and forgive the mu'adhdhins."],[795,"We performed the Farewell Hajj with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and we continued to pray two rakʿahs until we returned."],[796,"When one of you takes off his sandals in prayer, he should not place them in front of him and sin because of them, nor behind him where his Muslim brother would sin because of them, but let him place them between his legs."],[797,"There is nothing between a servant and disbelief except abandoning prayer."],[798,"At the end of time there will be people who deny the divine decree. Indeed, they are the Magians of this nation. If they fall ill, do not visit them, and if they die, do not attend their funerals."],[799,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and saw him praying in a single garment, wrapping it around himself, and I ate with him. He said: “Mention God’s name, eat with your right hand, and eat from what is nearest to you.”"],[800,"The poor among the Muslims came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, the wealthy have taken the highest ranks. They pray as we pray, fast as we fast, and perform Hajj as we perform Hajj, and they have surplus wealth from which they give charity, while we have nothing to give.” He said: “Shall I not direct you to something that, if you do it, you will overtake those who preceded you and none after you will catch up with you except one who does the like of what you do? Glorify God thirty-three times after every prayer, praise Him thirty-three times, and magnify Him thirty-four times.” This reached the wealthy, and they said the same as the poor had said, then they came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him. He said: “That is God’s bounty; He gives it to whomever He wills.”"],[801,"He used to object to those who recited “It is not for a prophet to be dishonest (yaghulla),” and he would say: “How could it not be for him to be killed (yuqtala) when God the Exalted said: 'and they kill the prophets without right'? But the hypocrites accused the Prophet ﷺ of taking something from the spoils, so God, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: 'It is not for a prophet to be dishonest (yaghulla).'”"],[802,"ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib proposed to the daughter of Abū Jahl, and the Prophet ﷺ said: “If you marry her, then return our daughter to us.”"],[803,"I am the guarantor of a house in the outskirts of Paradise, a house in the middle of Paradise, and a house in the highest part of Paradise for the one who abandons quarreling even if he is in the right, abandons lying even in jest, and has good character."],[804,"The Prophet ﷺ said the takbir for them in the dawn prayer, then gestured to them, then left. He returned with his head dripping, then led them in prayer, and said: 'I am only a human being; I was in a state of major ritual impurity and forgot.'"],[805,"Trim the mustaches and let the beards grow."],[806,"The people of Paradise will enter Paradise hairless, beardless, fair-skinned, with kohl-lined eyes, aged thirty-three, and upon the form of Adam, sixty cubits tall and seven cubits broad."],[807,"Abandoning the bequest is a disgrace in this world and a fire and shame in the Hereafter."],[808,"Whoever Allah wishes good for, He gives him understanding in the religion."],[809,"A man said to Abu Hurayrah: 'You have given us legal verdicts about everything; soon you will give us a verdict even about excrement.' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever removes an annoyance from a path of the paths of the Muslims, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people.'"],[810,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'My father is an old man who is unable to perform the Hajj. Shall I perform it on his behalf?' He said: 'Yes, perform Hajj on behalf of your father.'"],[811,"There is no usury except in deferred payment."],[812,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never struck any of his wives, nor did he ever strike anything with his hand except when striving in the cause of Allah. Nothing was ever taken from him such that he sought revenge against the one who took it, unless one of Allah's sacred limits was violated, in which case he would exact retribution for Allah's sake."],[813,"If you are asked: 'Which of the two terms did Musa fulfill?' Say: 'The better, the more complete, and the more righteous of them.' And if you are asked: 'Which of the two women did he marry?' Say: 'The younger of them, and she is the one who came and said: O my father, hire him, for the best of those you hire is the strong and trustworthy. He said: What did you see of his strength? She said: He lifted a heavy stone and threw it off the well. He said: And what did you see of his trustworthiness? She said: He said: Walk behind me and do not walk in front of me.'"],[814,"Whoever spends the night with the smell of meat grease on his hand and something befalls him, let him blame none but himself."],[815,"He saw a man leaving the mosque when the caller to prayer had given the call, and he said: 'As for this one, he has disobeyed Abu al-Qasim ﷺ.'"],[816,"A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, which people are best?' He said: 'He whose life is long and whose deeds are good.' He said: 'And which people are worst?' He said: 'He whose life is long and whose deeds are evil.'"],[817,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoined me, saying: 'O Anas, perform ablution thoroughly and your lifespan will be increased. Greet with salam whomever you meet from my ummah and your good deeds will multiply. When you enter your house, greet your family. And pray the Duha prayer, for it is the prayer of the repentant. Show mercy to the young and honor the old, and you will be among my companions on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[818,"O son of Adam, as long as you call upon Me and hope in Me, I will forgive you for what is in you, and I do not mind. If you were to come to Me with an earthful of sins, I would meet you with an earthful of forgiveness, as long as you do not associate anything with Me. And if your sins were to reach the clouds of the sky, then you asked Me for forgiveness, I would forgive you."],[819,"Three people Allah will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection, nor purify them, and they will have a painful punishment: an old man who commits adultery, a poor person who is arrogant, and a man for whom Allah has provided goods, but he only sells by swearing and only buys by swearing."],[820,"Umm Salamah said to me: 'Is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ insulted among you in front of the people?' I said: 'Glory be to Allah! How could the Messenger of Allah ﷺ be insulted?' She said: 'Is not Ali b. Abi Talib insulted, and those who love him? I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to love him.'"],[821,"The scent of a child is from the scent of Paradise."],[822,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Ali: 'You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me.'"],[823,"The likeness of my Ahl al-Bayt among you is like the ark of Nuh: whoever boards it is saved, and whoever stays behind drowns. And the likeness of my Ahl al-Bayt among you is like the Gate of Hittah among the Children of Israel: whoever enters it is forgiven."],[824,"When a slave joins the land of war, his blood becomes lawful."],[825,"Whoever dies in one of the two Harams will be raised secure on the Day of Resurrection."],[826,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the people of Quba: 'I hear that Allah has praised you for purity. What is this purity?' They said: 'By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, we do not know anything except that our Jewish neighbors wash their private parts after defecation, so we washed as they washed.'"],[827,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not delay the Maghrib prayer for the 'Isha' prayer or for anything else."],[828,"A scorpion stung the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying. When he finished, he said: 'May Allah curse the scorpion; it does not leave alone one who is praying or anyone else.' Then he called for water and salt and began to wipe over the sting and recited: 'Say: O disbelievers', 'Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak', and 'Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.'"],[829,"A person is with whom he loves."],[830,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sought forgiveness for me twenty-five times. Each time I counted them with my hand. He would say: 'Have you settled your father's debt on his behalf?' I would say: 'Yes.' Then he would say: 'May Allah forgive you.'"],[831,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to the mirbad (open enclosure). He saw 'Uthman b. 'Affan leading a camel loaded with flour, clarified butter, and honey. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'Make it kneel.' So he made it kneel. Then he called for a cooking pot and put in it some of the clarified butter, honey, and flour. Then he ordered that a fire be lit under it until it was cooked. Then he said: 'Eat.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate from it. Then he said: 'This is something that the people of Persia call khabis.'"],[832,"The excellence of the congregational prayer over the prayer of an individual is twenty-seven degrees."],[833,"The most beloved of you to me are those with the best character, who are easy-going and accommodating, who build bonds of affection and are loved by others. And the most hated of you to me are those who spread malicious gossip, those who cause division between loved ones, and those who seek to find fault with the innocent."],[834,"Whoever equips a warrior (for the cause of Allah), or provides iftar to a fasting person, or equips a pilgrim, will have the like of that person's reward without any of his reward being diminished."],[835,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade any of us from praying with his hands on his hips."],[836,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed a man from the Ansar, known as Ibn al-Lutbiyyah, to collect zakah. When he returned, the Prophet ﷺ sent for him to settle his accounts. He said: 'This is for you, and this was given to me as a gift.' This reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: 'We appoint men from among you over what Allah has entrusted to us. When one of you returns, he says: \"This is for you, and this was given to me as a gift.\" Why does he not sit in the house of his father and mother and see whether he would be given gifts? Whoever among you does any work for us, let him bring us all of it, whether little or much. Let any of you beware of coming on the Day of Resurrection with a camel that he carries on his neck, bellowing, or a cow that lows, or a sheep that bleats.'"],[837,"Whoever says after every prayer: 'I seek forgiveness from Allah, besides whom there is no deity, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of existence, and I repent to Him' will be forgiven, even if he fled from the battlefield."],[838,"No servant begins the day fasting except that the gates of heaven are opened for him, his limbs glorify Allah for him, and the inhabitants of the lowest heaven seek forgiveness for him until the sun sets. If he prays one or two rak'ahs voluntarily, the heavens shine with light for him, and his wives from among the houris say: 'O Allah, take his soul to us, for we long to see him.' If he says 'la ilaha illallah', or glorifies Allah, or says 'Allahu akbar', angels receive those words and record them until the sun sets."],[839,"Every two parties to a sale have no sale between them until they separate, except the sale of choice."],[840,"I passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was praying, and I greeted him, and he gestured to me."],[841,"He used to shorten the prayer at al-'Aqiq."],[842,"A minor has a right of preemption until he reaches maturity; when he reaches maturity, if he wishes he may take it, and if he wishes he may leave it."],[843,"He taught him the tashahhud: All greetings, prayers, and good things are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger."],[844,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and there were few riding camels, so we discussed what would suffice us of riding camels. I said, 'A small herd that we would come to in the middle of the night and enjoy riding them.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The lost camel of a Muslim is the burning of the Fire.'"],[845,"When you find a stray animal, do not hide it or conceal it; if it is identified, return it, otherwise it is the wealth of Allah, which He gives to whom He wills."],[846,"Indeed in the night there is an hour in which no Muslim servant asks Allah for anything but He gives it to him, and that is throughout the entire night."],[847,"The example of the one who is lenient concerning the command of Allah and the one who upholds the rights of Allah is like the example of a people who boarded a ship. One of them found a place and said, 'O these people, your path and passage is over me, and I am going to bore a hole here to perform ablution from it, draw water from it, and relieve myself in it.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If they leave him, he will perish and cause them to perish, but if they seize his hand, he will be saved and they will be saved.'"],[848,"A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with her two sons and asked him, so he gave her three dates, one date for each of them. She gave each of them a date, and they ate them. Then they looked at their mother, so she split the date into two halves and gave each of them half a date. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'May Allah have mercy on her; by her mercy to her two sons, He will have mercy on her.'"],[849,"A woman must not travel for more than three nights except with a husband or a male relative within the prohibited degrees."],[850,"I bear witness to Allah that no intelligent person stumbles but He raises him, then he stumbles but He raises him, then he stumbles but He raises him, until he reaches Paradise."],[851,"A servant will tell a lie, and the angel will distance himself from him by a mile's distance due to the stench of what he has brought."],[852,"There is no concern except the concern of debt, and no pain except the pain of the eye."],[853,"Abu Hurayrah addressed us from the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Allah, the Exalted, will surely offer Adam three excuses on the Day of Resurrection. Allah, the Exalted, will say: 'O Adam, were it not that I have cursed the liars, and I hate lying and breaking promises, and I punish for it, I would have had mercy today on all your descendants due to the severity of the punishment I have prepared for them. But the word from Me has become binding: if My messengers are denied and My command is disobeyed, I will surely fill Hell with jinn and people all together.' And Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say: 'O Adam, know that I will not admit anyone of your offspring into the Fire, nor punish with the Fire except one whom I know by My knowledge that, were I to return him to the world, he would return to the worst of what he was doing and would not turn back or repent.' And Allah, the Exalted, will say: 'O Adam, I have appointed you as an arbiter between Me and your descendants. Stand by the Scale and look at what is raised to you of their deeds. Whoever's good outweighs his evil by the weight of a grain, his is Paradise, so that you may know that I do not admit any of them into the Fire except a wrongdoer.'"],[854,"O my son, keep my secret, and you will be a believer. I have never disclosed his secret to anyone, even if it were my mother. The wives of the Prophet ﷺ ask me to tell them his secret, but I do not tell them, and I will never tell anyone his secret. Then he said: O my son, perfect your ablution, and your lifespan will be increased, and your two guardian angels will love you. Then he said: O my son, if you are able not to spend a night except in a state of ablution, then do so, for whoever death comes to while he is in a state of ablution will be given martyrdom. Then he said: O my son, if you are able to keep praying without ceasing, then do so, for the angels will keep praying for you as long as you keep praying. Then he said: O my son, beware of turning around in prayer, for turning around in prayer is destruction. If it is unavoidable, then in voluntary prayer, not in the obligatory prayer. Then he said to me: O my son, when you bow, place your palms on your knees, spread your fingers apart, and raise your hands away from your sides. When you raise your head from bowing, let every limb return to its proper position, for Allah will not look on the Day of Resurrection at one who does not straighten his backbone in his bowing and prostration. Then he said: O my son, when you prostrate, do not peck as a rooster pecks, and do not sit as a dog sits, and do not spread your forearms as a beast of prey spreads them. Spread the tops of your feet on the ground, and place your buttocks on your heels, for that will be easier for you on the Day of Resurrection in your reckoning. Then he said: O my son, be thorough in washing from major ritual impurity, and you will come out of your bath with no sin and no error upon you. I said: May my father and mother be your ransom, what is thoroughness? He said: You wet the roots of your hair and cleanse the skin. Then he said to me: O my son, if you are able to make some of your prayers in your house, then do so, for it increases the good of your house. Then he said to me: O my son, when you enter upon your family, greet them with peace, and it will be a blessing upon you and upon your household. Then he said: O my son, when you leave your house, let not your gaze fall upon anyone of the people of the Qiblah except that you greet him with peace, and you will return with your good deeds increased. Then he said: O my son, if you are able to pass the evening and morning with no deceit in your heart toward anyone, then do so. Then he said to me: O my son, when you leave your family, let not your gaze fall upon anyone of the people of the Qiblah except that you think he has more merit than you. Then he said to me: O my son, if you preserve my advice, then let nothing be dearer to you than death. Then he said to me: O my son, that is from my Sunnah. Whoever revives my Sunnah has loved me, and whoever loves me will be with me in Paradise. - This is not reported from Anas in this complete form except with this chain. Muslim al-Ansari was alone in it, and he was trustworthy."],[855,"Jacob ﷺ had a brotherly friend. One day he said to him: 'O Jacob, what took away your sight? What bent your back?' He said: 'As for what took away my sight, it was weeping over Joseph. As for what bent my back, it was grief over my son Benjamin.' Then Gabriel ﷺ came to him and said: 'O Jacob, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sends you greetings of peace, and says to you: Are you not ashamed to complain of Me to other than Me?' Jacob said: 'I only complain of my anguish and grief to Allah.' Gabriel said: 'Allah knows best what you complain of, O Jacob.' Then Jacob ﷺ said: 'O Lord, will You not have mercy on an old man? You have taken away my sight and bent my back. Return to me my fragrant one, Joseph, that I may smell him one whiff before death. Then do with me, O Lord, what You will.' Then Gabriel ﷺ came to him and said: 'O Jacob, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sends you greetings of peace, and says to you: Rejoice, and let your heart be glad. By My might and majesty, even if they were dead, I would raise them up for you. Make food for the poor, for the dearest of My servants to Me are the poor. Do you know why I took away your sight and bent your back, and why Joseph's brothers did what they did to Joseph? Because you slaughtered a sheep, and a certain poor man came to you while fasting, and you did not feed him from it.' After that, whenever Jacob wanted to eat, he would order a caller to announce: 'Is there any poor person fasting? Let him break his fast with Jacob.'"],[856,"Blessed is he who saw me, and he who believed in me, and he who saw the one who saw me."],[857,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and we came to a place where there was garlic. Some of the Muslims got some of it and came to the prayer place. He said: Whoever eats of this plant should not approach our prayer place."],[858,"He saw a person afflicted with a trial and said: Perhaps you asked your Lord to hasten the trial for you? He said: Yes. He said: Why did you not ask your Lord for well-being and say: Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire."],[859,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, which of the people is dearest to Allah, and which of the deeds is dearest to Allah? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The dearest of people to Allah is the most beneficial of them to people. The dearest of deeds to Allah is joy that you bring to a Muslim, or you relieve him of a distress, or you pay off a debt for him, or you drive away hunger from him. And to walk with my brother to fulfill a need is dearer to me than to seclude myself in this mosque for a month in the Mosque of Madinah. Whoever restrains his anger, Allah will cover his faults. Whoever suppresses his rage, even if he could have given vent to it, Allah will fill his heart with hope on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever walks with his brother to fulfill a need until he establishes it for him, Allah will make his feet firm on the day when feet slip."],[860,"A camel and a cow are for seven people."],[861,"The astute is he who holds his soul to account and works for what comes after death. The incapable is he who lets his soul follow its whims and hopes from Allah."],[862,"The Prophet ﷺ faced the rising of the sun and said: From here the horn of Satan rises, from here are earthquakes, trials, and the clamorers, and hardness of hearts."],[863,"Would one of you be unable to recite a third of the Qur'an in a night?\" They said, \"O Messenger of God, who can manage a third of the Qur'an?\" He said, \"Would one of you be unable to recite 'Say: He is God, the One'?\""],[864,"Ibn 'Umar never sat in a gathering but that he spoke certain words in it, except that he was asked about them, so he said: \"The Prophet ﷺ used to supplicate with them: 'O God, forgive me what I have done and what I have delayed, what I have concealed and what I have made public, and what You know better than I. O God, provide me with such obedience to You as will come between me and disobedience to You, and provide me with such fear of You as will make me reach Your mercy, and provide me with such certainty as will make the misfortunes of this world easy for me, and bless my hearing and my sight, and make them both my heirs, and set my vengeance upon the one who wronged me, and help me against the one who is hostile to me, and do not make my affliction in my religion, and do not make this world my greatest concern or the limit of my knowledge.'\""],[865,"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw a man praying with his garment hanging down, so the Messenger of God ﷺ came near him and folded his garment over him."],[866,"I agreed with my Lord in three things. I said, \"O Messenger of God, this is the Station of Abraham; if only we took it as a place of prayer,\" so God Most High revealed: \"And take the Station of Abraham as a place of prayer.\" And I said, \"O Messenger of God, if only you would veil your wives, for both the righteous and the wicked enter upon you,\" so God revealed the verse of the veil: \"And when you ask them for something, ask them from behind a veil.\" And I said concerning the captives of Badr, \"Strike their necks,\" but he consulted his companions, and they advised him to accept ransom, so God revealed: \"It is not for a prophet to have captives until he has made slaughter in the land,\" the verse."],[867,"There will come peoples at the end of time whose faces are the faces of humans, but whose hearts are the hearts of devils, like ravening wolves, with no mercy in their hearts. They shed blood and do not refrain from any indecency. If you enter into a transaction with them, they will cheat you; if you keep away from them, they will backbite you; if they speak to you, they will lie to you; if you entrust them with something, they will betray you. Their child is insolent, their youth is cunning, and their elder does not enjoin good or forbid evil. Taking pride in them is humiliation, and seeking what is in their hands is poverty. The forbearing among them is led astray, the one who enjoins good among them is accused, the believer among them is oppressed, and the sinner among them is honored. The Sunnah among them is an innovation, and innovation among them is the Sunnah. Then God will set their worst ones over them, and their best ones will supplicate but will not be answered.\""],[868,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was one of the most playful of people with a child."],[869,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: \"The one who serves water to the people is the last of them to drink.\""],[870,"The Prophet ﷺ performed the talbiyah from the mosque of Dhu al-Hulayfah."],[871,"The Muslims are on the verge of being besieged in Madinah until their farthest outpost is at Sal'."],[872,"Three things are true: God does not make one who has a share in Islam like one who has no share; God does not take charge of a servant and then entrust him to another; and a man does not love a people but that he will be gathered with them."],[873,"Take out of the Fire anyone who has a mustard seed's weight of faith in his heart.\" Then He says, \"By My might and My majesty, I will not make one who believed in Me for an hour of night or day like one who does not believe in Me.\""],[874,"Regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: \"And remember your Lord when you forget,\" he said: \"When you forget to make an exception, then make the exception when you remember.\" He said: \"This is specific to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and no one else may make an exception except in the continuation of an oath.\""],[875,"From the signs of the approach of the Hour is the swelling of the crescent moons, and that the crescent is seen for one night, then it is said: 'It is two nights old.'"],[876,"Whoever performs Hajj, let his last act at the House be circumambulation, except for menstruating women, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made a concession for them."],[877,"He forbade eating the meat of sacrificial animals after three days, and forbade nabidh in earthen jars, and forbade visiting graves. Then after that, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I had forbidden you from eating the meat of sacrificial animals after three days, so eat whatever you wish; and I forbade you from nabidh in jars, so drink, but every intoxicant is unlawful; and I forbade you from visiting graves, so visit them, but do not say what displeases Allah, Mighty and Majestic.'"],[878,"When I embraced Islam, I came to the Prophet ﷺ and he said to me: 'Bathe with water and lotus leaves, and shave off the hair of disbelief.'"],[879,"Visit graves, but do not speak obscenely."],[880,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to eat bread with dates, and he would say: 'This is the condiment of this.'"],[881,"Pardon the punishment of a person of virtue except in a prescribed punishment from the prescribed punishments of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."],[882,"From the excellence of a person's Islam is leaving what does not concern him."],[883,"Three people I will dispute with on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever I dispute with, I will overcome: a man who gave me a pledge then broke it—meaning the covenant of Allah—; a man who sold a free person and consumed his price; and a man who hired a worker and took full work from him, but did not pay him his wages."],[884,"The mouse is a metamorphosed creature, and the sign of that is that it drinks ewe's milk but does not drink camel's milk."],[885,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday: 'Alif Lam Mim. The revelation of the Book...' (Surat al-Sajdah) and 'Has there come upon man...' (Surat al-Insan)."],[886,"When he entered the lavatory, he would say: 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from male and female devils.'"],[887,"There are no days in which deeds are more virtuous than the ten days of Dhul-Hijjah. They said: Not even jihad in the path of Allah? He said: Not even jihad in the path of Allah, except for a man whose horse is hamstrung and his blood is shed."],[888,"When the verse 'And those who hoard gold and silver' was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Perish gold and silver. They said: O Messenger of Allah, so what wealth should we hoard? He said: A grateful heart, a remembering tongue, and a righteous wife."],[889,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn and circumcised them on the seventh day."],[890,"A little ostentation is polytheism. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, loves the pious, the hidden, the innocent, those who when they are absent are not missed, and when present are not recognized. Their hearts are lamps of guidance, they emerge from every dark, black tribulation."],[891,"The punishment of my ummah is in its worldly life."],[892,"Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfah, used to enter upon her, so she mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: Suckle him, and you will become forbidden to him."],[893,"There are no two Muslims for whom three children die before reaching puberty except that Allah will enter them into Paradise by the virtue of His mercy toward them."],[894,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ retired to his bed, he would say: O Allah, I seek refuge with You from evil, clinging, and from hunger, a bedfellow."],[895,"There is nothing more noble to Allah than the believer."],[896,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ with two small children of hers whom she was nursing. She asked the Prophet ﷺ for something to give her, but he found nothing to give her until he obtained three dates and gave them to her. She gave one date to this one and one date to this one, and kept one date. One of the two children cried, so she split the date into two halves and gave one half to this one and the other half to this one. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Bearing, giving birth, nursing, merciful to their children. Were it not for what they bring to their husbands, their praying women would enter Paradise."],[897,"Whoever sends one blessing upon me, Allah sends ten blessings upon him. Whoever sends ten blessings upon me, Allah sends one hundred blessings upon him. Whoever sends one hundred blessings upon me, Allah writes for him between his eyes a clearance from hypocrisy and a clearance from the Fire, and Allah will make him dwell on the Day of Resurrection with the martyrs."],[898,"I saw Ammar b. Yasir pray six rak'ahs after Maghrib. I said: O father, what is this prayer? He said: I saw my beloved, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, pray six rak'ahs after Maghrib and say: Whoever prays six rak'ahs after Maghrib, his sins are forgiven, even if they were like the foam of the sea."],[899,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to supplicate: O Allah, set right for me my religion, which You made the safeguard of my affair; and set right for me my worldly life, in which You placed my livelihood; and set right for me my Hereafter, to which You made my return; and make life an increase for me in every good, and death a relief for me from every evil."],[900,"Whoever does not believe in Allah's decree and does not believe in Allah's predestination, let him seek a god other than Allah."],[901,"A dream is not to be interpreted except to a scholar or a sincere advisor."],[902,"Beware of sins regarded as trivial, for the likeness of sins regarded as trivial is that of a people who camped in the bottom of a valley, and one brought a stick and another brought a stick until they gathered what they used to cook their bread. Indeed, when the one who commits sins regarded as trivial is taken to account for them, they will destroy him."],[903,"When dinner is served and the prayer is called, begin with dinner."],[904,"I saw 'Ali b. Abi Talib on the pulpit of Kufa saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The fornicator does not commit fornication while he is a believer, nor does the thief steal while he is a believer, nor does a man plunder a plunder at which people raise their eyes while he is a believer, nor does a man drink wine while he is a believer. A man said: O Commander of the Faithful, whoever commits fornication has disbelieved? 'Ali said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us to leave the hadiths of concessions ambiguous. He does not commit fornication while he is a believer that that fornication is lawful for him; if he believes it is lawful, he has disbelieved. Nor does he steal while he is a believer in that theft that it is lawful for him; if he believes it is lawful, he has disbelieved. Nor does he drink wine when he drinks it while he is a believer that it is lawful for him; if he drinks it while he is a believer that it is lawful for him, he has disbelieved. Nor does he plunder a plunder of high value when he plunders it while he is a believer that it is lawful for him; if he plunders it while he is a believer that it is lawful for him, he has disbelieved."],[905,"Whoever does not concern himself with the affairs of the Muslims is not one of them, and whoever does not begin his day and end it sincerely advising Allah, His Messenger, His Book, his leader, and the common Muslims is not one of them."],[906,"There is nothing more obedient to Allah than the son of Adam."],[907,"'Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, I was informed from Ibn al-Ashja'i, from his father, from Sufyan with his chain - the like of it."],[908,"Whoever brings joy into the household of a Muslim family, Allah will not be satisfied with any reward for him less than Paradise."],[909,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited this verse: 'Fear Allah as He should be feared, and do not die except as Muslims.' Then he said: If a drop of zaqqum were to fall into the seas of this world, it would spoil the livelihoods of the people of this world. How then will it be for the one whose food it is?"],[910,"When the Prophet ﷺ broke his fast, he would say: In the name of Allah; O Allah, for You I fasted, and with Your provision I broke my fast."],[911,"Fasting three days of every month is fasting for a lifetime: the white days, the thirteenth, fourteenth, and fifteenth."],[912,"It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days."],[913,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the mosque waiting for the prayer when a man stood up and said, \"I have committed a sin!\" He turned away from him. When the Prophet ﷺ had finished the prayer, the man stood up and repeated what he had said, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Did you not pray this prayer with us and perform the ablution for it well?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Indeed, it is an expiation for your sin.\""],[914,"The Prophet ﷺ wrote to his governors about the rules of the sadaqat (alms)."],[915,"Each of you will be spoken to by his Lord with no interpreter between him and his Lord. He will look to his right and see what he has sent forth, and he will look to his left and see what he has sent forth, and he will look in front of him and behold the Fire. So shield yourselves from the Fire, even with half a date."],[916,"You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me."],[917,"There is no one of my community who is given authority over any affair of the Muslims [the people] and does not protect them as he protects himself and his family, except that he will not smell the fragrance of Paradise."],[918,"Allah does not accept prayer from a woman until she conceals her adornment, nor from a girl who has reached puberty until she wears a head covering."],[919,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, did you ever do anything of what the people of the Jahiliyyah did?' He said, 'No, but I was appointed to two engagements; as for one of them, sleep overcame me, and as for the other, the people's night talk kept me from it.'"],[920,"Every intoxicant is khamr, and every khamr is haram."],[921,"Coitus interruptus was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, \"There is no harm if you do not do it, for it is only divine decree.\""],[922,"Whoever tells a lie about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[923,"Man is only called insan because he was given a covenant, and he forgot."],[924,"By Him who took his soul ﷺ, he did not die until most of his prayer was performed sitting."],[925,"The Prophet ﷺ rode a donkey to Quba to inquire about the paternal aunt and maternal aunt, and Allah Almighty revealed that \"there is no inheritance for them.\""],[926,"A true righteous dream is one of seventy parts of prophethood."],[927,"People will be carried on the Day of Resurrection, and the two sides of the Sirat will cause them to fall into the Fire like moths falling into it. Then Allah will save by His mercy whom He wills. Then permission will be given to the angels, the prophets, and the martyrs, and they will intercede and their intercession will be accepted. And Allah will bring out everyone who had a mustard seed's weight of faith in his heart."],[928,"When one of you dies, his seat is shown to him morning and evening. If he is one of the people of Paradise, then from Paradise; and if he is one of the people of the Fire, then from the Fire. And it is said: This is your seat until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, resurrects you to it on the Day of Resurrection."],[929,"I almost resolved to command that the prayer be established, then look and whoever does not attend the mosque, burn his house down upon him."],[930,"When the call for the morning prayer was given, he would pray two light rak'ahs before the morning prayer."],[931,"Deeds at the time of turmoil and tribulation are like emigration to me."],[932,"A bubbling dish was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he raised his hand from it and said: O Allah, do not feed us fire. [Indeed Allah has not fed us fire.]"],[933,"One who withholds zakah will be in the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."],[934,"Among the honor my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, granted me is that I was born circumcised, and no one ever saw my private parts."],[935,"I entered Paradise, and I heard the sound of footsteps before me. I said, 'O Jibril, what is this sound of footsteps?' He said, 'Bilal is walking ahead of you.'"],[936,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and water became scarce. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for a vessel and placed his hand in it, and I saw water gushing from between the fingers of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[937,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution washing each part three times."],[938,"A man passed by the Prophet ﷺ, and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw his strength and energy and were impressed. They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, if only this were in the path of Allah!' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'If he is striving for his young children, then he is in the path of Allah. If he went out striving for elderly parents, then he is in the path of Allah. If he went out striving for himself to keep himself chaste, then he is in the path of Allah. If he went out striving for his family, then he is in the path of Allah. But if he went out striving for pride and hoarding, then he is in the path of falsehood.'"],[939,"Using a toothpick is a sunnah."],[940,"The purification of the vessel of any of you, when a dog has lapped in it, is to wash it seven times."],[941,"Two ravenous wolves that spend the night in a pen containing sheep, tearing and eating, are not faster to ruin them than the pursuit of wealth and status is to ruin the religion of a Muslim."],[942,"Ma'add b. 'Adnan b. Udd b. Udad b. Zayd b. Bara' b. A'raq al-Thara.\" He said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The people of 'Ad and Thamud and the Companions of al-Rass, and many generations between that, none knows them but Allah.' Umm Salamah used to say: 'Ma'add is Ma'add, 'Adnan is 'Adnan, Udd is Udad, Zayd is Zand Humaysa', Bara' is Nabt, and A'raq al-Thara is Isma'il b. Ibrahim ﷺ ."],[943,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, my father has taken my wealth!' The Prophet ﷺ said to the man, 'Go and bring me your father.' Then Jibril ﷺ descended upon the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'Allah sends you greetings of peace and says: When the old man comes to you, ask him about something he said in his heart, which his two ears did not hear.' When the old man came, the Prophet ﷺ said to him, 'What is the matter with your son complaining about you? Do you want to take his wealth?' He said, 'Ask him, O Messenger of Allah, whether I spent it except on his paternal aunts or maternal aunts or on myself.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Enough! Leave this aside!'"],[944,"Did you not know that the forbearing man was about to be a prophet! Then he turned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'By al-Lat and al-'Uzza, I will not believe in you!' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had said to him, 'O Bedouin, what made you say what you said? You spoke untruth and did not honour my gathering.' He said, 'And you speak to me belittling the Messenger of Allah. By al-Lat and al-'Uzza, I will not believe in you unless this lizard believes in you!' He took out a lizard from his sleeve and threw it before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'If this lizard believes in you, I will believe in you!' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'O lizard!' The lizard spoke in clear Arabic that all the people understood: 'At your service and at your pleasure, O Messenger of the Lord of the worlds!' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to it, 'Whom do you worship?' It said, 'The One whose Throne is in the heaven, whose authority is in the earth, whose path is in the sea, whose mercy is in Paradise, and whose punishment is in the Fire.' He said, 'Who am I, O lizard?' It said, 'You are the Messenger of the Lord of the worlds and the Seal of the Prophets. He who believes in you has succeeded, and he who denies you has failed.' The Bedouin said, 'I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that you are truly the Messenger of Allah! By Allah, I came to you while there was no one on the face of the earth more hateful to me than you, and by Allah, at this moment you are dearer to me than myself and my child. My hair, my skin, my inner self, my secret and my open self have all believed in you!' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Praise be to Allah who has guided you to this religion, which rises and is not risen above. Allah does not accept it except with prayer, and He does not accept prayer except with Qur'an.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught him al-hamdu lillah and Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad. He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I have never heard in simple speech or poetry anything more beautiful than this!' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, 'This is the speech of the Lord of the worlds, and it is not poetry. If you recite Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad once, it is as if you have recited a third of the Qur'an. If you recite it twice, it is as if you have recited two thirds of the Qur'an. If you recite it three times, it is as if you have recited the entire Qur'an.' The Bedouin said, 'What an excellent god our God is; He accepts the easy and gives greatly!' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Give to the Bedouin!' So they gave him until they made him overwhelmed. 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf stood up and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I wish to give him a she-camel to draw near to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, one that is less than a Bukhti camel but above an ordinary Bedouin camel, and it is pregnant.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'You have described what you will give. Shall I describe for you what Allah will give you in return?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'You will have a she-camel of pearl, hollow, its legs of green chrysolite, its neck of yellow chrysolite, upon it a howdah, and on the howdah fine silk and brocade. It will pass with you over the Sirat like a flash of lightning.' The Bedouin left from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and met a thousand Bedouins on a thousand mounts with a thousand spears and a thousand swords. He said to them, 'Where are you heading?' They said, 'We are going to fight this one who lies and claims to be a prophet!' The Bedouin said, 'I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah!' They said, 'Have you apostatized?' He said, 'I have not apostatized!' He told them this account, and they all said, 'There is no god but Allah, Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah!' This reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he met them wrapped in a cloak. They dismounted on their knees, kissing what they had turned away from, and saying, 'There is no god but Allah, Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah!' They said, 'Command us with your command, O Messenger of Allah!' He said, 'Enter under the banner of Khalid b. al-Walid.' He said: 'There is no group from the Arabs, a thousand all together, who believed except the Banu Sulaym.' - None narrated it from Dawud b. Abi Hind with this full text except Kahmas, and none from Kahmas except Mu'tamir. Muhammad b. 'Abd al-A'la was alone in narrating it."],[945,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, advise me!” He said, “You must have fearful awareness of God, for it is the sum of all good! And you must strive in the path of God, for it is the monasticism of the Muslims! And you must remember God and recite His Book, for it is a light for you on earth and a remembrance for you in heaven! And restrain your tongue except from good, for then you will overcome Satan.”"],[946,"One day the Messenger of God ﷺ made a mark on the ground with a stick, then raised his head and said, “There is no soul that is born but that its place in Paradise and Hell has been written, and whether it is wretched or felicitous.” A man from the group said, “O Messenger of God, should we then abandon deeds?” He said, “No, but act, for everyone is facilitated. As for the people of felicity, they are facilitated toward felicity, and as for the people of wretchedness, they are facilitated toward wretchedness.” Then he recited: “As for him who gives and fears and affirms the best.”"],[947,"On the day of the conquest, the Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon Umm Hani’ bt. Abi Talib, and he was hungry. She said to him, “O Messenger of God, some in-laws of mine have sought refuge with me, and ‘Ali b. Abi Talib is not deterred by any critic’s reproach in the cause of God, and I fear that he will find out about them and kill them. So grant safety to whoever enters the house of Umm Hani’ until he hears the word of God!” So the Messenger of God ﷺ granted them safety and said, “We have granted protection to whomever Umm Hani’ has granted protection!” Then he said, “Do you have any food for us to eat?” She said, “I have nothing but dry pieces of bread, and I am embarrassed to offer them to you.” He said, “Bring them,” and he broke them into water, and she brought salt. He said, “Is there any condiment?” She said, “I have nothing but a little vinegar, O Messenger of God.” He said, “Bring it.” She poured it over his food, and he ate from it, then praised God, Mighty and Majestic, and said, “How excellent a condiment vinegar is! O Umm Hani’, no house that has vinegar will be devoid of sustenance.”"],[948,"There is no breastfeeding after weaning, and no orphanhood after puberty."],[949,"The Prophet ﷺ would not sleep until he recited “Alif Lam Mim. The sending down of the Book” (the prostration) and “Blessed is He in whose hand is the dominion.”"],[950,"The prayer of one sitting is half of the prayer of one standing."],[951,"Whoever visits the grave of his parents or one of them every Friday will be forgiven and recorded as dutiful."],[952,"We used to talk about how the Prophet ﷺ entrusted ‘Ali with seventy covenants that he did not entrust to anyone else."],[953,"A man cursed the wind in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Do not curse it, for it is commanded, and whoever curses something that does not deserve it, the curse returns upon him.”"],[954,"There is an angel in the heaven called Ishmael, over seventy thousand angels, each angel over seventy thousand angels."],[955,"Often I would scrape semen from the garment of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and then he would pray in it."],[956,"The Prophet ﷺ took al-Hasan and al-Husayn by the hand and said, “Whoever loves these two and their father and their mother will be with me in my rank on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[957,"He used to perform witr with: Sabbih isma Rabbika al-A'la (Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High), Qul ya ayyuha al-kafirun (Say: O disbelievers), and Qul huwa Allahu ahad (Say: He is Allah, the One)."],[958,"Whoever sleeps through his nightly portion (of Qur'an recitation), and then recites it between the forenoon and noon - it is as if he had recited it during the night."],[959,"Whoever fasts the Day of 'Arafah, it is an expiation for two years. And whoever fasts a day of Muharram, for each day there are thirty days (of reward)."],[960,"A servant does not attain the reality of faith until he guards his tongue."],[961,"Whoever is bestowed a blessing by Allah, let him increase in praising Allah. Whoever has many sins, let him seek Allah's forgiveness. Whoever's provision is delayed, let him increase in saying: 'There is no might nor power except with Allah.' Whoever stays with a people, he should not fast except with their permission. Whoever enters a people's home, let him sit where they tell him; for the people know best the private areas of their home."],[962,"Establishing a legal punishment on earth is better for its people than forty mornings of rain."],[963,"The Prophet ﷺ delayed the later 'Isha' prayer one night for a little while, then came out to us and said: 'What are you waiting for?' They said: 'The prayer.' He said: 'Indeed, you will continue to be in prayer as long as you wait for it.' Then he raised his gaze to the sky and said: 'The stars are a safeguard for the inhabitants of the sky, and when the stars depart, what they are promised will come to the inhabitants of the sky. I am a safeguard for my Companions, and when I depart, what my Companions are promised will come to them. My Companions are a safeguard for my Ummah, and when my Companions depart, what my Ummah is promised will come to it. Begin the prayer, O Bilal.'"],[964,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spent the night with her on her night. He got up to perform ablution for prayer, and she heard him saying during his ablution: 'Labbayk, Labbayk!' three times, and 'Nusirta, nusirta!' three times. When he came out, I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I heard you saying during your ablution: \"Labbayk, Labbayk\" three times, and \"Nusirta, nusirta\" three times, as if you were speaking to a person. Was there anyone with you?' He said: 'This is the poet of Banu Ka'b calling for my aid, claiming that Quraysh helped Banu Bakr against them.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out and ordered 'A'ishah to prepare his provisions, and not to inform anyone. She said: Abu Bakr entered upon her and said: 'O my daughter, what is this preparation?' She said: 'By Allah, I do not know.' He said: 'By Allah, this is not the time to raid Banu al-Asfar, so where does the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intend to go?' She said: 'By Allah, I have no knowledge.' She said: We stayed for three days, then he prayed the morning prayer with the people, and I heard the poet reciting: 'O Lord, I invoke Muhammad, the covenant of our father and his father, the ancient. We gave birth to you, and you were a son. Then we submitted and did not withdraw a hand. Indeed Quraysh broke their promise to you and violated your confirmed covenant. They claimed that you do not call anyone. So grant victory, may Allah guide you, a mighty victory. And call the servants of Allah, they will come as reinforcement. Among them the Messenger of Allah has come forth. If he is threatened with humiliation, his face darkens.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Labbayk, Labbayk!' three times, and 'Nusirta, nusirta' three times. Then the Prophet ﷺ went out. When he was at al-Rawha', he looked at a towering cloud and said: 'This cloud itself towers with the victory of Banu Ka'b.' A man from 'Adiyy b. 'Amr, the brother of Banu Ka'b b. 'Amr, stood up and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, and the victory of Banu 'Adiyy?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'May your chest be in the dust! Is 'Adiyy anything but Ka'b, and Ka'b anything but 'Adiyy?' That man was martyred on that journey. Then the Prophet ﷺ said: 'O Allah, conceal our news from them until we take them by surprise.' Then he went out until he camped at Marr. Abu Sufyan b. Harb, Hakim b. Hizam, and Budayl b. Warqa' went out that night until they overlooked Marr. Abu Sufyan looked at the fires and said: 'O Budayl, this is the fire of Banu Ka'b, your people!' He said: 'War has stirred them against you!' Muzaynah captured them that night, for they were the guards. They asked to be taken to al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib, so they were taken to him. Abu Sufyan asked him to seek protection for them from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He brought them until he entered upon the Prophet ﷺ, and asked him to grant protection to whomever he (al-'Abbas) protected. He said: 'I have protected whomever you protect, except Abu Sufyan!' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, do not restrict me!' He said: 'Whomever you protect, he is safe!' Then al-'Abbas brought them to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then he took them out. Abu Sufyan said: 'We intend to leave.' He said: 'Go forth in the morning.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up to perform ablution, and the Muslims rushed to his ablution water, sprinkling it on their faces. Abu Sufyan said: 'O Abu al-Fadl, your nephew's dominion has become great!' He said: 'It is not dominion, but prophethood, and in that they desire.'"],[965,"Were it not that you would become boastful, I would tell you of what Allah has promised on the tongue of His Prophet ﷺ for those who kill these people, meaning the Khawarij."],[966,"O Messenger of Allah, when we leave your presence, we engage in the talk of the Jahiliyyah! He said: 'When you sit in those gatherings in which you fear for yourselves, say upon your sitting: \"Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise. We bear witness that there is no god but You. We seek Your forgiveness and turn to You!\" Then what you have incurred therein will be expiated for you.'"],[967,"The woman with irregular bleeding performs a full bath from one menstrual period to the next."],[968,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ invoked blessing for three things: the pre-dawn meal, tharid, and the measuring (of grain)."],[969,"There will be in this ummah a sinking into the earth, a transformation of forms, and a casting of stones upon those who take singing girls, drink wine, and wear silk."],[970,"Whoever increases in remembrance of Allah has been absolved of hypocrisy."],[971,"Do not name grapes 'al-karm'; for indeed al-karm is the Muslim man."],[972,"Abu Bakr and Umar are the masters of the mature men of Paradise."],[973,"Regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: 'And beneath it was a treasure belonging to them' (18:82), he said: 'Gold and silver.'"],[974,"There will be trials, and your people will be brought to account! I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you command me? He said: 'Judge by the Book.'"],[975,"The witr is incumbent upon the people of the Qur'an."],[976,"He who seeks guidance through istikhara will not fail, he who consults others will not regret, and he who is frugal will not be impoverished."],[977,"We said: O Messenger of Allah, should we not enjoin good until we act upon it ourselves, and should we not forbid evil until we avoid all of it? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Rather enjoin good even if you do not act upon it, and forbid evil even if you do not avoid all of it.'"],[978,"Do not revile my Companions. For if one of you were to spend the like of Uhud in gold, he would not reach a mudd of one of them, nor even half of it."],[979,"Every intoxicant is unlawful."],[980,"He suffered from insomnia, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Shall I teach you words that if you say them you will sleep? Say: O Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and what they shade, Lord of the seven earths and what they carry, Lord of the devils and what they mislead — be a protector for me against the evil of all Your creation, lest any of them transgress against me or oppress. Mighty is Your protection, and there is no god but You.'"],[981,"There will be after me selfishness (or preferential treatment) and matters that you will disapprove of.” They said: “What do you command those who live to see that, O Messenger of God?” He said: “You fulfill the duty that is upon you, and you ask God for that which is yours.”"],[982,"He used to recite in the morning prayer on Friday: “Alif Lām Mīm, the revelation of the Book…” (Sūrat al-Sajdah) and “Has there come upon man…” (Sūrat al-Insān), and he did that consistently."],[983,"“Whoever leaves a hair on his body without washing it when performing the major ablution (ghusl) due to ritual impurity, such and such will be done to it in the Fire.” ʿAlī said: “For that reason I treated my hair as an enemy,” and he used to shave his hair."],[984,"The Prophet ﷺ used to straighten our shoulders in prayer."],[985,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ proclaim the talbiyah for both of them together: “Labbayka bi-ʿumrah wa-ḥajjah” (Here I am, O God, for an ʿumrah and a ḥajj)."],[986,"The Prophet ﷺ did not say the taslīm (salutation) in the two rakʿahs of the witr prayer."],[987,"O Messenger of God, the women of Banū Makhzūm have held mourning for al-Walīd b. al-Mughīrah. He gave her permission, and she said, weeping for him: “I weep for al-Walīd b. al-Walīd b. al-Mughīrah, I weep for al-Walīd b. al-Walīd, brother of the clan.”"],[988,"When Ādam ﷺ committed the sin that he committed, he raised his head toward the Throne and said: “I ask You by the right of Muḥammad, that You forgive me.” God revealed to him: “What is Muḥammad? Who is Muḥammad?” He said: “Blessed be Your name! When You created me, I raised my head toward Your Throne, and there was written on it: ‘There is no god but God; Muḥammad is the Messenger of God.’ So I knew that no one has greater standing with You than the one whose name You placed with Your name.” Then God, Mighty and Majestic, revealed to him: “O Ādam, he is the last of the prophets from your descendants, and his community is the last of the communities from your descendants. Were it not for him, O Ādam, I would not have created you.”"],[989,"This community will not come to an end until there emerge within it (from it) thirty lying deceivers (dajjāls), all of them claiming that he is the Messenger of God."],[990,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Ḥassān b. Thābit: “Satirize the polytheists, for God, Mighty and Majestic, supports you with the Holy Spirit.”"],[991,"When the prayer is called, and the evening meal is ready, then begin with the evening meal."],[992,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ feared a people, he said: “O God, we seek refuge in You from their evils, and we cast You against their throats.”"],[993,"I asked Ibn ʿUmar about the prayer while traveling, and he said: 'Two rakʿahs, sent down from heaven; if you wish, reject them.'"],[994,"He used to say when going to bed: 'O Allah, I seek refuge in Your noble countenance and Your perfect words from the evil of whatever You seize by the forelock. O Allah, You remove debt and sin. O Allah, Your army is not defeated, Your promise is not broken, and wealth does not avail the wealthy against You. Glory and praise be to You.'"],[995,"Showing teeth does not interrupt prayer, but laughing out loud does."],[996,"I fear for you three things, and they are coming: the slip of a scholar, the disputation of a hypocrite using the Quran, and worldly wealth that will be opened to you."],[997,"When ʿAli ﷺ killed the Kharijites on the day of al-Nahr, he said: 'Search for the mutilated one [the one with a defective limb].' They searched for him but did not find him; then they searched again and found him. He said: 'Were it not that you would become overjoyed, I would tell you what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, decreed on the tongue of His Prophet ﷺ for those who kill them.'"],[998,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when a Jew came to him and said: 'O Abu al-Qasim, what is the spirit?' Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: 'And they ask you about the spirit. Say: The spirit is from the command of my Lord.'"],[999,"A pilgrim in ihram was trampled by his mount and died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Wash him with water and sidr, shroud him in his two garments, do not apply perfume to him, and do not cover his head, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.'"],[1000,"It was said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Why did you not propose to the daughter of Hamzah?' He said: 'Hamzah is my brother through suckling.'"],[1001,"The Prophet ﷺ had four braids on his head."],[1002,"When he returned from a journey, he would begin with the mosque; he would pray two rakʿahs in it, then enter his home."],[1003,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ as the tenth of ten. A man from the Ansar stood up and said: 'O Prophet of Allah, who is the shrewdest and most resolute of people?' He said: 'Those who remember death the most and are best prepared for death before it descends. Those are the shrewd ones; they departed with the honor of this world and the nobility of the Hereafter.'"],[1004,"Mu'adh b. Jabal used to pray the last 'Isha' prayer with the Prophet ﷺ, then he would come to his people and lead them in that same prayer."],[1005,"Whoever persists in reciting Yasin every night, then dies – dies as a martyr."],[1006,"Be steadfast, and you will never be able to fully reckon it. And know that the best of your deeds is the prayer, and no one guards his ablution except a believer."],[1007,"Indeed Allah – Mighty and Majestic – revealed to me concerning 'Ali three things on the night I was taken on the Night Journey: that he is the master of the believers, the imam of the God-fearing, and the leader of the radiant-limbed ones."],[1008,"Do not artificially raise prices, do not hate one another, do not envy one another, do not turn your backs on one another, and be, O servants of Allah, brothers as Allah has commanded you."],[1009,"O 'Ali, with you on the Day of Resurrection will be a staff from the staffs of Paradise with which you will drive the hypocrites away from my basin."],[1010,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, is 'Umrah obligatory, its obligation like the obligation of Hajj? He said: \"And that you perform 'Umrah is better for you.\""],[1011,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to relieve himself and found no one to follow him. 'Umar b. al-Khattab became alarmed and brought him a purification vessel from behind him. He found the Prophet ﷺ prostrating in a drinking trough, so he withdrew from behind him until the Prophet ﷺ raised his head. He said: \"You have done well, O 'Umar, when you found me prostrating you withdrew from me. Indeed Jibril ﷺ came to me and said: Whoever from your community sends one blessing upon you, Allah will send ten blessings upon him and raise him ten degrees by it.\""],[1012,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to put his head into my room while he was in i'tikaf and I would comb his hair, and he would not enter his house except for human need."],[1013,"There will come upon you rulers who are worse in the sight of Allah than the Magians."],[1014,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I heard your supplication tonight, and what reached me from you was that you said: O Allah, forgive me my sin, and expand my dwelling for me, and bless me in what You have provided me. He said: \"Do you think they have left out anything?\""],[1015,"The best of you is the one who defends his clan as long as he does not commit sin."],[1016,"If one of you says when he is angry: 'I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed Satan,' his anger will leave him."],[1017,"Whoever is given four things is given four things, and the explanation of that is in the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: Whoever is given remembrance, Allah remembers him; for Allah, Exalted is He, says: 'So remember Me; I will remember you.' Whoever is given supplication is given response; for Allah, Exalted is He, says: 'Call upon Me; I will respond to you.' Whoever is given gratitude is given increase; for Allah, Exalted is He, says: 'If you are grateful, I will surely increase you.' And whoever is given seeking forgiveness is given forgiveness; for Allah, Exalted is He, says: 'Ask forgiveness of your Lord; indeed, He is ever Forgiving.'"],[1018,"Loyalty (wala') belongs to the one who sets free."],[1019,"I do not fear for my community a believer or a polytheist. As for the believer, his faith restrains him, and as for the polytheist, his disbelief suppresses him. But I fear for you a hypocrite with a knowledgeable tongue who says what you recognize and does what you disapprove of."],[1020,"A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have not left any need or want except that I have committed it.' He said: 'Do you not testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then this comes upon all of that.'"],[1021,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought a cheese during the expedition of Tabuk. He took a knife, cut it, and said: 'Eat in the name of Allah.'"],[1022,"I have a pool, and I am your predecessor at it."],[1023,"The Prophet ﷺ combined Zuhr and 'Asr, and Maghrib and 'Isha'."],[1024,"Whoever finds dates should break his fast on them, and whoever does not find any should break his fast on water, for water is purifying."],[1025,"He entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was standing in prayer, so he bowed (rak'ah) before the row, then walked to the row. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished, he said: 'May Allah increase you in eagerness, and do not do it again.'"],[1026,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks and the turban."],[1027,"A man from Banu Kilab came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and asked him about the stud fee of a stallion, and he forbade him. He said, 'O Messenger of God, we provide the stallion for mating and are rewarded with a gift.' So he granted him a concession regarding the gift."],[1028,"What is between the navel and the knee is 'awrah."],[1029,"Secret charity extinguishes the wrath of the Lord."],[1030,"You should eat the meat of the back, for it is among the best of it."],[1031,"None of you believes until he loves you for the sake of my love. Do they hope to enter Paradise through my intercession, while the Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib will not enter it?"],[1032,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by Abu 'A'ish Zayd b. al-Samit, one of the Banu Zurayq, who had sat down and said, 'O God, I ask You by the fact that praise is Yours, there is no god but You, O Benefactor, O Originator of the heavens and the earth, O Possessor of majesty and honor.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said to a group of his companions with him, 'Do you know what this man has supplicated with?' They said, 'God and His Messenger know best.' He said, 'He has supplicated by His greatest name, by which when He is called upon He answers, and when He is asked by it He gives.'"],[1033,"When the prayer is called and dinner is ready, begin with dinner."],[1034,"The image-makers will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to them, 'Bring to life what you have created.'"],[1035,"Supplication is worship. Then he recited: 'And your Lord said, Call upon Me, I will respond to you. Indeed, those who disdain My worship' – he said, meaning 'My supplication.'"],[1036,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to recite in the two 'Eid prayers and on Friday: 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High' and 'Has there come to you the report of the Overwhelming?'"],[1037,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, when he stood up at night, would cleanse his mouth with the tooth stick."],[1038,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Juhfah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and said: \"Do you not testify that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and that I am the Messenger of Allah, and that this Quran has come from Allah?\" We said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"This Quran has one end in the hand of Allah and the other end in your hands, so hold fast to it, for you will never be destroyed or go astray after it ever.\""],[1039,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ borrowed from a man a quantity of dates of a certain kind. When the man came to demand repayment, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"We have nothing today, so if you wish, give us more time until something comes to us and we can repay you.\" The man said: \"What treachery!\" Umar became angry, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Leave us, O Umar, for the one who has a right may speak. Go to Khawlah bt. Hakim al-Ansariyyah and seek some dates for us from her.\" He said: So they went, and she said: \"By Allah, I have nothing but dates stored as provision.\" They informed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"Take them and repay him.\" When they had repaid him, the man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said to him: \"Have you received full payment?\" He said: \"Yes, you have paid in full and been generous.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed the best of Allah's servants in the sight of Allah are those who fulfill and are generous.\""],[1040,"When one of you comes to a people while they are sitting, let him greet them with salam, and if a need arises for him and he wants to leave, let him greet them with salam, for the first is not more deserving than the last."],[1041,"Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us from Muhammad b. Abd al-Rahim, from Abu Asim, from Ajlan (H). And Hafs b. Umar al-Muqi narrated to us, Qabisah narrated to us from Sufyan, from Ibn Ajlan (H). And Muhammad b. Ali al-Marwazi al-Hafiz narrated to us, Khalaf b. Shadhan narrated to us, my father narrated to me from my grandfather, from Shubah, from Bakr b. Wail, from Ibn Ajlan (H). And Yahya b. Uthman b. Salih al-Misri narrated to us, Abdullah b. Salih narrated to us, al-Layth b. Sad narrated to me from Muhammad b. Ajlan (H). And al-Miqdam b. Dawud narrated to us, Asad b. Musa narrated to us, Said b. Salim al-Qaddah narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Ajlan. All of them said: From Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ - the like of it."],[1042,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us to Yemen, and he said: \"Go and cooperate with each other, and do not disagree; give glad tidings and do not drive people away; make things easy and do not make them difficult.\" Abu Musa returned and said: \"There are two drinks there: one is called mizr, made from wheat and barley, and the other is called bit, made from honey.\" He said: \"Every intoxicant that distracts from the remembrance of Allah and from prayer is forbidden.\""],[1043,"When I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, falling from the sky to the earth is dearer to me than lying about him. And I heard him ﷺ say: \"At the end of time there will emerge people young in age, foolish in intellect, who speak the best of the speech of creation, but their faith does not go beyond their throats. They will pass out of the religion as the arrow passes through the game. Wherever you find them, kill them, for there is reward in killing them for the one who kills them.\""],[1044,"A letter from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us: Do not make use of the hide or sinew of dead animals."],[1045,"M 1 (H) And Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us, Abu Mamar Ismail b. Ibrahim al-Qatii narrated to us, Abdullah b. Jafar al-Madini narrated to us from Ubayd Allah b. Umar, from al-Qasim b. Muhammad, from Aishah - similar to it, but he did not mention the poetry. No one narrated it from Ubayd Allah b. Umar except Abdullah b. Jafar. Abu Mamar was alone in narrating it."],[1046,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say: \"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the burden of debt and from the ruin of the unmarried.\""],[1047,"No vein twitches nor eye blinks except due to a sin, and what Allah averts is greater."],[1048,"Whoever steals a span of land or usurps it will come carrying it on the Day of Resurrection down to the lowest of the seven earths."],[1049,"Beware of consulting people, for it buries brilliance and exposes faults."],[1050,"The one who takes back his gift is like the one who returns to his vomit."],[1051,"O Abu Hurayrah, be content with what Allah has apportioned for you and you will be rich. Be scrupulous and you will be a servant of Allah. Love for people what you love for yourself and you will be a believer. Be a good neighbor to those who neighbor you and you will be a Muslim. Beware of excessive laughter, for it deadens the heart. Loud laughter is from Satan, while smiling is from Allah."],[1052,"O uncle, your children are contentious people, and others are more distant."],[1053,"No nation ever perished until it associated partners with Allah, and no nation associated partners with Allah until the first of its association was denying divine decree."],[1054,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man from praying a prayer in which he does not complete its bowing and prostration."],[1055,"Regarding wiping over the leather socks: for the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."],[1056,"Indeed Allah has prescribed excellence in all things. So when you kill, kill well; and when you slaughter, slaughter well. Let each of you sharpen his blade and spare suffering to the animal he slaughters."],[1057,"The Ansar are my inner circle and my trusted confidants. Accept from their good-doers and overlook their wrongdoers."],[1058,"The one who pretends to have been given what he has not been given is like the one who wears two garments of falsehood."],[1059,"Good conduct, good demeanor, moderation, and deliberation are one part of twenty-four parts of prophethood."],[1060,"The best of your religion is its easiest."],[1061,"The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother."],[1062,"Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy."],[1063,"I was aided by the east wind, and 'Ad was destroyed by the west wind."],[1064,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: O God, let me enjoy my hearing and my sight until You make them my heir; and grant me well-being in my religion; and gather me upon what You have given me life; and help me against the one who wronged me, until You show me my vengeance from him! O God, I have submitted my religion, turned my face to You, entrusted my affair to You, and leaned my back upon You. There is no refuge nor escape from You except to You. I believe in Your Messenger whom You sent, and in Your Book which You sent down."],[1065,"Whoever fulfills his desire in this world, a barrier is placed between him and his lust in the Hereafter. Whoever stretches his eyes toward the adornment of the luxurious will be despised in the kingdom of heaven. Whoever patiently endures severe subsistence with beautiful patience, God will settle him in al-Firdaws wherever He wills."],[1066,"It is an act of disbelief for a man to claim a lineage that is not known, or to deny it, even if it is subtle."],[1067,"Bilal was commanded to make the adhan even and the iqamah odd."],[1068,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by 'Abd Allah b. Rawahah al-Ansari while he was reminding his companions, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Indeed, you are the assembly whom God commanded me to keep myself patient with! Then he recited this verse: 'And keep yourself patient with those who call upon their Lord in the morning and the evening' until His saying, exalted is He: 'and his affair had been in excess.' Indeed, no number of you sits except that the same number of angels sits with them; if they glorify God, they glorify Him; if they praise God, they praise Him; if they magnify God, they magnify Him. Then they ascend to the Lord, and He knows better than them, so they say: Our Lord, Your servants glorified You so we glorified You, magnified You so we magnified You, and praised You so we praised You! Our Lord says: O My angels, I make you witness that I have forgiven them! They say: Among them is so-and-so and so-and-so, the sinner! He says: They are the people; no one who sits with them will be made wretched."],[1069,"Hearts are four: a smooth heart in which there is like a shining lamp, and that is the heart of the believer, and its lamp contains its light. A wrapped heart tied over its covering, and that is the heart of the disbeliever. An upside-down heart, and that is the heart of the hypocrite; he knew then he denied. A heart with a covering, and that is a heart in which there is faith and hypocrisy; the example of faith in it is like a herb that good water nourishes, and the example of hypocrisy is like a wound that pus and blood nourish; whichever of the two fluids overcomes its companion, it overcomes him."],[1070,"My maternal uncle, Jadd b. Qays, carried me among the seventy riders who came to the Messenger of God ﷺ on the night of al-'Aqabah from among the Ansar. The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us and with him was his uncle al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib. He said: 'O uncle, take the pledge from your maternal uncles!' The seventy said to him: 'O Muhammad, ask for your Lord and for yourself whatever you wish!' He said: 'As for what I ask of you for my Lord, that you worship Him and do not associate anything with Him. As for what I ask of you for myself, that you protect me from what you protect yourselves from.' They said: 'What will we have if we do that?' He said: 'Paradise.'"],[1071,"The banner of the Prophet ﷺ was black."],[1072,"A woman has two veils. It was said: \"And what are they?\" He said: \"The husband and the grave.\" It was said: \"Which of them is more concealing?\" He said: \"The grave.\""],[1073,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man with disheveled hair and said, \"Why would any of you disfigure himself?\" and gestured with his hand, meaning to take some of it."],[1074,"Part of the excellence of a person's Islam is leaving that which does not concern him."],[1075,"Maghrib prayer is the witr of the day, so perform witr for the night prayer."],[1076,"Fatimah said when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was taken: \"O father, to his Lord he is nearest! O father, the Garden of Firdaws is his abode! O father, to Jibril we announce his death!\""],[1077,"An oath is only either a sin or regret."],[1078,"Abu Dharr al-Ghifari stood before Banu Ghifar and said: \"O Banu Ghifar, the truthful, the believed ﷺ told me that people will be gathered in three groups: a group well-fed and clothed, a group walking and running, and a group dragged by the angels with the Fire herding them from behind.\" He said: \"We know these and these, but what about those who walk and run?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A calamity will befall the riding animals until no mount remains, such that one of you would give his walled garden for an old camel with a saddle and not find it.\""],[1079,"Umar b. al-Khattab began to narrate to us about the people of Badr and said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to show us the places where the people of Badr would fall the day before Badr, saying, 'This is the place where so-and-so will fall tomorrow, and this is the place where so-and-so will fall tomorrow, if Allah wills.'\" Umar said: \"By the One who sent him with the truth, they did not miss the boundaries that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had set!\" They were placed in a well, some on top of others. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went until he reached them and said, \"O so-and-so son of so-and-so, and O so-and-so son of so-and-so, have you found what Allah and His Messenger promised you to be true? Indeed I have found what Allah promised me to be true.\" Umar said: \"O Messenger of Allah, how do you speak to bodies that have no souls?\" He said: \"You are not more able to hear what I say than they are, except that they cannot reply anything.\""],[1080,"I entered upon Ibn Mas'ud on the day of Ashura, and before him was a bowl of tharid and meat-stripped bones. I said: \"O Abu Abd al-Rahman, is this not the day of Ashura?\" He said: \"Yes, we used to fast with the Prophet ﷺ before the month of Ramadan was made obligatory. When the month of Ramadan was made obligatory, it abrogated it.\" Then he said: \"Sit!\" So I sat and ate."],[1081,"The Hour will not come until people vie with one another in building mosques."],[1082,"For what the sky has watered, one-tenth is due; and for what is watered by bucket, half of one-tenth is due."],[1083,"O Allah, forgive the pilgrim and the one for whom the pilgrim seeks forgiveness."],[1084,"A man said to the Prophet ﷺ: \"I find within myself such a thing that to be a burnt cinder would be dearer to me than to speak of it!\" He said: \"That is pure faith.\""],[1085,"Modesty is part of faith, and faith leads to Paradise. Obscenity is part of harshness, and harshness leads to the Fire."],[1086,"Verily Allah, Mighty and Majestic, records for a sick person the utmost of what he used to do in health as long as he is confined by his illness, and for a traveler the best of what he used to do while resident."],[1087,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ freed Safiyyah and made her emancipation her dower."],[1088,"A man should not touch a man, and a woman should not touch a woman."],[1089,"My love is due to those who befriend one another for My sake, and My love is due to those who help one another for My sake. There is no believing man or believing woman for whom Allah grants three children from his own loins who do not reach the age of accountability, except that Allah will admit him to Paradise by the bounty of His mercy toward them."],[1090,"The Kharijites are the dogs of the Fire."],[1091,"Mu'adh b. Jabal went out seeking the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but he did not find him. He searched for him in his houses but did not find him. He followed him from lane to lane until he was directed to him on Mount Thawab. He went out and climbed Mount Thawab, looked right and left, and caught sight of him in the cave that people had taken as a path to the Mosque of Victory. Mu'adh said: \"There he was, prostrating. I descended from the top of the mountain while he was prostrating, and he did not raise his head until I thought ill of him, thinking that he had been taken in death. When he raised his head, I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I thought ill of you, thinking that you had passed away.' He said: 'Jibril ﷺ came to me in this spot and said: \"Verily Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sends you greetings of peace and says to you: What would you love Me to do with your nation?\" I said: \"Allah knows best.\" He departed, then came back to me and said: \"He says: I will not cause you grief regarding your nation.\" So I prostrated. The best means by which one draws near to Allah is prostration.'\""],[1092,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ annulled the marriage of a virgin and a previously married woman whom their fathers had married off while they were unwilling."],[1093,"When a Muslim performs ablution and washes his hands, the sins his hands committed are expiated. When he washes his face, the sins his eyes looked upon are expiated. When he wipes his head, the sins his ears heard are expiated. When he washes his feet, the sins his feet walked toward are expiated. Then he stands for prayer, and that is an additional merit."],[1094,"I served the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for ten years, and I never knew of anything that I did that suited him or anything that I did that displeased him, out of contentment with what Allah, Exalted, had decreed. Some of his wives would say: \"If only you had done such and such; why did you do such and such?\" He would say: \"Leave him, for nothing occurs except what Allah wills.\" I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ take revenge for himself over anything, unless a sacred ordinance of Allah was violated. When a sacred ordinance of Allah was violated, he was the most intense of people in anger for Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Never were two matters presented to him but that he chose the easier of them, as long as it did not entail Allah's displeasure. If it entailed Allah's displeasure, he was the farthest of people from it."],[1095,"Intercession is only made for those of my nation who commit major sins."],[1096,"He stood between the two jamarat in the Hajj he performed, and that was on the Day of Sacrifice, and said: 'This is the day of the greater Hajj.'"],[1097,"She used to perform ghusl with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from a single vessel."],[1098,"When one of you hears a ringing in his ear, let him remember me and invoke blessings upon me."],[1099,"Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, even like a nest of a sandgrouse, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise."],[1100,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the people of Madinah: 'O Allah, bless them in their sa' and their mudd.'"],[1101,"Look at those below you and do not look at those above you, for it is more likely that you will not belittle the blessing of Allah, the Mighty and Sublime."],[1102,"A believer continues to be swift and righteous as long as he does not shed forbidden blood; when he sheds forbidden blood, he is exhausted."],[1103,"He forbade sleeping before 'Isha and engaging in talk after it."],[1104,"Between my house and my pulpit is a garden of the gardens of Paradise, and my pulpit is upon one of the canals of Paradise."],[1105,"Indeed Allah has ordained obligations, so do not neglect them; and He has set limits, so do not overstep them; and He has remained silent about many things, not out of forgetfulness, so do not seek them out—as a mercy from Allah, so accept them."],[1106,"Whoever restrains anger while able to act upon it, Allah will offer him any of the wide-eyed maidens of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever marries off a slave, Allah will place upon his head a crown of kingship on the Day of Resurrection."],[1107,"Whoever touches his private part should perform wudu."],[1108,"The most excellent form of worship is understanding of religion, and the most excellent part of religion is piety."],[1109,"The Prophet ﷺ recited [the verse with] “a spring of murky water” (ʿaynin ḥamiʾah)."],[1110,"Three types of people will not be terrified by the greatest terror, nor will they be subjected to the reckoning. They will be upon a hill of musk until the reckoning of all creatures is completed: a man who recited the Qurʾan seeking the countenance of Allah and led a people in prayer while they were pleased with him; a caller who calls to the five prayers seeking the countenance of Allah; and a slave who was excellent in what was between him and his Lord and in what was between him and his masters."],[1111,"A man said, “O Messenger of Allah, may one of us pray in a single garment?” He replied, “Does every one of you find two garments?”"],[1112,"Whoever sees a fault of his brother and conceals it will enter Paradise."],[1113,"Instruct your dying ones to say: “There is no deity but Allah,” and say: “Steadfastness, steadfastness, and there is no power except with Allah.”"],[1114,"Whoever recites the Qurʾan and acts upon it during the hours of the night and day, permitting its permissible and forbidding its forbidden, Allah will forbid his flesh and blood to the Fire and will make him a companion of the noble, righteous scribes, so that on the Day of Resurrection the Qurʾan will be an argument for him."],[1115,"Ṭalḥah b. ʿUbayd Allāh spoke harshly to ʿĀmir b. Fuhayrah, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: “Gently, O Ṭalḥah, for he was present at Badr just as you were present, and the best of you is the one who is best to his freedmen.”"],[1116,"The prophets will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection upon mounts so that they may arrive from their graves to the gathering place. Ṣāliḥ ﷺ will be sent upon his she-camel, and my two sons, al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn, will be sent upon my she-camel al-ʿAḍbāʾ, and I will be sent upon al-Burāq, whose stride reaches as far as its eye can see. Bilāl will be sent upon a she-camel from the she-camels of Paradise, and he will call the adhān purely and pronounce the shahādah truly, truly, until when he says, “I bear witness that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah,” the believers from the first and the last will bear witness for him, and it will be accepted from those from whom it is accepted and rejected for those for whom it is rejected."],[1117,"The slave has three rights over his master: he should not be rushed away from his prayer, he should not be kept from his food, and he should be fully satisfied with every kind of satiation."],[1118,"He used to pray four rakʿahs before the ʿaṣr prayer."],[1119,"There will be at the end of my ummah women who are clothed yet naked, on their heads something like the humps of camels. Curse them, for they are cursed."],[1120,"Whoever eats garlic or onion should keep away from us, or keep away from our mosque, or stay in his house."],[1121,"When God wills evil for a servant, He makes him eager for bricks and clay until he builds."],[1122,"I recited to the Prophet ﷺ: “God is the One who created you from weakness.” He said: “From weakness.” “Then He made after weakness strength.” He said: “Then He made after weakness strength.”"],[1123,"The Prophet ﷺ recited: “And you will drink as the thirsty camels drink.”"],[1124,"The Messenger of God ﷺ urinated at a people’s garbage dump, then performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[1125,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would not refrain from anything from my face while he was fasting."],[1126,"Among the signs of the Hour’s approach is that the new moon will be seen in advance and it will be said, “It is for two nights,” that mosques will be used as thoroughfares, and that sudden death will appear."],[1127,"A person is with the one he loves."],[1128,"Whoever recites “Say: He is God, the One” fifty times every day will be called on the Day of Resurrection from his grave: “Arise, O praiser of God, and enter Paradise.”"],[1129,"God – blessed and exalted is He – has an angel who calls out at every prayer: “O children of Adam, rise to your fires that you have kindled against yourselves and extinguish them.”"],[1130,"I have pardoned the alms on horses and slaves, and there is no zakat on what is less than two hundred dirhams."],[1131,"Regarding God’s saying – mighty and glorious is He – “By the witness and the witnessed,” he said: “The witness is my grandfather, the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the witnessed is the Day of Resurrection.” Then he recited this verse: “Indeed, We have sent you as a witness and a bearer of good tidings and a warner,” and he recited: “That is a day for which mankind will be gathered, and that is a day witnessed.”"],[1132,"No servant prays the dawn prayer, then sits remembering God until the sun rises, but that will be for him a barrier from the Fire."],[1133,"The Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary was raised up to me, and there were four rivers: two visible rivers and two hidden rivers. As for the two visible ones, they are the Nile and the Euphrates; as for the two hidden ones, they are two rivers in Paradise. And I was brought three cups: a cup containing milk, a cup containing honey, and a cup containing wine. I took the one containing milk and drank, and it was said: You have attained the primordial nature—you and your community."],[1134,"I said: O Messenger of God, whom should I treat most kindly? He said: \"Your mother.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Your mother.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Then your father.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Then the nearest, then the next nearest.\""],[1135,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was leading his companions in the sunset prayer. I heard him saying: \"It has no repeller\"—and his voice was coming out of the mosque—\"Indeed, the punishment of your Lord is surely occurring; it has no repeller.\" It was as if my heart was split open."],[1136,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: \"O 'Imran.\" I said: At your service. He said: \"Say: O God, I seek guidance from You for the most sound of my affairs, and I seek Your protection from the evil of my self.\""],[1137,"Whoever frees a Muslim slave, God will free, for every limb of that slave, a limb of his from the Fire."],[1138,"The soul of a believer is suspended as long as he has a debt."],[1139,"The Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned misappropriation of war spoils and said: \"Let one of you beware of coming on the Day of Resurrection with a camel on his neck that bellows.\""],[1140,"A man had recently married, and the Messenger of God ﷺ dispatched an expedition and sent that man among them. When the people came back, he hurried to his family, and found his wife standing at her door. Jealousy entered him, so he readied a spear to thrust at her. She said: Do not rush; look at what is in the house. He entered the house and found a snake coiled on her bed. He thrust at the snake, and it died, and the man died too. This reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"Indeed, these houses have dwellers from the jinn,\" and he forbade killing house snakes."],[1141,"There is no deed more beloved to God—Mighty and Majestic—than a deed done in the ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah, except a man who goes out with his wealth and his life, then does not return."],[1142,"Cover your vessels, tie your waterskins, shut your doors, and extinguish your lamps; for Satan does not open a shut door, nor uncover a cover, nor untie a waterskin. And indeed the little vermin may set ablaze the house upon its occupants."],[1143,"The Prophet ﷺ sold a mudabbar (slave promised freedom upon his owner's death) belonging to Nuʿaym b. ʿAbdallāh."],[1144,"When the Banū al-ʿĀṣ reach thirty men, they will take the religion of God as a means of deceit, the wealth of God as private property, and the servants of God as slaves."],[1145,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by some people shooting arrows while swearing, saying: \"You missed, by God!\" and \"You hit, by God!\" When they saw the Messenger of God ﷺ, they stopped. He said: \"Shoot, for the oaths of archers are futile; there is no sin in them and no expiation.\""],[1146,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered Makkah on the Day of the Conquest, and around the Kaʿbah there were three hundred and sixty idols, Iblīs having fastened their feet with lead. He came with a stick and began striking each idol with it, and it would fall on its face, while he said: \"The truth has come, and falsehood has vanished. Indeed, falsehood is bound to vanish\" [Qur'an 17:81], until he had passed by all of them."],[1147,"A Muslim prays while his sins are placed upon his head. Every time he prostrates, they fall away from him, so by the time he finishes his prayer, his sins have fallen away."],[1148,"For the traveler, (the period for wiping over leather socks) is three days and their nights, and for the resident, one day and one night."],[1149,"The Friday bath is obligatory upon every one who has reached puberty."],[1150,"You are in a time when whoever abandons a tenth of what he has been commanded will perish; and a time will come when whoever acts upon a tenth of what he has been commanded will be saved."],[1151,"The Prophet ﷺ proposed to Umm Mubashshir bt. al-Barāʾ b. Maʿrūr, and she said: \"I made a condition with my husband that I would not marry after him.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"This is not proper.\""],[1152,"What is wrong with one of you, when a worry presses upon him, that he should take up his bow and thereby dispel his worry?"],[1153,"Whoever builds a mosque for God, God will build for him a house in Paradise."],[1154,"The night prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ was obligatory when God, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: \"O you wrapped in garments, arise to pray the night, except a little\" [Qur'an 73:1–2]. It was the first obligation, and they used to pray until their feet became cracked. God, Mighty and Majestic, withheld the end of the surah from them for a year, then He revealed: \"He knows that you will not be able to keep count of it, so He has turned to you in mercy; recite, then, what is easy of the Qur'an\" [Qur'an 73:20]. Thus the night prayer became voluntary."],[1155,"The prayer is cut off by the black dog, the woman, and the donkey. I said: What is it with the black dog as opposed to the white one? He said: I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ just as you asked me, and he said: 'The black dog is a devil.'"],[1156,"None may touch the Qur'an except one who is ritually pure."],[1157,"Hudhayfa b. al-Yaman and 'Uqba b. 'Amr, Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, met. One of them said to his companion: 'Narrate to me what you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ.' One of them narrated and the other confirmed him. One of them said: 'A servant will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and made to stand before God – Mighty and Majestic – and He will say: \"What do you have to your credit?\" He will say: \"I used to engage in transactions with people. When I dealt with someone in difficulty, I let him off; and when I dealt with someone well-off, I gave him respite.\" God will say: \"I am more entitled than My servant to be lenient,\" and He will forgive him.' The other said: 'You have spoken the truth. Thus I heard it from the Messenger of God.'"],[1158,"The people of Paradise will enter Paradise hairless, beardless, with kohl-lined eyes."],[1159,"The prayer of one sitting is half of the prayer of one standing."],[1160,"In every prayer, recitation is done. What the Messenger of God ﷺ made us hear, we made you hear; and what he concealed from us, we concealed from you."],[1161,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped his head once."],[1162,"When he began the prayer, he raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders; and when he bowed, and after he raised his head from bowing; and he did not raise them between the two prostrations."],[1163,"Be lenient, and leniency will be shown to you."],[1164,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded Bilal to put his fingers in his ears when giving the call to prayer, and he said: 'It makes your voice higher.'"],[1165,"Bilal used to give the call to prayer in pairs, and he pronounced the testimony of faith emphatically, facing the qibla. He would say: 'I bear witness that there is no god but God' – twice; 'I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God' – twice. Then he would repeat them, saying: 'I bear witness that there is no god but God' – twice; 'I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God' – twice, facing the qibla. Then he would turn to his right and say: 'Come to prayer' – twice. Then he would turn to his left and say: 'Come to success' – twice. Then he would face the qibla and say: 'God is most great, God is most great. There is no god but God.' His iqama was single: 'The prayer has been established' – once. He used to give the call to prayer on Friday for the Friday prayer during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ when the shadow became like a sandal strap."],[1166,"When he went out for the two 'ids, he took one route and returned by another."],[1167,"He used to begin on the two 'ids with the prayer before the sermon, then he would say takbir in the first [rak'ah] seven times before the recitation, and in the second [rak'ah] five times before the recitation. He used to go out on the two 'ids walking and return walking, and he used to say takbir between the parts of the sermon, and he would say takbir frequently on the two 'ids."],[1168,"When he delivered the sermon on the two 'ids, he would deliver it on a bow, and when he delivered the sermon on Friday, he would deliver it on a staff."],[1169,"The Prophet ﷺ said one day to a boy from the Ansar: 'Hand me my sandals.' The boy said: 'O Prophet of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, leave me so that I may put them on your feet myself.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Allah, this servant of Yours seeks Your pleasure, so be pleased with him.'"],[1170,"Whoever loves the Ansar, it is out of love for me; and whoever hates the Ansar, it is out of hatred for me. [Mu'awiyah] said: 'Choose whichever land you wish, for you will not return to Hadramawt.' I said: 'My kinsfolk are in Syria and my household is in Kufa.' He said: 'One man from your household is better than ten from your kinsfolk.' I said: 'I did not return to Hadramawt out of delight in it. It is not appropriate for an emigrant to return to the place from which he emigrated except for a reason.' He said: 'What is your reason?' I said: 'The saying of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the fitnas: wherever you differ, we shall withdraw from you; and wherever you unite, we shall come to you. This is the reason.' He said: 'I have appointed you governor of Kufa, so go to it.' I said: 'After the Prophet ﷺ I have no need of anyone. Do you not see that Abu Bakr wanted me and I refused, 'Umar wanted me and I refused, and 'Uthman wanted me and I refused, yet I did not abandon giving allegiance to them? The letter of Abu Bakr came to me when the people of our region apostatized, and I stood among them until Allah returned them to Islam without any appointment.' Then he called 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Hakam and said to him: 'I have appointed you governor of Kufa. Go with Wa'il b. Hujr, honor him, and fulfill his needs.' He said: 'O Commander of the Believers, you thought ill of me. You command me to honor a man whom I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ honor, as well as Abu Bakr, 'Umar, 'Uthman, and you?' Mu'awiyah was pleased with that from him. I arrived with him in Kufa, and he did not remain long before he died. - Muhammad b. Hujr said: al-wirat are the 'ammar (builders), al-aqwal are the kings, al-'ayahilah are the great ones. In the al-Maktab al-Islami edition it was corrupted as (al-Muhajirin Abi Umayyah), but it is correct in the manuscripts and the 'Ilmiyyah edition."],[1171,"O Abu Musa, shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah (There is no might and no power except with Allah).'"],[1172,"Whoever meets his Muslim brother with what he loves in order to please him thereby, Allah will please him on the Day of Resurrection."],[1173,"A slave who obeys Allah and obeys his masters - Allah will admit him to Paradise before his masters. The master will say: 'My Lord, this was my slave in the world.' He will say: 'I rewarded him for his deeds, and I rewarded you for your deeds.'"],[1174,"The Prophet ﷺ walked at a fast pace in his Hajj from the Stone to the Stone."],[1175,"The world will not come to an end until a man from my household rules, whose name matches my name, and he fills the earth with justice and fairness as it was filled with oppression and injustice."],[1176,"I used to rub the semen from the garment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with thumamah (a type of grass)."],[1177,"Whoever has a favor done to him and says to the doer: 'May Allah reward you with good,' has indeed excelled in praise."],[1178,"When a man says to his brother: 'May Allah reward you with good,' he has indeed excelled in praise."],[1179,"Ishaq b. Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Razzaq, by reading from al-Thawri, from Musa b. 'Ubayda, from Muhammad b. Thabit, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet ﷺ with its like."],[1180,"Seek help in fulfilling your needs through concealment, for every possessor of a blessing is envied."],[1181,"She abandons the prayer during the days of her menstrual periods, then she performs a full bath once, then she performs ablution for the like of the days of her menstrual periods; and if she sees a yellowish discharge, she sprinkles water, performs ablution, and prays."],[1182,"That the Prophet ﷺ prayed for rain and turned his cloak inside out, making its upper part its lower part."],[1183,"When he had prayed the morning prayer, he would sit remembering Allah until the sun rose."],[1184,"A man is with the one he loves."],[1185,"Aslam, Ghifar, Muzayna, and Juhayna are better in the sight of Allah than Banu Asad, Ghatafan, and Banu 'Amir b. Sa'sa'a."],[1186,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and made a supplication the like of which the people had never heard, and he sought refuge with a seeking of refuge the like of which the people had never heard. Some of the people said to him: 'How can we, O Messenger of Allah, supplicate with the like of what you supplicated, and seek refuge as you sought refuge?' He said: 'Say: O Allah, we ask You by what Muhammad Your servant and Messenger asked You, and we seek refuge from what Muhammad Your servant and Messenger sought refuge from.'"],[1187,"Our best horseman is Abu Qatada, and our best footman is Salama b. al-Akwa'."],[1188,"That he guarded the Prophet ﷺ on the night of Badr. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Allah, protect Abu Qatada as he protected Your Prophet this night.'"],[1189,"The polytheists raided the milch-camels of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I mounted and overtook them and killed Mas'ada. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw me, he said: 'May his face prosper!' Then he said: 'O Allah, forgive him' three times, and he gave me the spoils of Mas'ada as a reward."],[1190,"Women are not obliged to go on military expeditions, nor to attend the Friday prayer, nor to follow funeral processions."],[1191,"Whoever takes a handspan from the path of the Muslims, Allah will collar him on the Day of Resurrection with seven earths."],[1192,"The Qur’an is the speech of Allah, exalted is He, uncreated."]]);
